{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"language":"python","display_name":"Python 3","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.13.16","mimetype":"text/x-python","codemirror_mode":{"name":"ipython","version":3},"pygments_lexer":"ipython3","nbconvert_exporter":"python","file_extension":".py"},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"nvidiaTeslaT4","dataSources":[{"sourceType":"competition","sourceId":46105}],"dockerImageVersionId":28755,"isInternetEnabled":false,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":false}},"nbformat_minor":4,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# ASL Signs → Conditional Diffusion (word → MediaPipe landmark sequence → avatar)\n\nGiven a word from the 250-sign vocabulary of the *Google – Isolated Sign Language Recognition* competition, the model\ngenerates a 64-frame sequence of upper-body MediaPipe landmarks (hands, arms and **a detailed face**) that signs that word,\nwith a controllable **duration**. The second half of the notebook turns this motion into something usable for an avatar.\n\n**Pipeline**\n\n| step | what happens |\n|---|---|\n| 1. Preprocessing | parquet → 127 landmarks per frame (2 hands, shoulders/elbows/wrists, **79 face points: lips, brows, eyes, nose, contour**) → body-invariant normalisation → gap filling → resampled to `T = 64` frames → one cached `.npy` file holding **x, y and z** |\n| 2. Splitting | only corrupt clips are removed (everything else is kept), then **signer-independent** splits: test **and** validation signers never appear in train |\n| 3. Dataset | `(word id, landmarks (T, C), real duration, which parts were detected)`, standardised with train-only statistics; a **duration prior** per word |\n| 4. Model | DiT-style Transformer denoiser (adaLN-Zero) conditioned on the **word and the duration** + Gaussian diffusion, classifier-free guidance, DDIM sampler |\n| 5. Training | EMA weights, warm-up + cosine learning rate, early stopping; the loss ignores hands / face that were not detected |\n| 6. Test performance | denoising loss per test signer, recognition accuracy, Fréchet distance and nearest-real joint error (per body part) on unseen signers |\n| 7. Smoothing | **One Euro filter** on generated sequences (no retraining) + a jitter metric |\n| 8. Duration | the duration prior, duration control, playback at the real speed |\n| 9. Face | lips / brows / eyes detail, face blend-shape curves for an avatar |\n| 10. 3D | how noisy is MediaPipe `z`? `use_z=True`, or a separate **depth lifter** |\n| 11. Avatar | **retargeting**: landmarks → bone rotations (analytic IK for arms, IK for fingers), BVH + JSON export |\n| 12. Human evaluation | a blind rating kit for deaf / native signers + the analysis of their answers |\n| 13. Export | best EMA model as a single self-contained bundle + a zip with metrics and figures |\n\n**How to use:** run the cells from top to bottom. Each section first *defines* its code, then a cell marked **▶** runs it and\nshows the result. Preprocessing is cached in `/kaggle/working/cache`, so it only runs once. Sections 7-12 only need the trained\nmodel (they can also be run from a reloaded `ckpt_best.pt`).","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Setup: imports and configuration\nAll hyper-parameters live in `Config`. Edit the values here; nothing else in the notebook overrides them.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Imports & configuration\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport copy\nimport itertools\nimport json\nimport math\nimport os\nimport time\nimport zipfile\nfrom dataclasses import asdict, dataclass\nfrom multiprocessing import Pool\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\n\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nimport torch\nimport torch.nn as nn\nimport torch.nn.functional as F\nfrom IPython.display import FileLink, display\nfrom torch.utils.data import DataLoader, Dataset\nfrom tqdm.auto import tqdm\n\n\n# Face detail used everywhere in the notebook:\n#   \"expressive\" = lips, eyebrows, eyes, nose and face contour (79 points)   |   \"basic\" = 9 reference points\n# It changes the number of landmarks (and therefore the cache and the model size): change it BEFORE running anything.\nFACE_PRESET = \"expressive\"\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Config:\n    # ---- paths ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    data_dir: str = \"/kaggle/input/competitions/asl-signs\"   # contains train.csv and train_landmark_files/\n    work_dir: str = \"/kaggle/working\"                        # cache, checkpoints, figures, final zip\n\n    # ---- preprocessing --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    num_frames: int = 64             # every clip is resampled to T frames\n    use_z: bool = False              # the cache always holds x, y, z; True = the model also generates z (MediaPipe z is noisy, see section 10)\n    face_preset: str = FACE_PRESET   # recorded in the model bundle (set FACE_PRESET above, not here)\n    cache_dir: str = \"\"              # \"\" = <work_dir>/cache. Share one cache between runs (e.g. use_z False / True) by setting it\n    fps: float = 30.0                # ASSUMED frame rate of the videos: only used to turn frame counts into seconds\n    min_hand_frac: float = 0.0       # drop clips whose hands are detected in fewer than this share of frames (0 = keep every clip)\n    min_frames: int = 3              # drop clips with fewer raw frames than this\n    clean_hand_frac: float = 0.5     # clips with hands detected in >= this share of frames form the 'clean' subset (reporting only)\n    num_proc: int = 4                # CPU processes used to read the parquet files\n    overwrite_cache: bool = False    # True = redo the preprocessing even if the cache exists\n\n    # ---- splitting (whole signers are held out; done AFTER the quality filter) --------------------\n    test_frac: float = 0.2           # ~20 % of the signers (and of the clips) go to test\n    val_frac: float = 0.1            # ~10 % of the signers go to validation\n    min_test_per_sign: int = 5       # every sign should have at least this many test clips ...\n    min_val_per_sign: int = 2        # ... and this many validation clips\n    split_trials: int = 20000        # max. number of signer subsets scored per split\n    seed: int = 42\n\n    # ---- data loading ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    batch_size: int = 128\n    num_workers: int = 2\n    augment: bool = True             # random rotation / zoom / shift of the train clips\n    face_loss_weight: float = 0.3    # loss weight of one face coordinate (79 face points would otherwise dominate the 42 hand points)\n\n    # ---- model ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    d_model: int = 384\n    depth: int = 8\n    n_heads: int = 4\n    mlp_ratio: float = 4.0\n    dropout: float = 0.0\n\n    # ---- diffusion ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    diffusion_steps: int = 1000\n    prediction_type: str = \"v\"       # \"eps\" | \"x0\" | \"v\"\n    p_uncond: float = 0.1            # probability of dropping the word during training (classifier-free guidance)\n    use_duration: bool = True        # condition the model on the clip duration (kept as a number, not resampled away)\n    p_dur_drop: float = 0.1          # probability of hiding ONLY the duration -> the model also works when no duration is given\n    dur_prior_shrink: float = 5.0    # per-word duration statistics are pulled towards the global ones (pseudo-count)\n\n    # ---- training -------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    epochs: int = 100                # upper bound; early stopping usually ends the run earlier\n    lr: float = 1e-4\n    weight_decay: float = 1e-2\n    warmup_steps: int = 500\n    grad_clip: float = 1.0\n    ema_decay: float = 0.999\n    amp: bool = True                 # fp16 autocast on CUDA\n    early_stopping: bool = True\n    patience: int = 8                # epochs without improvement before stopping\n    min_delta: float = 1e-4          # smallest decrease of the validation loss that counts as an improvement\n\n    # ---- evaluation -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    gen_per_word: int = 10           # generated clips per test word\n    gen_steps: int = 50              # DDIM steps\n    guidance: float = 2.0            # classifier-free guidance scale\n    eval_max_words: Optional[int] = None   # evaluate only a random subset of words (None = all test words)\n    clf_epochs: int = 50             # recognition classifier (trained on REAL train clips only)\n    clf_patience: int = 4\n    clf_hidden: int = 256\n    clf_embed_dim: int = 128         # embedding size used for the Fréchet distance\n\n    # ---- temporal smoothing of generated sequences (One Euro filter, section 7) ----------------------\n    smooth: bool = True              # smooth the generated clips before they are shown / exported\n    smooth_min_cutoff: float = 2.0   # Hz. Lower = smoother when the hands are almost still\n    smooth_beta: float = 4.0         # higher = less lag during fast movements\n    smooth_d_cutoff: float = 1.0     # Hz, cut-off used to estimate the speed","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-17T22:46:37.519804Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-17T22:46:37.520174Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-17T22:46:43.44309Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-17T22:46:37.520148Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-17T22:46:43.442475Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":1},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### ▶ Setup\nCreates the configuration, picks the device and fixes the random seeds.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"cfg = Config(num_proc=min(4, os.cpu_count() or 1))\nos.makedirs(cfg.work_dir, exist_ok=True)\ndevice = \"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\"\ntorch.manual_seed(cfg.seed)\nnp.random.seed(cfg.seed)\n\nprint(\"device:\", device)\ndisplay(pd.Series(asdict(cfg), name=\"value\").to_frame())","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-17T22:46:43.444192Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-17T22:46:43.444603Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-17T22:46:43.742858Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-17T22:46:43.444581Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-17T22:46:43.741989Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"device: cuda\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"                                                  value\ndata_dir           /kaggle/input/competitions/asl-signs\nwork_dir                                /kaggle/working\nnum_frames                                           64\nuse_z                                             False\nface_preset                                  expressive\ncache_dir                                              \nfps                                                30.0\nmin_hand_frac                                       0.0\nmin_frames                                            3\nclean_hand_frac                                     0.5\nnum_proc                                              4\noverwrite_cache                                   False\ntest_frac                                           0.2\nval_frac                                            0.1\nmin_test_per_sign                                     5\nmin_val_per_sign                                      2\nsplit_trials                                      20000\nseed                                                 42\nbatch_size                                          128\nnum_workers                                           2\naugment                                            True\nface_loss_weight                                    0.3\nd_model                                             384\ndepth                                                 8\nn_heads                                               4\nmlp_ratio                                           4.0\ndropout                                             0.0\ndiffusion_steps                                    1000\nprediction_type                                       v\np_uncond                                            0.1\nuse_duration                                       True\np_dur_drop                                          0.1\ndur_prior_shrink                                    5.0\nepochs                                              100\nlr                                               0.0001\nweight_decay                                       0.01\nwarmup_steps                                        500\ngrad_clip                                           1.0\nema_decay                                         0.999\namp                                                True\nearly_stopping                                     True\npatience                                              8\nmin_delta                                        0.0001\ngen_per_word                                         10\ngen_steps                                            50\nguidance                                            2.0\neval_max_words                                     None\nclf_epochs                                           50\nclf_patience                                          4\nclf_hidden                                          256\nclf_embed_dim                                       128\nsmooth                                             True\nsmooth_min_cutoff                                   2.0\nsmooth_beta                                         4.0\nsmooth_d_cutoff                                     1.0","text/html":"<div>\n<style scoped>\n    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n        vertical-align: middle;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n        vertical-align: top;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe thead th {\n        text-align: right;\n    }\n</style>\n<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n  <thead>\n    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n      <th></th>\n      <th>value</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <th>data_dir</th>\n      <td>/kaggle/input/competitions/asl-signs</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>work_dir</th>\n      <td>/kaggle/working</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>num_frames</th>\n      <td>64</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>use_z</th>\n      <td>False</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>face_preset</th>\n      <td>expressive</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>cache_dir</th>\n      <td></td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>fps</th>\n      <td>30.0</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>min_hand_frac</th>\n      <td>0.0</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>min_frames</th>\n      <td>3</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>clean_hand_frac</th>\n      <td>0.5</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>num_proc</th>\n      <td>4</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>overwrite_cache</th>\n      <td>False</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>test_frac</th>\n      <td>0.2</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>val_frac</th>\n      <td>0.1</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>min_test_per_sign</th>\n      <td>5</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>min_val_per_sign</th>\n      <td>2</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>split_trials</th>\n      <td>20000</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>seed</th>\n      <td>42</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>batch_size</th>\n      <td>128</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>num_workers</th>\n      <td>2</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>augment</th>\n      <td>True</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>face_loss_weight</th>\n      <td>0.3</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>d_model</th>\n      <td>384</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>depth</th>\n      <td>8</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>n_heads</th>\n      <td>4</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>mlp_ratio</th>\n      <td>4.0</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>dropout</th>\n      <td>0.0</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>diffusion_steps</th>\n      <td>1000</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>prediction_type</th>\n      <td>v</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>p_uncond</th>\n      <td>0.1</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>use_duration</th>\n      <td>True</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>p_dur_drop</th>\n      <td>0.1</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>dur_prior_shrink</th>\n      <td>5.0</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>epochs</th>\n      <td>100</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>lr</th>\n      <td>0.0001</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>weight_decay</th>\n      <td>0.01</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>warmup_steps</th>\n      <td>500</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>grad_clip</th>\n      <td>1.0</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>ema_decay</th>\n      <td>0.999</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>amp</th>\n      <td>True</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>early_stopping</th>\n      <td>True</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>patience</th>\n      <td>8</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>min_delta</th>\n      <td>0.0001</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>gen_per_word</th>\n      <td>10</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>gen_steps</th>\n      <td>50</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>guidance</th>\n      <td>2.0</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>eval_max_words</th>\n      <td>None</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>clf_epochs</th>\n      <td>50</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>clf_patience</th>\n      <td>4</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>clf_hidden</th>\n      <td>256</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>clf_embed_dim</th>\n      <td>128</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>smooth</th>\n      <td>True</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>smooth_min_cutoff</th>\n      <td>2.0</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>smooth_beta</th>\n      <td>4.0</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>smooth_d_cutoff</th>\n      <td>1.0</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n</div>"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":2},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 1. Preprocessing & feature reduction\n\nEach parquet file stores 543 landmarks per frame (`face` 468 | `left_hand` 21 | `pose` 33 | `right_hand` 21), with NaN where\nMediaPipe lost a body part. We keep **127 nodes** (with `FACE_PRESET = \"expressive\"`):\n\n| nodes | content |\n|---|---|\n| 0–20  | left hand (21 landmarks) |\n| 21–41 | right hand (21 landmarks) |\n| 42–47 | pose: left/right shoulder, left/right elbow, left/right wrist |\n| 48–126 | face: outer lips (20), inner lips (20), eyebrows (5 + 5), eye contours (8 + 8), nose (5), face contour (8) |\n\nThe coordinates are cached as **x, y, z** (3 per node). The model sees `C = 127 × 2 = 254` channels by default, or `C = 381` when\n`cfg.use_z = True`: the channels are only *selected* when the data is loaded, so switching `use_z` does **not** need a new preprocessing.\n\nPer clip:\n1. **Normalise**: origin = mean shoulder midpoint, unit = mean shoulder width (computed over the whole clip, so the motion is kept).\n2. **Fill gaps**: linear interpolation over time; a hand that is never detected is collapsed onto its pose wrist.\n3. **Resample** to `T = 64` frames (also normalises the signing speed). **The original length is not lost**: it is stored (`n_frames`)\n   and later used as a *condition* of the model (section 3).\n4. **Remember what was really detected**: for every frame we store whether the left hand, the right hand and the face were detected\n   (`*_parts.npy`). Gap-filled values are only a convenient input; the training loss ignores them (section 4), so no clip has to be\n   thrown away just because MediaPipe lost a hand.\n\nTo add or remove face points, edit the groups in `FACE_PRESETS` below (all node constants are derived from them).","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Landmark selection constants\nTYPE_OFFSET = {\"face\": 0, \"left_hand\": 468, \"pose\": 489, \"right_hand\": 522}   # start of each part in the 543 landmarks\nN_RAW = 543\nPOSE_KEEP = [11, 12, 13, 14, 15, 16]                 # L-shoulder, R-shoulder, L-elbow, R-elbow, L-wrist, R-wrist\n\n# Face landmarks (indices of the 468-point MediaPipe face mesh), grouped by facial part. The order inside a group is a\n# closed loop (lips, eyes) or a line (brows), which is how the groups are drawn.\nFACE_PRESETS = {\n    \"basic\": {\"face_basic\": [10, 33, 263, 1, 61, 291, 13, 14, 152]},    # forehead, eye corners, nose tip, mouth corners, inner lips, chin\n    \"expressive\": {\n        \"lips_outer\": [61, 185, 40, 39, 37, 0, 267, 269, 270, 409, 291, 375, 321, 405, 314, 17, 84, 181, 91, 146],\n        \"lips_inner\": [78, 191, 80, 81, 82, 13, 312, 311, 310, 415, 308, 324, 318, 402, 317, 14, 87, 178, 88, 95],\n        \"brow_r\": [70, 63, 105, 66, 107],\n        \"brow_l\": [300, 293, 334, 296, 336],\n        \"eye_r\": [33, 160, 159, 158, 133, 153, 145, 144],             # outer corner, upper lid, inner corner, lower lid\n        \"eye_l\": [263, 387, 386, 385, 362, 380, 374, 373],\n        \"nose\": [1, 98, 327, 168, 6],\n        \"oval\": [10, 338, 284, 454, 152, 234, 54, 103],               # forehead, temples, cheeks, chin\n    },\n}\nFACE_GROUPS = FACE_PRESETS[FACE_PRESET]\nFACE_KEEP = [i for g in FACE_GROUPS.values() for i in g]\nassert len(set(FACE_KEEP)) == len(FACE_KEEP), \"a face landmark appears twice\"\n\nLH = slice(0, 21)\nRH = slice(21, 42)\nPOSE = slice(42, 42 + len(POSE_KEEP))                # nodes 42..47\nFACE = slice(POSE.stop, POSE.stop + len(FACE_KEEP))  # face nodes\nNUM_NODES = FACE.stop\nP_LS, P_RS, P_LE, P_RE, P_LW, P_RW = range(POSE.start, POSE.stop)\n\n# node range of every face group, e.g. FACE_SLICE[\"lips_outer\"]\nFACE_SLICE, _start = {}, FACE.start\nfor _name, _lm in FACE_GROUPS.items():\n    FACE_SLICE[_name] = slice(_start, _start + len(_lm))\n    _start += len(_lm)\nFACE_NODE = {raw: FACE.start + k for k, raw in enumerate(FACE_KEEP)}   # raw face landmark index -> node index\n\n# Body parts used to report errors (nearest-real MPJPE)\nPART_GROUPS = {\"left_hand\": LH, \"right_hand\": RH, \"arms\": POSE}\nif FACE_PRESET == \"expressive\":\n    PART_GROUPS.update({\"lips\": slice(FACE_SLICE[\"lips_outer\"].start, FACE_SLICE[\"lips_inner\"].stop),\n                        \"brows\": slice(FACE_SLICE[\"brow_r\"].start, FACE_SLICE[\"brow_l\"].stop),\n                        \"eyes\": slice(FACE_SLICE[\"eye_r\"].start, FACE_SLICE[\"eye_l\"].stop),\n                        \"nose + contour\": slice(FACE_SLICE[\"nose\"].start, FACE_SLICE[\"oval\"].stop)})\nelse:\n    PART_GROUPS[\"face\"] = FACE\n\n# Lookup table: raw landmark index (0..542) -> our node index, or -1 if the landmark is dropped.\n_GLOBAL_TO_NODE = np.full(N_RAW, -1, dtype=np.int16)\n_GLOBAL_TO_NODE[TYPE_OFFSET[\"left_hand\"] + np.arange(21)] = np.arange(LH.start, LH.stop)\n_GLOBAL_TO_NODE[TYPE_OFFSET[\"right_hand\"] + np.arange(21)] = np.arange(RH.start, RH.stop)\n_GLOBAL_TO_NODE[TYPE_OFFSET[\"pose\"] + np.array(POSE_KEEP)] = np.arange(POSE.start, POSE.stop)\n_GLOBAL_TO_NODE[TYPE_OFFSET[\"face\"] + np.array(FACE_KEEP)] = np.arange(FACE.start, FACE.stop)\nprint(f\"{NUM_NODES} nodes per frame: 2 x 21 hand + {len(POSE_KEEP)} pose + {len(FACE_KEEP)} face ({FACE_PRESET})\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-17T22:46:43.743927Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-17T22:46:43.7442Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-17T22:46:43.757972Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-17T22:46:43.744173Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-17T22:46:43.7572Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"127 nodes per frame: 2 x 21 hand + 6 pose + 79 face (expressive)\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":3},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Plot helpers (skeleton drawing, loss curves, evaluation summary)\nHAND_EDGES = [(0, 1), (1, 2), (2, 3), (3, 4), (0, 5), (5, 6), (6, 7), (7, 8), (5, 9), (9, 10), (10, 11), (11, 12),\n              (9, 13), (13, 14), (14, 15), (15, 16), (13, 17), (17, 18), (18, 19), (19, 20), (0, 17)]\nPOSE_EDGES = [(P_LS, P_RS), (P_LS, P_LE), (P_LE, P_LW), (P_RS, P_RE), (P_RE, P_RW)]\n\n\nFACE_STYLE = {\"lips_outer\": \"crimson\", \"lips_inner\": \"darkred\", \"brow_r\": \"tab:brown\", \"brow_l\": \"tab:brown\",\n              \"eye_r\": \"tab:cyan\", \"eye_l\": \"tab:cyan\", \"nose\": \"tab:green\", \"oval\": \"tab:green\"}\nFACE_LOOPS = (\"lips_outer\", \"lips_inner\", \"eye_r\", \"eye_l\")        # drawn as closed loops\nFACE_LINES = (\"brow_r\", \"brow_l\")                                  # drawn as open lines\n\n\ndef _draw_frame(ax, f: np.ndarray):\n    \"\"\"Draw one frame f (NUM_NODES, D): arms in black, left hand blue, right hand red, face parts in their own colour.\"\"\"\n    for a, b in POSE_EDGES:\n        ax.plot(f[[a, b], 0], f[[a, b], 1], \"k-\", lw=1)\n    for sl, col in ((LH, \"tab:blue\"), (RH, \"tab:red\")):\n        for a, b in HAND_EDGES:\n            ax.plot(f[sl][[a, b], 0], f[sl][[a, b], 1], \"-\", color=col, lw=1)\n    for name, sl in FACE_SLICE.items():\n        pts, col = f[sl], FACE_STYLE.get(name, \"tab:green\")\n        if name in FACE_LOOPS:\n            pts = np.vstack([pts, pts[:1]])\n        if name in FACE_LOOPS or name in FACE_LINES:\n            ax.plot(pts[:, 0], pts[:, 1], \"-\", color=col, lw=0.8)\n        else:\n            ax.plot(pts[:, 0], pts[:, 1], \".\", color=col, ms=3)\n\n\ndef _save(fig, save_path: Optional[str], **kw):\n    if save_path:\n        fig.savefig(save_path, **kw)\n    return fig\n\n\ndef plot_sequence(seq: np.ndarray, n_frames: int = 8, title: str = \"\", save_path: Optional[str] = None):\n    \"\"\"seq (T, NUM_NODES, D) -> n_frames evenly spaced skeleton snapshots (y axis pointing down, like the image).\"\"\"\n    idx = np.linspace(0, len(seq) - 1, n_frames).astype(int)\n    fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, n_frames, figsize=(2.2 * n_frames, 2.6), sharex=True, sharey=True)\n    for ax, t in zip(np.atleast_1d(axes), idx):\n        _draw_frame(ax, seq[t])\n        ax.set_title(f\"t={t}\", fontsize=8)\n        ax.set_aspect(\"equal\")\n        ax.axis(\"off\")\n    np.atleast_1d(axes)[0].invert_yaxis()      # the axes share y, so invert it only ONCE\n    fig.suptitle(title)\n    fig.tight_layout()\n    return _save(fig, save_path, dpi=120)\n\n\ndef plot_real_vs_generated(word: str, real: np.ndarray, gen: np.ndarray, n_frames: int = 8, save_path: Optional[str] = None):\n    \"\"\"Same word: real test clips (top rows) vs generated clips (bottom rows). real / gen: (k, T, NUM_NODES, D).\"\"\"\n    rows = [(f\"real #{i + 1}\", s) for i, s in enumerate(real)] + [(f\"generated #{i + 1}\", s) for i, s in enumerate(gen)]\n    allxy = np.concatenate([s[..., :2].reshape(-1, 2) for _, s in rows])\n    lo, hi = np.percentile(allxy, 0.5, axis=0), np.percentile(allxy, 99.5, axis=0)   # common zoom for every panel\n    fig, axes = plt.subplots(len(rows), n_frames, figsize=(1.9 * n_frames, 1.9 * len(rows)), squeeze=False)\n    for r, (label, seq) in enumerate(rows):\n        for c, t in enumerate(np.linspace(0, len(seq) - 1, n_frames).astype(int)):\n            ax = axes[r, c]\n            _draw_frame(ax, seq[t])\n            ax.set_xlim(lo[0], hi[0])\n            ax.set_ylim(hi[1], lo[1])                  # inverted y\n            ax.set_aspect(\"equal\")\n            ax.axis(\"off\")\n            if r == 0:\n                ax.set_title(f\"t={t}\", fontsize=8)\n            if c == 0:\n                ax.text(-0.05, 0.5, label, transform=ax.transAxes, rotation=90, ha=\"right\", va=\"center\", fontsize=9,\n                        color=\"tab:green\" if label.startswith(\"real\") else \"tab:purple\")\n    fig.suptitle(f\"'{word}': real (unseen signers) vs generated\", y=1.0)\n    fig.tight_layout()\n    return _save(fig, save_path, dpi=110, bbox_inches=\"tight\")\n\n\ndef plot_loss_curves(hist: dict, save_path: Optional[str] = None):\n    \"\"\"Train vs validation (EMA) diffusion loss per epoch, with the best epoch marked.\"\"\"\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(6.5, 3.8))\n    ax.plot(hist[\"epoch\"], hist[\"train\"], label=\"train (random noise level, word dropout)\", color=\"tab:blue\")\n    ax.plot(hist[\"epoch\"], hist[\"val\"], label=\"validation (EMA, fixed noise)\", color=\"tab:orange\")\n    if hist[\"best_epoch\"]:\n        ax.axvline(hist[\"best_epoch\"], color=\"gray\", ls=\"--\", lw=1,\n                   label=f\"best epoch {hist['best_epoch']} ({hist['best_val']:.4f})\")\n    if hist[\"stopped_early\"]:\n        ax.annotate(\"early stop\", (hist[\"epoch\"][-1], hist[\"val\"][-1]), textcoords=\"offset points\", xytext=(-45, 15),\n                    arrowprops=dict(arrowstyle=\"->\"))\n    ax.set(xlabel=\"epoch\", ylabel=\"masked MSE (diffusion target)\", title=\"Diffusion training curves\")\n    ax.grid(alpha=0.3)\n    ax.legend()\n    fig.tight_layout()\n    return _save(fig, save_path, dpi=120)\n\n\ndef plot_eval_summary(results: dict, save_path: Optional[str] = None):\n    \"\"\"Three panels: recognition accuracy, nearest-real joint error, Fréchet distance.\"\"\"\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(13, 3.8))\n\n    w, x = 0.38, np.arange(2)\n    b1 = ax[0].bar(x - w / 2, [results[\"recognition_top1_real_test\"], results[\"recognition_top5_real_test\"]], w,\n                   color=\"tab:green\", label=\"real test clips (upper bound)\")\n    b2 = ax[0].bar(x + w / 2, [results[\"recognition_top1_generated\"], results[\"recognition_top5_generated\"]], w,\n                   color=\"tab:purple\", label=\"generated clips\")\n    ax[0].set_xticks(x, [\"top-1\", \"top-5\"])\n    ax[0].set_ylim(0, 1.1)\n    ax[0].set_title(\"Recognition accuracy (classifier trained on real train clips)\", fontsize=9)\n    ax[0].legend(fontsize=8)\n    for b in (b1, b2):\n        ax[0].bar_label(b, fmt=\"%.2f\", fontsize=8)\n\n    bars = [(\"generated -> real\\nsame word\", results[\"mpjpe_gen_to_nearest_real_same_word\"], \"tab:purple\"),\n            (\"generated -> real\\nother word\", results[\"mpjpe_gen_to_nearest_real_other_word\"], \"tab:gray\"),\n            (\"real -> real\\nsame word\", results[\"mpjpe_real_to_nearest_real_same_word\"], \"tab:green\")]\n    bars = [b for b in bars if b[1] is not None]\n    b = ax[1].bar([n for n, _, _ in bars], [v for _, v, _ in bars], color=[c for _, _, c in bars])\n    ax[1].bar_label(b, fmt=\"%.3f\", fontsize=8)\n    ax[1].set_title(\"Nearest-real MPJPE (shoulder widths, lower = better)\", fontsize=9)\n    ax[1].tick_params(axis=\"x\", labelsize=8)\n\n    fd = [results[\"frechet_distance_floor_real_train_vs_real_test\"], results[\"frechet_distance_gen_vs_real_test\"]]\n    b = ax[2].bar([\"floor: real train\\nvs real test\", \"generated\\nvs real test\"], fd, color=[\"tab:green\", \"tab:purple\"])\n    ax[2].bar_label(b, fmt=\"%.2f\", fontsize=8)\n    ax[2].set_title(\"Fréchet distance (lower = better)\", fontsize=9)\n    ax[2].tick_params(axis=\"x\", labelsize=8)\n    fig.tight_layout()\n    return _save(fig, save_path, dpi=120)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-17T22:46:43.760236Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-17T22:46:43.760958Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-17T22:46:43.789622Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-17T22:46:43.760918Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-17T22:46:43.788784Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":4},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Single-clip processing: parquet -> normalised, gap-filled, resampled (T, C) array\ndef load_selected_landmarks(path: str) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Read one parquet file -> float32 array (n_frames, NUM_NODES, 3), NaN where a landmark is missing.\n\n    Rows are mapped with (type, landmark_index) instead of relying on the row order, and only the kept\n    landmarks are materialised (not the full 543-landmark tensor).\"\"\"\n    df = pd.read_parquet(path, columns=[\"frame\", \"type\", \"landmark_index\", \"x\", \"y\", \"z\"])\n    raw_idx = df[\"type\"].map(TYPE_OFFSET).to_numpy(np.int64) + df[\"landmark_index\"].to_numpy(np.int64)\n    node = _GLOBAL_TO_NODE[raw_idx]\n    keep = node >= 0\n    df, node = df[keep], node[keep]\n    # frame numbers may not start at 0 or be contiguous -> map them to 0..n_frames-1\n    frames, frame_pos = np.unique(df[\"frame\"].to_numpy(), return_inverse=True)\n    arr = np.full((len(frames), NUM_NODES, 3), np.nan, dtype=np.float32)\n    arr[frame_pos, node] = df[[\"x\", \"y\", \"z\"]].to_numpy(dtype=np.float32)\n    return arr\n\n\ndef normalize_landmarks(arr: np.ndarray, eps: float = 1e-3) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Make coordinates independent of where the signer stands, their size and the camera distance.\n\n    One transform per CLIP (not per frame, so the real body motion is preserved):\n        centre = mean over frames of the shoulder midpoint\n        width  = mean shoulder width\n        xy'    = (xy - centre) / width   -> shoulders at about (±0.5, 0), lengths in \"shoulder widths\"\n    If the shoulders are never detected, centre/width come from the bounding box of all valid points.\"\"\"\n    arr = arr.copy()\n    xy = arr[..., :2]\n    ls, rs = xy[:, P_LS], xy[:, P_RS]\n    with np.errstate(all=\"ignore\"):                       # nanmean warns when everything is NaN\n        centre = np.nanmean((ls + rs) / 2.0, axis=0)      # (2,)\n        width = np.nanmean(np.linalg.norm(ls - rs, axis=-1))\n    if not (np.isfinite(centre).all() and np.isfinite(width) and width > eps):\n        finite = xy[np.isfinite(xy).all(-1)]\n        if len(finite) == 0:\n            return np.full_like(arr, np.nan)\n        lo, hi = finite.min(0), finite.max(0)\n        centre, width = (lo + hi) / 2.0, max(float((hi - lo).max()), eps)\n    arr[..., :2] = (xy - centre) / width\n    arr[..., 2] /= width                                  # z is only rescaled (it is not in image units)\n    return arr\n\n\ndef _interp_missing(x: np.ndarray, valid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Linear interpolation over time, vectorised. x (T, F), valid (T,) bool with at least one True.\n    Frames before the first / after the last valid frame copy the nearest valid frame.\"\"\"\n    if valid.all():\n        return x\n    t = np.arange(len(x))\n    vidx = np.nonzero(valid)[0]                           # frames with real data, e.g. [2, 5, 9]\n    # For every frame t, find the valid frames just before (left) and after (right) it:\n    #   searchsorted gives the position in vidx of the first valid frame >= t; clipping handles the two ends.\n    pos = np.searchsorted(vidx, t)\n    right = vidx[np.clip(pos, 0, len(vidx) - 1)]\n    left = vidx[np.clip(pos - 1, 0, len(vidx) - 1)]\n    # w = where t lies between left (0) and right (1); 0 if left == right (valid frames and the two ends)\n    w = np.where(right > left, (t - left) / np.maximum(right - left, 1), 0.0)[:, None]\n    return x[left] * (1.0 - w) + x[right] * w\n\n\ndef _fill_part(out: np.ndarray, part: slice, fallback) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Interpolate the frames where body part `part` is missing; use `fallback` if it is never detected.\n    Returns the (T,) bool mask of frames where the part was detected.\"\"\"\n    T = out.shape[0]\n    x = out[:, part]\n    # MediaPipe finds a whole part (e.g. all 21 hand points) or nothing, so a frame is valid if every point is finite\n    valid = np.isfinite(x[..., :2]).all(axis=(1, 2))\n    if valid.any():\n        out[:, part] = _interp_missing(x.reshape(T, -1), valid).reshape(x.shape)\n    else:\n        out[:, part] = fallback\n    return valid\n\n\ndef fill_missing(arr: np.ndarray) -> Tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n    \"\"\"Replace every NaN. Returns (filled array, present (T, 3) bool = [left hand, right hand, face] measured BEFORE filling).\n    The pose is filled first because a never-detected hand is collapsed onto its pose wrist.\"\"\"\n    out = arr.copy()\n    _fill_part(out, POSE, 0.0)\n    left = _fill_part(out, LH, out[:, P_LW][:, None, :])\n    right = _fill_part(out, RH, out[:, P_RW][:, None, :])\n    face = _fill_part(out, FACE, 0.0)\n    return np.nan_to_num(out, nan=0.0), np.stack([left, right, face], axis=1)\n\n\ndef resample_time(x: np.ndarray, t_out: int) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Linear resampling of (T, F) to (t_out, F) (also normalises the signing speed).\"\"\"\n    if len(x) == 1:\n        return np.repeat(x, t_out, axis=0)\n    pos = np.linspace(0, len(x) - 1, t_out)               # fractional source frame for every output frame\n    i0 = np.floor(pos).astype(int)\n    i1 = np.minimum(i0 + 1, len(x) - 1)\n    w = (pos - i0)[:, None]\n    return x[i0] * (1.0 - w) + x[i1] * w\n\n\ndef process_sequence(path: str, num_frames: int):\n    \"\"\"parquet path -> (features (T, NUM_NODES * 3) float16, raw n_frames, hand_frac, face_frac, ok, present (T, 3) uint8).\n    x, y AND z are kept (the model later selects its channels with `use_z`).\n    present[t] = (left hand, right hand, face) really detected in (resampled) frame t; the rest is gap-filling.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        arr = load_selected_landmarks(path)\n        if len(arr) == 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"empty sequence\")\n        arr, present = fill_missing(normalize_landmarks(arr))\n        hand_frac = float(present[:, :2].any(axis=1).mean())      # fraction of frames with at least one hand\n        face_frac = float(present[:, 2].mean())\n        x = resample_time(arr.reshape(len(arr), -1), num_frames)\n        src = np.round(np.linspace(0, len(arr) - 1, num_frames)).astype(int)   # nearest source frame (a flag cannot be interpolated)\n        return x.astype(np.float16), len(arr), hand_frac, face_frac, True, present[src].astype(np.uint8)\n    except Exception:\n        return np.zeros((num_frames, NUM_NODES * 3), np.float16), 0, 0.0, 0.0, False, np.zeros((num_frames, 3), np.uint8)\n\n\ndef _worker(args):\n    return process_sequence(*args)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-17T22:46:43.790723Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-17T22:46:43.791058Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-17T22:46:43.813388Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-17T22:46:43.791036Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-17T22:46:43.812514Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":5},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Whole-dataset preprocessing (cached on disk) + quality filter\ndef parts_path(cache_path) -> Path:\n    \"\"\"Per-frame detection flags (left hand, right hand, face), stored next to the landmark cache.\"\"\"\n    return Path(str(cache_path).replace(\".npy\", \"_parts.npy\"))\n\n\ndef preprocess_dataset(cfg: Config) -> Tuple[Path, pd.DataFrame]:\n    \"\"\"Process every parquet file once. Writes into the cache folder (`cfg.cache_dir`, default `<work_dir>/cache/`):\n        <tag>.npy        float16 (N, T, NUM_NODES * 3)  x, y, z of every node, row i = row i of train.csv\n        <tag>_parts.npy  uint8   (N, T, 3)              1 where the left hand / right hand / face was really detected\n        <tag>_meta.csv   train.csv + cache_idx, n_frames (ORIGINAL length), hand_frac, face_frac, ok\n    Later runs just reload them. The cache does not depend on `use_z`.\"\"\"\n    cache_dir = Path(cfg.cache_dir or Path(cfg.work_dir) / \"cache\")\n    cache_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    tag = f\"T{cfg.num_frames}_xyz_{NUM_NODES}nodes_{FACE_PRESET}_v3\"\n    npy_path, meta_path = cache_dir / f\"{tag}.npy\", cache_dir / f\"{tag}_meta.csv\"\n    pp = parts_path(npy_path)\n    if npy_path.exists() and pp.exists() and meta_path.exists() and not cfg.overwrite_cache:\n        print(f\"[preprocess] loading cached {npy_path}\")\n        return npy_path, pd.read_csv(meta_path)\n\n    df = pd.read_csv(Path(cfg.data_dir) / \"train.csv\")\n    # memory-mapped outputs: rows are written one by one without holding the whole dataset in RAM\n    cache = np.lib.format.open_memmap(npy_path, mode=\"w+\", dtype=np.float16, shape=(len(df), cfg.num_frames, NUM_NODES * 3))\n    parts = np.lib.format.open_memmap(pp, mode=\"w+\", dtype=np.uint8, shape=(len(df), cfg.num_frames, 3))\n    tasks = [(str(Path(cfg.data_dir) / p), cfg.num_frames) for p in df[\"path\"]]\n    stats = np.zeros((len(df), 4), np.float32)            # n_frames, hand_frac, face_frac, ok\n\n    with Pool(cfg.num_proc) as pool:\n        # imap keeps the input order, so result i belongs to row i\n        for i, (feat, n, hand_frac, face_frac, ok, pres) in enumerate(\n                tqdm(pool.imap(_worker, tasks, chunksize=32), total=len(tasks), desc=\"preprocess\")):\n            cache[i], parts[i] = feat, pres\n            stats[i] = n, hand_frac, face_frac, ok\n    cache.flush()\n    parts.flush()\n\n    meta = df.assign(cache_idx=np.arange(len(df)), n_frames=stats[:, 0].astype(int), hand_frac=stats[:, 1],\n                     face_frac=stats[:, 2], ok=stats[:, 3].astype(bool))\n    meta.to_csv(meta_path, index=False)                   # written last: an interrupted run leaves no valid cache\n    print(f\"[preprocess] {meta['ok'].sum()}/{len(meta)} clips OK -> {npy_path}\")\n    return npy_path, meta\n\n\ndef filter_quality(meta: pd.DataFrame, cfg: Config) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    \"\"\"Drop only unusable clips: failed preprocessing and clips shorter than `min_frames`. Clips with few detected hands are\n    kept (their undetected hands are ignored by the loss); `min_hand_frac > 0` would remove them, it is off by default.\"\"\"\n    failed = ~meta[\"ok\"]\n    short = meta[\"ok\"] & (meta[\"n_frames\"] < cfg.min_frames)\n    few_hands = meta[\"ok\"] & ~short & (meta[\"hand_frac\"] < cfg.min_hand_frac)\n    keep = ~(failed | short | few_hands)\n    print(f\"[filter] kept {int(keep.sum())}/{len(meta)} clips | dropped: {int(failed.sum())} failed, \"\n          f\"{int(short.sum())} too short, {int(few_hands.sum())} with too few hand frames\")\n    clean = (meta.loc[keep, \"hand_frac\"] >= cfg.clean_hand_frac).mean()\n    print(f\"[filter] {clean:.0%} of the kept clips are 'clean' (hands detected in >= {cfg.clean_hand_frac:.0%} of the frames) | \"\n          f\"face detected in >= 50 % of the frames: {(meta.loc[keep, 'face_frac'] >= 0.5).mean():.0%}\")\n    return meta[keep].reset_index(drop=True)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-17T22:46:43.814374Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-17T22:46:43.814648Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-17T22:46:43.847793Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-17T22:46:43.814628Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-17T22:46:43.846929Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":6},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### ▶ Run preprocessing\nFirst run only: reads every parquet file (the result is cached). Shows the dataset size, the distribution of raw clip lengths and\nof hand visibility (red line = `clean_hand_frac`, the limit of the *clean* subset used for reporting), what the filter removes\n(only corrupt clips) and one preprocessed clip (the face is drawn in detail: lips, eyes, brows).","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"cache_path, meta_all = preprocess_dataset(cfg)\nclips_per_sign = meta_all[\"sign\"].value_counts()\nprint(f\"{len(meta_all)} clips | {meta_all['sign'].nunique()} signs | {meta_all['participant_id'].nunique()} signers | \"\n      f\"clips per sign: min {clips_per_sign.min()}, median {int(clips_per_sign.median())}, max {clips_per_sign.max()}\")\ndisplay(meta_all.head())\n\nfig, ax = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(10, 3))\nax[0].hist(meta_all[\"n_frames\"].clip(upper=100), bins=50)\nax[0].set_title(\"raw clip length (frames, clipped at 100)\")\nax[1].hist(meta_all[\"hand_frac\"], bins=40)\nax[1].axvline(cfg.clean_hand_frac, color=\"r\", ls=\"--\", label=\"clean_hand_frac\")\nax[1].set_title(\"fraction of frames with a detected hand\")\nax[1].legend()\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()\n\nmeta = filter_quality(meta_all, cfg)\n\n# what the model actually sees: normalised, gap-filled, resampled to T frames\nrow = meta.iloc[0]\nseq = np.asarray(np.load(cache_path, mmap_mode=\"r\")[row[\"cache_idx\"]], np.float32).reshape(cfg.num_frames, NUM_NODES, -1)\n_ = plot_sequence(seq, title=f\"preprocessed example: '{row['sign']}' (signer {row['participant_id']})\")\nplt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-17T22:46:43.848839Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-17T22:46:43.849188Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-17T22:57:24.84001Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-17T22:46:43.849152Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-17T22:57:24.839281Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"preprocess:   0%|          | 0/94477 [00:00<?, ?it/s]","application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"version_major":2,"version_minor":0,"model_id":"2aea429d28e14261b928def0940954a5"}},"metadata":{}},{"name":"stdout","text":"[preprocess] 94477/94477 clips OK -> /kaggle/working/cache/T64_xyz_127nodes_expressive_v3.npy\n94477 clips | 250 signs | 21 signers | clips per sign: min 299, median 381, max 415\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"                                            path  participant_id  sequence_id  \\\n0  train_landmark_files/26734/1000035562.parquet           26734   1000035562   \n1  train_landmark_files/28656/1000106739.parquet           28656   1000106739   \n2   train_landmark_files/16069/100015657.parquet           16069    100015657   \n3  train_landmark_files/25571/1000210073.parquet           25571   1000210073   \n4  train_landmark_files/62590/1000240708.parquet           62590   1000240708   \n\n    sign  cache_idx  n_frames  hand_frac  face_frac    ok  \n0   blow          0        23   0.478261        1.0  True  \n1   wait          1        11   0.181818        1.0  True  \n2  cloud          2       105   0.266667        1.0  True  \n3   bird          3        12   1.000000        1.0  True  \n4   owie          4        18   1.000000        1.0  True  ","text/html":"<div>\n<style scoped>\n    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n        vertical-align: middle;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n        vertical-align: top;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe thead th {\n        text-align: right;\n    }\n</style>\n<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n  <thead>\n    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n      <th></th>\n      <th>path</th>\n      <th>participant_id</th>\n      <th>sequence_id</th>\n      <th>sign</th>\n      <th>cache_idx</th>\n      <th>n_frames</th>\n      <th>hand_frac</th>\n      <th>face_frac</th>\n      <th>ok</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <th>0</th>\n      <td>train_landmark_files/26734/1000035562.parquet</td>\n      <td>26734</td>\n      <td>1000035562</td>\n      <td>blow</td>\n      <td>0</td>\n      <td>23</td>\n      <td>0.478261</td>\n      <td>1.0</td>\n      <td>True</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>1</th>\n      <td>train_landmark_files/28656/1000106739.parquet</td>\n      <td>28656</td>\n      <td>1000106739</td>\n      <td>wait</td>\n      <td>1</td>\n      <td>11</td>\n      <td>0.181818</td>\n      <td>1.0</td>\n      <td>True</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>2</th>\n      <td>train_landmark_files/16069/100015657.parquet</td>\n      <td>16069</td>\n      <td>100015657</td>\n      <td>cloud</td>\n      <td>2</td>\n      <td>105</td>\n      <td>0.266667</td>\n      <td>1.0</td>\n      <td>True</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>3</th>\n      <td>train_landmark_files/25571/1000210073.parquet</td>\n      <td>25571</td>\n      <td>1000210073</td>\n      <td>bird</td>\n      <td>3</td>\n      <td>12</td>\n      <td>1.000000</td>\n      <td>1.0</td>\n      <td>True</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>4</th>\n      <td>train_landmark_files/62590/1000240708.parquet</td>\n      <td>62590</td>\n      <td>1000240708</td>\n      <td>owie</td>\n      <td>4</td>\n      <td>18</td>\n      <td>1.000000</td>\n      <td>1.0</td>\n      <td>True</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n</div>"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1000x300 with 2 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"name":"stdout","text":"[filter] kept 94374/94477 clips | dropped: 0 failed, 103 too short, 0 with too few hand frames\n[filter] 69% of the kept clips are 'clean' (hands detected in >= 50% of the frames) | face detected in >= 50 % of the frames: 100%\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1760x260 with 8 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":7},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 2. Signer-independent splitting\n\nThe split uses every clip that survives the filter (only corrupt or too-short clips are removed), so the balance is measured on the data that is really used.\n\n* **Test** and **validation** each receive whole signers (≈ 20 % and ≈ 10 % of them). None of them appears in train, so the\n  validation loss (used for early stopping) and the test metrics both measure generalisation to *new* signers.\n* A signer's clips cannot be re-balanced, so we **search** the signer subset that best mimics the whole dataset\n  (every combination when there are few, otherwise random subsets). Each candidate gets a score (lower = better):\n  * distance between its sign distribution and the overall one (total variation),\n  * gap between its size and the target size,\n  * a large penalty for every sign with fewer than `min_test_per_sign` / `min_val_per_sign` clips.\n* Sanity checks: no signer in two splits, no clip lost or duplicated, every sign present in train.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Splitting\ndef choose_signers(counts: pd.DataFrame, k: int, target_dist: np.ndarray, target_size: float, min_per_sign: int,\n                   rng: np.random.Generator, n_trials: int) -> List:\n    \"\"\"Pick k signers (rows of `counts`, a signers x signs table of clip counts) whose clips best mimic the dataset.\"\"\"\n    n_signers = len(counts)\n    if math.comb(n_signers, k) <= n_trials:                       # e.g. C(21, 4) = 5985: try them all\n        candidates = itertools.combinations(range(n_signers), k)\n    else:\n        candidates = (rng.choice(n_signers, k, replace=False) for _ in range(n_trials))\n    total, table = counts.values.sum(), counts.values\n    best, best_score = None, float(\"inf\")\n    for rows in candidates:\n        c = table[list(rows)].sum(0)                              # clips per sign if these signers are chosen\n        tv = 0.5 * np.abs(c / c.sum() - target_dist).sum()        # 0 = same sign distribution as the full data\n        size_gap = abs(c.sum() - target_size) / total             # 0 = exactly the requested size\n        too_few = (c < min_per_sign).mean()                       # share of signs with too few clips\n        score = tv + size_gap + 10.0 * too_few\n        if score < best_score:\n            best, best_score = list(rows), score\n    return list(counts.index[best])\n\n\ndef make_splits(meta: pd.DataFrame, cfg: Config) -> Dict[str, pd.DataFrame]:\n    \"\"\"meta (already quality-filtered) -> {\"train\", \"val\", \"test\"} with disjoint signers.\"\"\"\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(cfg.seed)\n    counts = pd.crosstab(meta[\"participant_id\"], meta[\"sign\"])   # signers x signs\n    n_signers, total = len(counts), len(meta)\n    target_dist = counts.values.sum(0) / total\n\n    test_ids = choose_signers(counts, max(1, round(cfg.test_frac * n_signers)), target_dist, cfg.test_frac * total,\n                              cfg.min_test_per_sign, rng, cfg.split_trials)\n    rest = counts.drop(index=test_ids)\n    val_ids = choose_signers(rest, max(1, round(cfg.val_frac * n_signers)), target_dist, cfg.val_frac * total,\n                             cfg.min_val_per_sign, rng, cfg.split_trials)\n\n    split_of = meta[\"participant_id\"].map(lambda p: \"test\" if p in test_ids else \"val\" if p in val_ids else \"train\")\n    splits = {name: meta[split_of == name].reset_index(drop=True) for name in (\"train\", \"val\", \"test\")}\n\n    # ---- sanity checks ----\n    signers = {name: set(d[\"participant_id\"]) for name, d in splits.items()}\n    assert not (signers[\"train\"] & signers[\"val\"] or signers[\"train\"] & signers[\"test\"] or signers[\"val\"] & signers[\"test\"]), \\\n        \"a signer appears in two splits\"\n    assert sum(len(d) for d in splits.values()) == total, \"clips lost or duplicated\"\n    missing = set(meta[\"sign\"]) - set(splits[\"train\"][\"sign\"])\n    assert not missing, f\"signs absent from train: {missing}\"\n    return splits\n\n\ndef report_splits(splits: Dict[str, pd.DataFrame], clean_thr: float = 0.5) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    \"\"\"One row per split: size, signers, sign coverage, clips per sign, distance to the overall sign distribution,\n    share of clean clips (hands detected in >= clean_thr of the frames).\"\"\"\n    all_signs = sorted(pd.concat(splits.values())[\"sign\"].unique())\n    overall = pd.concat(splits.values())[\"sign\"].value_counts().reindex(all_signs)\n    overall = overall / overall.sum()\n    total = sum(len(d) for d in splits.values())\n    rows = []\n    for name, d in splits.items():\n        vc = d[\"sign\"].value_counts().reindex(all_signs, fill_value=0)\n        rows.append(dict(split=name, clips=len(d), share=f\"{len(d) / total:.1%}\", signers=d[\"participant_id\"].nunique(),\n                         signs_present=int((vc > 0).sum()), min_per_sign=int(vc.min()), max_per_sign=int(vc.max()),\n                         TV_vs_overall=round(float(0.5 * np.abs(vc / vc.sum() - overall).sum()), 4),\n                         clean_share=f\"{(d['hand_frac'] >= clean_thr).mean():.0%}\"))\n    return pd.DataFrame(rows)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-17T22:57:24.841283Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-17T22:57:24.841581Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-17T22:57:24.859741Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-17T22:57:24.841555Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-17T22:57:24.858956Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":8},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### ▶ Run the split\nShows the split table (`TV_vs_overall` = distance between the split's sign distribution and the overall one; 0 = identical)\nand which signers ended up where.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"splits = make_splits(meta, cfg)\ndisplay(report_splits(splits, cfg.clean_hand_frac))\nfor name in (\"val\", \"test\"):\n    print(f\"{name:4s} signers:\", sorted(int(p) for p in splits[name][\"participant_id\"].unique()))\n\nper_signer = (pd.concat([d.assign(split=n) for n, d in splits.items()])\n              .groupby([\"participant_id\", \"split\"]).size().unstack(fill_value=0)[[\"train\", \"val\", \"test\"]])\nper_signer.plot(kind=\"bar\", stacked=True, figsize=(10, 3), title=\"clips per signer, coloured by split\")\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-17T22:57:24.860721Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-17T22:57:24.860998Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-17T22:57:25.580316Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-17T22:57:24.860968Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-17T22:57:25.579688Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"   split  clips  share  signers  signs_present  min_per_sign  max_per_sign  \\\n0  train  66061  70.0%       15            250           206           299   \n1    val   9439  10.0%        2            250            29            43   \n2   test  18874  20.0%        4            250            58            86   \n\n   TV_vs_overall clean_share  \n0         0.0063         68%  \n1         0.0224         72%  \n2         0.0158         73%  ","text/html":"<div>\n<style scoped>\n    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n        vertical-align: middle;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n        vertical-align: top;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe thead th {\n        text-align: right;\n    }\n</style>\n<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n  <thead>\n    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n      <th></th>\n      <th>split</th>\n      <th>clips</th>\n      <th>share</th>\n      <th>signers</th>\n      <th>signs_present</th>\n      <th>min_per_sign</th>\n      <th>max_per_sign</th>\n      <th>TV_vs_overall</th>\n      <th>clean_share</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <th>0</th>\n      <td>train</td>\n      <td>66061</td>\n      <td>70.0%</td>\n      <td>15</td>\n      <td>250</td>\n      <td>206</td>\n      <td>299</td>\n      <td>0.0063</td>\n      <td>68%</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>1</th>\n      <td>val</td>\n      <td>9439</td>\n      <td>10.0%</td>\n      <td>2</td>\n      <td>250</td>\n      <td>29</td>\n      <td>43</td>\n      <td>0.0224</td>\n      <td>72%</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>2</th>\n      <td>test</td>\n      <td>18874</td>\n      <td>20.0%</td>\n      <td>4</td>\n      <td>250</td>\n      <td>58</td>\n      <td>86</td>\n      <td>0.0158</td>\n      <td>73%</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n</div>"},"metadata":{}},{"name":"stdout","text":"val  signers: [34503, 61333]\ntest signers: [22343, 32319, 36257, 62590]\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1000x300 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":9},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 3. Word conditioning + Dataset\n\n`SignVocab` maps words to ids: id 0 is the *null* word (used for classifier-free guidance), ids 1–250 are the signs.\nThe model learns one embedding per word. Optionally, `build_text_embedding_table` turns each word into a frozen sentence\nembedding (needs `transformers` and internet) so that the conditioning carries word semantics.\n\nThe dataset standardises every clip with a per-coordinate mean and **one global std**, both computed on the **train** split only,\nand applies a random rotation / zoom / shift to the train clips (the same transform for every frame, so the motion is unchanged).\n\n**Duration.** All clips are resampled to 64 frames, which would erase how long a sign really lasts (a 0.4 s sign and a 2 s sign look alike).\nThe original length (`n_frames`) is therefore kept and given to the model as a second condition: a standardised *log-duration*.\n`DurationPrior` stores, per word, the mean and spread of the log-duration measured on the **train** clips (shrunk towards the global\nvalues for words with few clips); it is used to *predict* a plausible duration when the user only gives a word. The frame rate of the\nvideos is not given by the competition: `cfg.fps = 30` is an assumption that only affects the conversion to seconds.\n\n**Which parts were detected?** The dataset also returns `present (T, 3)` (left hand, right hand, face detected in that frame) and builds\nthe loss weights from it (`dataset.weights`).","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Vocabulary / optional text embedding\nclass SignVocab:\n    NULL_ID = 0\n\n    def __init__(self, words: List[str]):\n        self.itos = [\"<null>\"] + sorted({self.normalize(w) for w in words})\n        self.stoi = {w: i for i, w in enumerate(self.itos)}\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def normalize(word: str) -> str:\n        return str(word).strip().lower()\n\n    def encode(self, word: str) -> int:\n        return self.stoi[self.normalize(word)]\n\n    def decode(self, idx: int) -> str:\n        return self.itos[idx]\n\n    def __len__(self) -> int:          # includes the null word\n        return len(self.itos)\n\n    def save(self, path) -> None:\n        Path(path).write_text(json.dumps(self.itos))\n\n    @classmethod\n    def from_itos(cls, itos: List[str]) -> \"SignVocab\":\n        v = cls([])\n        v.itos = list(itos)\n        v.stoi = {w: i for i, w in enumerate(v.itos)}\n        return v\n\n\n@torch.no_grad()\ndef build_text_embedding_table(vocab: SignVocab, model_name: str = \"sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2\",\n                               device: str = \"cpu\") -> torch.Tensor:\n    \"\"\"OPTIONAL. (len(vocab), D) frozen, mean-pooled sentence embedding per word; row 0 (null word) is zeros.\"\"\"\n    from transformers import AutoModel, AutoTokenizer\n    tok, enc = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(model_name), AutoModel.from_pretrained(model_name).to(device).eval()\n    batch = tok(vocab.itos[1:], padding=True, return_tensors=\"pt\").to(device)\n    h = enc(**batch).last_hidden_state\n    m = batch[\"attention_mask\"].unsqueeze(-1).float()\n    emb = F.normalize((h * m).sum(1) / m.sum(1), dim=-1).cpu()      # average over the real tokens only\n    return torch.cat([torch.zeros(1, emb.shape[1]), emb], dim=0)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-17T22:57:25.582882Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-17T22:57:25.583396Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-17T22:57:25.592415Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-17T22:57:25.583366Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-17T22:57:25.591709Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":10},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Duration prior + normalisation statistics + Dataset\nclass DurationPrior:\n    \"\"\"How long does each sign last? Log-duration statistics of the TRAIN clips, per word and overall.\n\n    * `standardise(n_frames)` -> the number given to the model as condition ((log n - mean) / std over all clips).\n    * `sample(ids)`           -> a plausible condition for each word id: log n ~ Normal(word mean, word std).\n    * `seconds(z)`            -> back to seconds (needs `fps`, ASSUMED to be 30 unless you know better).\n    Words with few clips are pulled towards the global statistics (`shrink` = pseudo-count).\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, fps: float, log_mu: float, log_sd: float, word_mu: np.ndarray, word_sd: np.ndarray):\n        self.fps, self.log_mu, self.log_sd = float(fps), float(log_mu), float(log_sd)\n        self.word_mu, self.word_sd = np.asarray(word_mu, np.float64), np.asarray(word_sd, np.float64)\n\n    @classmethod\n    def fit(cls, meta_train: pd.DataFrame, vocab: \"SignVocab\", fps: float = 30.0, shrink: float = 5.0) -> \"DurationPrior\":\n        logn = np.log(np.maximum(meta_train[\"n_frames\"].to_numpy(np.float64), 1.0))\n        mu, sd = logn.mean(), logn.std() + 1e-6\n        ids = np.array([vocab.encode(s) for s in meta_train[\"sign\"]])\n        word_mu, word_sd = np.full(len(vocab), mu), np.full(len(vocab), sd)          # id 0 (null word) keeps the global values\n        for w in np.unique(ids):\n            v = logn[ids == w]\n            n = len(v)\n            word_mu[w] = (v.sum() + shrink * mu) / (n + shrink)\n            word_sd[w] = math.sqrt((n * v.var() + shrink * sd ** 2) / (n + shrink))\n        return cls(fps, mu, sd, word_mu, word_sd)\n\n    def standardise(self, n_frames) -> np.ndarray:\n        return (np.log(np.maximum(np.asarray(n_frames, np.float64), 1.0)) - self.log_mu) / self.log_sd\n\n    def seconds(self, z) -> np.ndarray:\n        return np.exp(np.asarray(z, np.float64) * self.log_sd + self.log_mu) / self.fps\n\n    def typical(self, ids) -> np.ndarray:\n        \"\"\"Standardised duration of an average clip of each word.\"\"\"\n        return (self.word_mu[np.asarray(ids)] - self.log_mu) / self.log_sd\n\n    def sample(self, ids, rng: np.random.Generator, temperature: float = 1.0) -> np.ndarray:\n        ids = np.asarray(ids)\n        logn = self.word_mu[ids] + temperature * self.word_sd[ids] * rng.standard_normal(len(ids))\n        return (logn - self.log_mu) / self.log_sd\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n        return dict(fps=self.fps, log_mu=self.log_mu, log_sd=self.log_sd, word_mu=self.word_mu.tolist(), word_sd=self.word_sd.tolist())\n\n    @classmethod\n    def from_dict(cls, d: dict) -> \"DurationPrior\":\n        return cls(d[\"fps\"], d[\"log_mu\"], d[\"log_sd\"], d[\"word_mu\"], d[\"word_sd\"])\n\n\ndef select_xyz(x: np.ndarray, D: int) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"(..., NUM_NODES * 3) cached x, y, z  ->  (..., NUM_NODES * D): keep (x, y) or (x, y, z) of every node.\"\"\"\n    return x.reshape(*x.shape[:-1], NUM_NODES, 3)[..., :D].reshape(*x.shape[:-1], NUM_NODES * D)\n\n\ndef compute_stats(cache_path, meta_train: pd.DataFrame, use_z: bool, max_clips: int = 10000, seed: int = 0,\n                  chunk: int = 500) -> Tuple[np.ndarray, float]:\n    \"\"\"Per-coordinate mean and ONE global std, estimated on (a subset of) the TRAIN clips, read chunk by chunk.\n\n    A single std is deliberate: after shoulder-centring the shoulder coordinates barely move, and dividing them\n    by their tiny own std would blow up their noise in the diffusion target.\"\"\"\n    cache, D = np.load(cache_path, mmap_mode=\"r\"), (3 if use_z else 2)\n    rows = np.random.default_rng(seed).choice(len(meta_train), size=min(max_clips, len(meta_train)), replace=False)\n    rows = np.sort(meta_train[\"cache_idx\"].to_numpy()[rows])\n    s1 = s2 = 0.0\n    n = 0\n    for i in range(0, len(rows), chunk):\n        x = select_xyz(np.asarray(cache[rows[i:i + chunk]], np.float32), D).reshape(-1, NUM_NODES * D).astype(np.float64)\n        s1, s2, n = s1 + x.sum(0), s2 + (x ** 2).sum(0), n + len(x)\n    mean = s1 / n\n    return mean.astype(np.float32), float(np.sqrt(max((s2 / n - mean ** 2).mean(), 1e-12)))\n\n\nclass ASLLandmarkDataset(Dataset):\n    \"\"\"Yields dict(landmarks (T, C) standardised, mask (T,) all True, present (T, 3) bool [left hand, right hand, face],\n    dur (standardised log-duration), token_id, participant_id[, text_emb]).\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, meta: pd.DataFrame, cache_path, vocab: SignVocab, stats: Tuple[np.ndarray, float],\n                 dur_prior: DurationPrior, use_z: bool = False, augment: bool = False, text_table: Optional[torch.Tensor] = None,\n                 face_w: float = 0.3, rot_deg: float = 10.0, scale_range: float = 0.1, shift_range: float = 0.05):\n        self.meta = meta.reset_index(drop=True)\n        self.cache_path = str(cache_path)\n        self._cache = self._pres = None         # opened lazily, so each DataLoader worker owns its memmap\n        self.pres_path = str(parts_path(cache_path))\n        self.cache_idx = self.meta[\"cache_idx\"].to_numpy()\n        self.token_ids = np.array([vocab.encode(s) for s in self.meta[\"sign\"]], dtype=np.int64)\n        self.participants = self.meta[\"participant_id\"].to_numpy()\n        self.D = 3 if use_z else 2\n        self.T, c_cache = np.load(self.cache_path, mmap_mode=\"r\").shape[1:]\n        assert c_cache == NUM_NODES * 3, f\"cache has {c_cache} channels, expected {NUM_NODES * 3}: wrong FACE_PRESET / old cache?\"\n        self.C = NUM_NODES * self.D\n        self.mean, self.std = np.asarray(stats[0], np.float32), float(stats[1])\n        self.dur = dur_prior.standardise(self.meta[\"n_frames\"].to_numpy()).astype(np.float32)\n        self.augment, self.text_table, self.face_w = augment, text_table, face_w\n        self.rot_deg, self.scale_range, self.shift_range = rot_deg, scale_range, shift_range\n\n    def __len__(self) -> int:\n        return len(self.meta)\n\n    def _get_cache(self):\n        if self._cache is None:\n            self._cache = np.load(self.cache_path, mmap_mode=\"r\")\n        return self._cache\n\n    def _get_pres(self):\n        if self._pres is None:\n            self._pres = np.load(self.pres_path, mmap_mode=\"r\")\n        return self._pres\n\n    def load_raw(self, cache_rows) -> np.ndarray:\n        \"\"\"Cached clips of the given cache rows -> float32 (n, T, C) with the model's channels (not standardised).\"\"\"\n        return select_xyz(np.asarray(self._get_cache()[cache_rows], dtype=np.float32), self.D)\n\n    def weights(self, present: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n        \"\"\"present (B, T, 3) bool -> loss weights (B, T, C). A coordinate gets weight 0 when it is only gap-filling (hand or face\n        not detected in that frame), `face_w` for a detected face coordinate, 1 otherwise. Channels are laid out node by node.\"\"\"\n        B, T, _ = present.shape\n        D = self.D\n        w = torch.ones(B, T, NUM_NODES * D, device=present.device)\n        w[..., LH.start * D:LH.stop * D] = present[..., 0:1].float()\n        w[..., RH.start * D:RH.stop * D] = present[..., 1:2].float()\n        w[..., FACE.start * D:FACE.stop * D] = present[..., 2:3].float() * self.face_w\n        return w\n\n    def _augment(self, x: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n        \"\"\"One random rotation + zoom + shift per clip, applied identically to every frame and joint.\"\"\"\n        # torch's RNG is used because it is seeded differently in every DataLoader worker (numpy's is not)\n        def uniform(lo, hi):\n            return lo + (hi - lo) * torch.rand(1).item()\n        th = math.radians(uniform(-self.rot_deg, self.rot_deg))\n        s = uniform(1 - self.scale_range, 1 + self.scale_range)\n        shift = np.array([uniform(-self.shift_range, self.shift_range) for _ in range(2)], np.float32)\n        R = np.array([[math.cos(th), -math.sin(th)], [math.sin(th), math.cos(th)]], np.float32)\n        v = x.reshape(self.T, -1, self.D).copy()                  # (T, nodes, D)\n        v[..., :2] = (v[..., :2] @ R.T) * s + shift\n        if self.D == 3:\n            v[..., 2] *= s\n        return v.reshape(self.T, -1)\n\n    def __getitem__(self, idx: int) -> dict:\n        x = self.load_raw(self.cache_idx[idx])\n        if self.augment:\n            x = self._augment(x)\n        x = (x - self.mean) / self.std\n        present = np.asarray(self._get_pres()[self.cache_idx[idx]], dtype=bool)      # (T, 3): which parts were detected\n        item = {\"landmarks\": torch.from_numpy(x), \"mask\": torch.ones(self.T, dtype=torch.bool),\n                \"present\": torch.from_numpy(present), \"dur\": torch.tensor(self.dur[idx]),\n                \"token_id\": torch.tensor(self.token_ids[idx]), \"participant_id\": torch.tensor(int(self.participants[idx]))}\n        if self.text_table is not None:\n            item[\"text_emb\"] = self.text_table[self.token_ids[idx]]\n        return item\n\n\ndef make_loaders(cfg: Config, cache_path, splits: Dict[str, pd.DataFrame], vocab: SignVocab,\n                 text_table: Optional[torch.Tensor] = None) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"splits -> train-only statistics (+ duration prior) -> one Dataset and one DataLoader per split.\"\"\"\n    stats = compute_stats(cache_path, splits[\"train\"], cfg.use_z)\n    dur_prior = DurationPrior.fit(splits[\"train\"], vocab, cfg.fps, cfg.dur_prior_shrink)\n    np.savez(Path(cfg.work_dir) / \"stats.npz\", mean=stats[0], std=stats[1])\n    Path(cfg.work_dir, \"duration_prior.json\").write_text(json.dumps(dur_prior.to_dict()))\n    vocab.save(Path(cfg.work_dir) / \"vocab.json\")\n    datasets = {name: ASLLandmarkDataset(df, cache_path, vocab, stats, dur_prior, cfg.use_z, text_table=text_table,\n                                         augment=cfg.augment and name == \"train\", face_w=cfg.face_loss_weight)   # val/test stay deterministic\n                for name, df in splits.items()}\n    loaders = {name: DataLoader(ds, batch_size=cfg.batch_size, shuffle=name == \"train\", drop_last=name == \"train\",\n                                num_workers=cfg.num_workers, pin_memory=torch.cuda.is_available(),\n                                persistent_workers=cfg.num_workers > 0)\n               for name, ds in datasets.items()}\n    return dict(loaders=loaders, datasets=datasets, vocab=vocab, stats=stats, dur_prior=dur_prior, splits=splits, cache_path=cache_path)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-17T22:57:25.593568Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-17T22:57:25.593927Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-17T22:57:25.628246Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-17T22:57:25.593905Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-17T22:57:25.627517Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":11},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### ▶ Build datasets and data loaders\nAlso fits the duration prior and shows what the typical duration of a few words is.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"vocab = SignVocab(meta[\"sign\"].tolist())\ndata = make_loaders(cfg, cache_path, splits, vocab)\nloaders, datasets, stats, dur_prior = data[\"loaders\"], data[\"datasets\"], data[\"stats\"], data[\"dur_prior\"]\nT, C = datasets[\"train\"].T, datasets[\"train\"].C\n\nbatch = next(iter(loaders[\"train\"]))\nfor k, v in batch.items():\n    print(f\"{k:15s} shape={tuple(v.shape)} dtype={v.dtype}\")\nprint(f\"standardised landmarks: mean={batch['landmarks'].mean():.3f}  std={batch['landmarks'].std():.3f}  (should be ~0 and ~1)\")\nprint(\"example words:\", [vocab.decode(int(i)) for i in batch[\"token_id\"][:8]])\nprint(\"clips per split:\", {n: len(ds) for n, ds in datasets.items()})\nw_ex = [\"thankyou\", \"hello\", \"airplane\"] if \"thankyou\" in vocab.stoi else vocab.itos[1:4]\nprint(\"typical duration (s) per word, from the train clips (fps assumed %.0f):\" % cfg.fps,\n      {w: round(float(dur_prior.seconds(dur_prior.typical([vocab.encode(w)]))[0]), 2) for w in w_ex})","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-17T22:57:25.629253Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-17T22:57:25.629781Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-17T22:57:32.644902Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-17T22:57:25.629759Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-17T22:57:32.643379Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"landmarks       shape=(128, 64, 254) dtype=torch.float32\nmask            shape=(128, 64) dtype=torch.bool\npresent         shape=(128, 64, 3) dtype=torch.bool\ndur             shape=(128,) dtype=torch.float32\ntoken_id        shape=(128,) dtype=torch.int64\nparticipant_id  shape=(128,) dtype=torch.int64\nstandardised landmarks: mean=-0.008  std=1.040  (should be ~0 and ~1)\nexample words: ['red', 'zipper', 'see', 'farm', 'will', 'because', 'chocolate', 'tongue']\nclips per split: {'train': 66061, 'val': 9439, 'test': 18874}\ntypical duration (s) per word, from the train clips (fps assumed 30): {'thankyou': 0.54, 'hello': 0.65, 'airplane': 0.89}\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":12},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 4. Diffusion model\n\n**Denoiser** – a DiT-style Transformer. Every *frame* is one token (`C = 114` coordinates → `d_model`) with a fixed sinusoidal\nposition code. The diffusion step, the word and the **duration** are merged into one conditioning vector that modulates every block through\n**adaLN-Zero** (shift / scale / gate predicted from the condition, zero-initialised so every block starts as the identity).\n\n**Diffusion** – cosine noise schedule, `eps` / `x0` / `v` prediction (default `v`), MSE loss. During training the word is\nreplaced by the null word 10 % of the time, which lets the sampler use **classifier-free guidance**. Sampling uses\ndeterministic **DDIM** with 50 steps.\n\n**Duration condition** – a standardised log-duration goes through a small MLP and is *added* to the conditioning vector. During training\nit is hidden together with the word (the unconditional branch of guidance) and, independently, 10 % of the time on its own\n(`p_dur_drop`), so the model also works when the user gives only a word. A learned *null duration* vector is used when it is hidden.\n\n**Loss weights** – coordinates of a hand / of the face that were not detected get weight 0, face coordinates get `face_loss_weight`\n(79 face points would otherwise outweigh the 42 hand points that carry most of the meaning).","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Building blocks\ndef sinusoidal_embedding(x: torch.Tensor, dim: int, max_period: float = 10000.0) -> torch.Tensor:\n    \"\"\"x (...,) -> (..., dim) sin/cos embedding (used for diffusion steps and frame positions).\"\"\"\n    half = dim // 2\n    freqs = torch.exp(-math.log(max_period) * torch.arange(half, device=x.device, dtype=torch.float32) / half)\n    args = x.float().unsqueeze(-1) * freqs\n    emb = torch.cat([torch.cos(args), torch.sin(args)], dim=-1)\n    return F.pad(emb, (0, dim % 2))\n\n\nclass ConditionEncoder(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"word id (0 = null) -> conditioning vector (B, d_model).\n    Learned embedding by default, or an MLP over a frozen text-embedding table.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, num_tokens: int, d_model: int, text_table: Optional[torch.Tensor] = None):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.table = None\n        if text_table is None:\n            self.embed = nn.Embedding(num_tokens, d_model)\n        else:\n            self.register_buffer(\"table\", text_table.float(), persistent=True)\n            self.proj = nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(text_table.shape[1], d_model), nn.SiLU(), nn.Linear(d_model, d_model))\n            self.null = nn.Parameter(torch.zeros(d_model))          # learned \"no word\" vector\n\n    def forward(self, ids: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n        if self.table is None:\n            return self.embed(ids)\n        out = self.proj(self.table[ids])\n        return torch.where((ids == 0).unsqueeze(-1), self.null.expand_as(out), out)\n\n\nclass DiTBlock(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"Transformer block conditioned with adaLN-Zero.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, d: int, heads: int, mlp_ratio: float = 4.0, dropout: float = 0.0):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.norm1 = nn.LayerNorm(d, elementwise_affine=False, eps=1e-6)\n        self.attn = nn.MultiheadAttention(d, heads, dropout=dropout, batch_first=True)\n        self.norm2 = nn.LayerNorm(d, elementwise_affine=False, eps=1e-6)\n        hidden = int(d * mlp_ratio)\n        self.mlp = nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(d, hidden), nn.GELU(approximate=\"tanh\"), nn.Dropout(dropout), nn.Linear(hidden, d))\n        self.ada = nn.Sequential(nn.SiLU(), nn.Linear(d, 6 * d))\n        nn.init.zeros_(self.ada[-1].weight)\n        nn.init.zeros_(self.ada[-1].bias)\n\n    def forward(self, x: torch.Tensor, c: torch.Tensor, key_padding_mask: Optional[torch.Tensor] = None) -> torch.Tensor:\n        # The condition c predicts a shift / scale / gate for the attention branch (s1, sc1, g1) and for the MLP\n        # branch (s2, sc2, g2). The gates start at zero, so at initialisation the block returns x unchanged.\n        s1, sc1, g1, s2, sc2, g2 = self.ada(c).unsqueeze(1).chunk(6, dim=-1)      # each (B, 1, d)\n        h = self.norm1(x) * (1 + sc1) + s1\n        h, _ = self.attn(h, h, h, key_padding_mask=key_padding_mask, need_weights=False)\n        x = x + g1 * h\n        h = self.norm2(x) * (1 + sc2) + s2\n        return x + g2 * self.mlp(h)\n\n\nclass LandmarkDiT(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"Denoiser f(x_t, t, word, duration). x_t (B, T, C), t (B,) int, ids (B,) int, mask (B, T) bool (True = real frame),\n    dur (B,) standardised log-duration (NaN = unknown) or None = the model is not conditioned on the duration.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, in_channels: int, num_tokens: int, d_model: int = 256, depth: int = 6, n_heads: int = 4,\n                 mlp_ratio: float = 4.0, dropout: float = 0.0, text_table: Optional[torch.Tensor] = None):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.d_model = d_model\n        self.in_proj = nn.Linear(in_channels, d_model)\n        self.time_mlp = nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(d_model, d_model), nn.SiLU(), nn.Linear(d_model, d_model))\n        self.cond = ConditionEncoder(num_tokens, d_model, text_table)\n        self.dur_mlp = nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(d_model, d_model), nn.SiLU(), nn.Linear(d_model, d_model))   # duration -> vector\n        self.dur_null = nn.Parameter(torch.zeros(d_model))                                                  # \"duration unknown\"\n        self.blocks = nn.ModuleList([DiTBlock(d_model, n_heads, mlp_ratio, dropout) for _ in range(depth)])\n        self.final_norm = nn.LayerNorm(d_model, elementwise_affine=False, eps=1e-6)\n        self.final_ada = nn.Sequential(nn.SiLU(), nn.Linear(d_model, 2 * d_model))\n        self.out_proj = nn.Linear(d_model, in_channels)\n        for m in (self.final_ada[-1], self.out_proj, self.dur_mlp[-1]):    # zero-init outputs -> the model starts by predicting 0\n            nn.init.zeros_(m.weight)\n            nn.init.zeros_(m.bias)\n\n    def forward(self, x: torch.Tensor, t: torch.Tensor, ids: torch.Tensor, mask: Optional[torch.Tensor] = None,\n                dur: Optional[torch.Tensor] = None) -> torch.Tensor:\n        T = x.shape[1]\n        pos = sinusoidal_embedding(torch.arange(T, device=x.device), self.d_model)      # (T, d) frame positions\n        h = self.in_proj(x) + pos.to(x.dtype)\n        c = self.time_mlp(sinusoidal_embedding(t, self.d_model)) + self.cond(ids)       # (B, d) step + word\n        if dur is not None:                                    # + duration (a learned vector where it is NaN = hidden)\n            emb = self.dur_mlp(sinusoidal_embedding(torch.nan_to_num(dur) * 100.0, self.d_model))   # x100: spreads the ~N(0,1) value over the frequencies\n            c = c + torch.where(torch.isnan(dur).unsqueeze(-1), self.dur_null.expand_as(emb), emb)\n        kpm = None if mask is None else ~mask                  # attention ignores keys where kpm is True\n        for blk in self.blocks:\n            h = blk(h, c, kpm)\n        shift, scale = self.final_ada(c).unsqueeze(1).chunk(2, dim=-1)\n        return self.out_proj(self.final_norm(h) * (1 + scale) + shift)\n\n\ndef build_model(cfg: Config, in_channels: int, num_tokens: int, text_table: Optional[torch.Tensor] = None) -> LandmarkDiT:\n    return LandmarkDiT(in_channels, num_tokens, cfg.d_model, cfg.depth, cfg.n_heads, cfg.mlp_ratio, cfg.dropout, text_table)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-17T22:57:32.647183Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-17T22:57:32.64782Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-17T22:57:32.677752Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-17T22:57:32.64775Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-17T22:57:32.676604Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":13},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Gaussian diffusion: training loss + DDIM sampler with classifier-free guidance\ndef cosine_betas(n: int, s: float = 0.008) -> torch.Tensor:\n    \"\"\"Cosine schedule (Nichol & Dhariwal): abar_t = cos²(...) decreases smoothly from 1 (clean) to ~0 (pure noise).\"\"\"\n    steps = torch.arange(n + 1, dtype=torch.float64) / n\n    abar = torch.cos((steps + s) / (1 + s) * math.pi / 2) ** 2\n    abar = abar / abar[0]\n    return (1 - abar[1:] / abar[:-1]).clamp(1e-5, 0.999).float()\n\n\nclass GaussianDiffusion(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"Notation: abar_t = share of signal left at step t.  x_t = sqrt(abar_t) * x0 + sqrt(1 - abar_t) * noise.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, num_steps: int = 1000, prediction_type: str = \"v\"):\n        super().__init__()\n        assert prediction_type in (\"eps\", \"x0\", \"v\")\n        self.num_steps, self.prediction_type = num_steps, prediction_type\n        self.register_buffer(\"abar\", torch.cumprod(1.0 - cosine_betas(num_steps), dim=0))\n\n    def _coefs(self, t: torch.Tensor) -> Tuple[torch.Tensor, torch.Tensor]:\n        \"\"\"(sqrt(abar_t), sqrt(1 - abar_t)) shaped (B, 1, 1) to broadcast over (B, T, C).\"\"\"\n        ab = self.abar[t].view(-1, 1, 1)\n        return ab.sqrt(), (1 - ab).sqrt()\n\n    def q_sample(self, x0, t, noise):\n        sa, sn = self._coefs(t)\n        return sa * x0 + sn * noise\n\n    def target(self, x0, noise, t):\n        \"\"\"What the network is trained to output.\"\"\"\n        if self.prediction_type == \"eps\":\n            return noise\n        if self.prediction_type == \"x0\":\n            return x0\n        sa, sn = self._coefs(t)\n        return sa * noise - sn * x0               # v-prediction (Salimans & Ho)\n\n    def to_x0(self, xt, t, out):\n        \"\"\"Turn the network output back into an estimate of the clean clip x0.\"\"\"\n        sa, sn = self._coefs(t)\n        if self.prediction_type == \"eps\":\n            return (xt - sn * out) / sa\n        if self.prediction_type == \"x0\":\n            return out\n        return sa * xt - sn * out\n\n    def training_loss(self, model, x0, ids, mask=None, p_uncond: float = 0.1, generator=None, weight=None, dur=None,\n                      p_dur_drop: float = 0.0):\n        B, dev = x0.shape[0], x0.device\n        t = torch.randint(0, self.num_steps, (B,), device=dev, generator=generator)    # one random noise level per clip\n        noise = torch.randn(x0.shape, device=dev, dtype=x0.dtype, generator=generator)\n        if p_uncond > 0:                                   # classifier-free guidance: sometimes hide the word\n            drop = torch.rand(B, device=dev, generator=generator) < p_uncond\n            ids = torch.where(drop, torch.zeros_like(ids), ids)\n            if dur is not None:                            # an unconditional sample knows neither the word nor the duration\n                dur = torch.where(drop, torch.full_like(dur, float(\"nan\")), dur)\n        if dur is not None and p_dur_drop > 0:             # sometimes hide ONLY the duration (NaN = unknown)\n            dur = torch.where(torch.rand(B, device=dev, generator=generator) < p_dur_drop, torch.full_like(dur, float(\"nan\")), dur)\n        pred = model(self.q_sample(x0, t, noise), t, ids, mask, dur)\n        se = (pred.float() - self.target(x0, noise, t).float()) ** 2                       # (B, T, C)\n        # weight 0 = ignore: padded frames and hands that were not detected; weight 1 = normal coordinate\n        w = torch.ones_like(se) if weight is None else weight\n        if mask is not None:\n            w = w * mask.unsqueeze(-1).float()\n        return (se * w).sum() / w.sum().clamp(min=1.0)\n\n    @torch.no_grad()\n    def ddim_sample(self, model, ids, num_frames: int, channels: int, mask=None, steps: int = 50, guidance: float = 2.0,\n                    clip_x0: Optional[float] = 5.0, generator=None, dur=None) -> torch.Tensor:\n        \"\"\"Deterministic DDIM (eta = 0). guidance = 1: plain conditional model; > 1: follow the word more strongly.\"\"\"\n        model.eval()\n        B, dev = ids.shape[0], ids.device\n        x = torch.randn(B, num_frames, channels, device=dev, generator=generator)\n        ts = torch.linspace(self.num_steps - 1, 0, steps, device=dev).round().long()   # e.g. 999, 979, ..., 0\n        null = torch.zeros_like(ids)\n        for i, t in enumerate(ts):\n            tt = t.expand(B)\n            if guidance == 1.0:\n                out = model(x, tt, ids, mask, dur)\n            else:\n                # one batched pass for the conditional and the unconditional prediction\n                # (the unconditional branch has neither the word nor the duration)\n                both = model(torch.cat([x, x]), torch.cat([tt, tt]), torch.cat([ids, null]),\n                             None if mask is None else torch.cat([mask, mask]),\n                             None if dur is None else torch.cat([dur, torch.full_like(dur, float(\"nan\"))]))\n                out_c, out_u = both.chunk(2)\n                out = out_u + guidance * (out_c - out_u)     # move `guidance` times further towards the word\n            x0 = self.to_x0(x, tt, out)                      # current guess of the clean clip\n            if clip_x0 is not None:\n                x0 = x0.clamp(-clip_x0, clip_x0)             # keeps the guess in the data range (stabilises sampling)\n            ab = self.abar[t]\n            eps = (x - ab.sqrt() * x0) / (1 - ab).sqrt().clamp(min=1e-8)    # noise implied by (x_t, x0 guess)\n            ab_next = self.abar[ts[i + 1]] if i + 1 < len(ts) else torch.ones((), device=dev)\n            # DDIM step: rebuild x at the next (less noisy) level from the x0 guess and the same noise direction\n            x = ab_next.sqrt() * x0 + (1 - ab_next).sqrt() * eps\n        if mask is not None:\n            x = x * mask.unsqueeze(-1)\n        return x","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-17T22:57:32.679085Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-17T22:57:32.679613Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-17T22:57:32.718669Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-17T22:57:32.679579Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-17T22:57:32.717577Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":14},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# EMA, loss evaluation and the model bundle (one file with weights + config + vocab + normalisation stats)\nclass EMA:\n    \"\"\"Exponential moving average of the weights (much better samples than the raw weights).\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, model: nn.Module, decay: float = 0.999):\n        self.module = copy.deepcopy(model).eval().requires_grad_(False)\n        self.decay = decay\n        self.num_updates = 0\n\n    @torch.no_grad()\n    def update(self, model: nn.Module):\n        # Warm-up: with a fixed decay of 0.999 the average would stay near the random initial weights for ~1000 steps.\n        # min(decay, (1 + n) / (10 + n)) follows the model quickly at first and reaches the full decay later.\n        self.num_updates += 1\n        d = min(self.decay, (1 + self.num_updates) / (10 + self.num_updates))\n        for pe, p in zip(self.module.parameters(), model.parameters()):\n            pe.lerp_(p.detach(), 1.0 - d)\n        for be, b in zip(self.module.buffers(), model.buffers()):\n            be.copy_(b)\n\n\n@torch.no_grad()\ndef evaluate(model, diffusion, loader, device, use_duration: bool = True) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Conditional denoising loss with FIXED noise and noise levels, so values are comparable between epochs and splits.\"\"\"\n    model.eval()\n    gen = torch.Generator(device=device).manual_seed(123)\n    tot, n = 0.0, 0\n    for b in loader:\n        x, m, ids = b[\"landmarks\"].to(device), b[\"mask\"].to(device), b[\"token_id\"].to(device)\n        w = loader.dataset.weights(b[\"present\"].to(device))\n        dur = b[\"dur\"].to(device) if use_duration else None\n        tot += diffusion.training_loss(model, x, ids, m, p_uncond=0.0, generator=gen, weight=w, dur=dur).item() * len(x)\n        n += len(x)\n    return tot / max(n, 1)\n\n\ndef save_bundle(path, model: nn.Module, cfg: Config, vocab: SignVocab, stats, num_frames: int, dur_prior: DurationPrior,\n                epoch: Optional[int] = None, val_loss: Optional[float] = None) -> None:\n    mean, std = stats\n    torch.save({\"state\": {k: v.detach().cpu() for k, v in model.state_dict().items()},\n                \"cfg\": asdict(cfg), \"vocab\": vocab.itos,\n                \"stats_mean\": torch.as_tensor(np.asarray(mean, np.float32)), \"stats_std\": float(std),\n                \"in_channels\": model.in_proj.in_features, \"num_frames\": int(num_frames), \"dur_prior\": dur_prior.to_dict(),\n                \"epoch\": epoch, \"val_loss\": val_loss}, path)\n\n\ndef load_bundle(path, device: str = \"cpu\"):\n    \"\"\"-> (model, diffusion, vocab, (mean, std), cfg, num_frames, dur_prior), ready for `generate(...)` / `sample_ids(...)`.\"\"\"\n    b = torch.load(path, map_location=\"cpu\", weights_only=True)      # load on CPU, move the model afterwards\n    cfg = Config(**b[\"cfg\"])\n    assert cfg.face_preset == FACE_PRESET, f\"the bundle was trained with face_preset={cfg.face_preset!r}: set FACE_PRESET to it and re-run the first cells\"\n    vocab = SignVocab.from_itos(b[\"vocab\"])\n    table = b[\"state\"].get(\"cond.table\")                               # only present if a text-embedding table was used\n    model = build_model(cfg, b[\"in_channels\"], len(vocab), table)\n    model.load_state_dict(b[\"state\"])\n    model.to(device).eval()\n    diffusion = GaussianDiffusion(cfg.diffusion_steps, cfg.prediction_type).to(device)\n    return (model, diffusion, vocab, (b[\"stats_mean\"].numpy(), b[\"stats_std\"]), cfg, b[\"num_frames\"],\n            DurationPrior.from_dict(b[\"dur_prior\"]))","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-17T22:57:32.720128Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-17T22:57:32.720585Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-17T22:57:32.7437Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-17T22:57:32.720563Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-17T22:57:32.74263Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":15},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### ▶ Build the model\nInstantiates the denoiser and the diffusion process, checks the shapes on a real batch, prints the starting loss\n(about 1.0 because the output layer is zero-initialised) and plots the noise schedule.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"model = build_model(cfg, C, len(vocab))\ndiffusion = GaussianDiffusion(cfg.diffusion_steps, cfg.prediction_type)\nprint(f\"model parameters: {sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters()) / 1e6:.2f} M | clip shape (T, C) = ({T}, {C})\")\n\nwith torch.no_grad():\n    t = torch.randint(0, cfg.diffusion_steps, (4,))\n    out = model(batch[\"landmarks\"][:4], t, batch[\"token_id\"][:4], batch[\"mask\"][:4], batch[\"dur\"][:4] if cfg.use_duration else None)\n    loss0 = diffusion.training_loss(model, batch[\"landmarks\"], batch[\"token_id\"], batch[\"mask\"], cfg.p_uncond,\n                                    weight=datasets[\"train\"].weights(batch[\"present\"]),\n                                    dur=batch[\"dur\"] if cfg.use_duration else None, p_dur_drop=cfg.p_dur_drop)\nprint(\"model output shape:\", tuple(out.shape), \"| initial loss:\", round(loss0.item(), 4))\n\nplt.figure(figsize=(5, 2.8))\nplt.plot(diffusion.abar.sqrt().numpy(), label=\"signal  sqrt(abar_t)\")\nplt.plot((1 - diffusion.abar).sqrt().numpy(), label=\"noise   sqrt(1-abar_t)\")\nplt.xlabel(\"diffusion step t\")\nplt.title(\"cosine noise schedule\")\nplt.legend()\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-17T22:57:32.744789Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-17T22:57:32.745136Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-17T22:57:37.354824Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-17T22:57:32.745114Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-17T22:57:37.354153Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"model parameters: 22.46 M | clip shape (T, C) = (64, 254)\nmodel output shape: (4, 64, 254) | initial loss: 1.0815\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 500x280 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":16},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 5. Sampling helpers\n`sample_ids` generates in batches (fast enough to evaluate every test word); `generate` turns words into landmark sequences\nin shoulder-normalised coordinates.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Sampling helpers\n@torch.no_grad()\ndef sample_ids(model, diffusion, ids: torch.Tensor, num_frames: int, channels: int, steps: int = 50, guidance: float = 2.0,\n               device: str = \"cpu\", batch_size: int = 256, seed: int = 0, dur: Optional[torch.Tensor] = None) -> torch.Tensor:\n    \"\"\"word ids (N,) [+ standardised durations (N,)] -> STANDARDISED generated clips (N, T, C) on the CPU.\"\"\"\n    model, diffusion = model.to(device).eval(), diffusion.to(device)\n    gen = torch.Generator(device=device).manual_seed(seed)\n    return torch.cat([diffusion.ddim_sample(model, ids[i:i + batch_size].to(device), num_frames, channels, None, steps, guidance,\n                                            generator=gen, dur=None if dur is None else dur[i:i + batch_size].to(device)).cpu()\n                      for i in range(0, len(ids), batch_size)])\n\n\ndef destandardise(x: np.ndarray, stats) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Standardised (N, T, C) -> landmark coordinates (N, T, NUM_NODES, D).\"\"\"\n    mean, std = stats\n    return (x * std + mean).reshape(x.shape[0], x.shape[1], NUM_NODES, -1)\n\n\ndef generate(model, diffusion, vocab: SignVocab, words: List[str], stats, num_frames: int, channels: int,\n             dur_prior: Optional[DurationPrior] = None, n_per_word: int = 4, steps: int = 50, guidance: float = 2.0,\n             device: str = \"cpu\", seed: int = 0, duration_s: Optional[float] = None):\n    \"\"\"words -> (clips, seconds): clips {word: (n_per_word, T, NUM_NODES, D)} in shoulder-normalised coordinates and\n    seconds {word: (n_per_word,)} = the duration each clip was generated for.\n\n    dur_prior=None   -> the model is not conditioned on the duration (seconds are NaN).\n    duration_s=None  -> every clip gets a duration drawn from the word's prior (natural variety).\n    duration_s=1.2   -> every clip is generated for 1.2 s.\"\"\"\n    ids_np = np.repeat([vocab.encode(w) for w in words], n_per_word)\n    dur = secs = None\n    if dur_prior is not None:\n        z = dur_prior.sample(ids_np, np.random.default_rng(seed)) if duration_s is None \\\n            else dur_prior.standardise(np.full(len(ids_np), duration_s * dur_prior.fps))\n        dur, secs = torch.tensor(z, dtype=torch.float32), dur_prior.seconds(z)\n    x = destandardise(sample_ids(model, diffusion, torch.from_numpy(ids_np), num_frames, channels, steps, guidance, device,\n                                 seed=seed, dur=dur).numpy(), stats)\n    secs = np.full(len(ids_np), np.nan) if secs is None else secs\n    sl = lambda i: slice(i * n_per_word, (i + 1) * n_per_word)\n    return {w: x[sl(i)] for i, w in enumerate(words)}, {w: secs[sl(i)] for i, w in enumerate(words)}","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-17T22:57:37.355802Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-17T22:57:37.356721Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-17T22:57:37.369574Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-17T22:57:37.356694Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-17T22:57:37.368492Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":17},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 6. Training (with early stopping)\nEach epoch: one pass over the train split (the EMA weights are updated after every step), then the **EMA** model is scored on the\nvalidation signers with *fixed* noise, so the validation curve is smooth and comparable between epochs.\n\nLoss: squared error on the diffusion target, **ignoring the coordinates of a hand / of the face in frames where it was not detected** (those values are only gap-filling, not data); face coordinates are weighted by `face_loss_weight`.\n\nLearning rate: linear warm-up for `warmup_steps`, then cosine decay down to 10 % of `lr`.\nEarly stopping: if the validation loss has not improved by at least `min_delta` for `patience` epochs, training stops and the\nbest EMA weights are restored.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Training loop with early stopping\ndef lr_at(step: int, total_steps: int, cfg: Config) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Linear warm-up, then cosine decay from lr to 0.1 * lr.\"\"\"\n    if step < cfg.warmup_steps:\n        return cfg.lr * (step + 1) / cfg.warmup_steps\n    progress = min(1.0, (step - cfg.warmup_steps) / max(1, total_steps - cfg.warmup_steps))\n    return cfg.lr * (0.1 + 0.9 * 0.5 * (1 + math.cos(math.pi * progress)))\n\n\ndef train_one_epoch(model, ema, diffusion, loader, opt, scaler, cfg: Config, device: str, step: int, total_steps: int):\n    \"\"\"One pass over the train loader. Returns (mean train loss, updated global step).\"\"\"\n    model.train()\n    use_amp = scaler.is_enabled()\n    running = 0.0\n    for b in loader:\n        x, m, ids = b[\"landmarks\"].to(device), b[\"mask\"].to(device), b[\"token_id\"].to(device)\n        w = loader.dataset.weights(b[\"present\"].to(device))\n        dur = b[\"dur\"].to(device) if cfg.use_duration else None\n        for g in opt.param_groups:\n            g[\"lr\"] = lr_at(step, total_steps, cfg)\n        with torch.autocast(device_type=\"cuda\", dtype=torch.float16, enabled=use_amp):\n            loss = diffusion.training_loss(model, x, ids, m, cfg.p_uncond, weight=w, dur=dur, p_dur_drop=cfg.p_dur_drop)\n        opt.zero_grad(set_to_none=True)\n        scaler.scale(loss).backward()          # mixed precision: scale the loss to avoid fp16 underflow ...\n        scaler.unscale_(opt)                   # ... and unscale before clipping the gradients\n        nn.utils.clip_grad_norm_(model.parameters(), cfg.grad_clip)\n        scaler.step(opt)\n        scaler.update()\n        ema.update(model)\n        running += loss.item()\n        step += 1\n    return running / len(loader), step\n\n\ndef train(model, diffusion, loaders: dict, cfg: Config, device: str, vocab: SignVocab, stats, dur_prior: DurationPrior):\n    \"\"\"Train with EMA and early stopping. The best EMA weights are saved to `<work_dir>/ckpt_best.pt` and loaded back\n    into the returned EMA model (so it is the BEST model, not the last one).\n    Returns (ema, history) with history = dict(epoch, train, val, lr, best_epoch, best_val, stopped_early).\"\"\"\n    model, diffusion = model.to(device), diffusion.to(device)\n    ema = EMA(model, cfg.ema_decay)\n    opt = torch.optim.AdamW(model.parameters(), lr=cfg.lr, weight_decay=cfg.weight_decay, betas=(0.9, 0.99))\n    scaler = torch.amp.GradScaler(\"cuda\", enabled=cfg.amp and device.startswith(\"cuda\"))\n    total_steps = cfg.epochs * len(loaders[\"train\"])\n    best_path = Path(cfg.work_dir) / \"ckpt_best.pt\"\n    patience = cfg.patience if cfg.early_stopping else float(\"inf\")\n    min_delta = cfg.min_delta if cfg.early_stopping else 0.0\n\n    hist = {\"epoch\": [], \"train\": [], \"val\": [], \"lr\": [], \"best_epoch\": 0, \"best_val\": float(\"inf\"), \"stopped_early\": False}\n    header = (f\"{'epoch':>9} | {'train':>8} | {'val(EMA)':>8} | {'best val':>8} | {'best ep':>7} | {'lr':>8} | \"\n              f\"{'no-improve':>10} | {'time':>5}\")\n    print(header + \"\\n\" + \"-\" * len(header))\n    step, bad = 0, 0\n    for epoch in range(1, cfg.epochs + 1):\n        t0 = time.time()\n        tr, step = train_one_epoch(model, ema, diffusion, loaders[\"train\"], opt, scaler, cfg, device, step, total_steps)\n        va = evaluate(ema.module, diffusion, loaders[\"val\"], device, cfg.use_duration)\n        for k, v in ((\"epoch\", epoch), (\"train\", tr), (\"val\", va), (\"lr\", opt.param_groups[0][\"lr\"])):\n            hist[k].append(v)\n\n        # Improvement = beats the best loss by more than min_delta. Epochs still inside the LR warm-up never count\n        # towards the patience (the loss is still dropping fast and the EMA is still catching up).\n        improved = va < hist[\"best_val\"] - min_delta\n        if improved:\n            hist[\"best_val\"], hist[\"best_epoch\"], bad = va, epoch, 0\n            save_bundle(best_path, ema.module, cfg, vocab, stats, loaders[\"train\"].dataset.T, dur_prior, epoch, va)\n        elif step >= cfg.warmup_steps:\n            bad += 1\n\n        print(f\"{epoch:>4d}/{cfg.epochs:<4d} | {tr:>8.4f} | {va:>8.4f} | {hist['best_val']:>8.4f} | {hist['best_epoch']:>7d} | \"\n              f\"{hist['lr'][-1]:>8.2e} | {f'{bad}/{patience}':>10} | {time.time() - t0:>4.0f}s\" + (\"  *\" if improved else \"\"))\n        if bad >= patience:\n            hist[\"stopped_early\"] = True\n            print(f\"early stopping: no improvement > {cfg.min_delta} for {cfg.patience} epochs\")\n            break\n\n    ema.module.load_state_dict(torch.load(best_path, map_location=device, weights_only=True)[\"state\"])\n    return ema, hist","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-17T22:57:37.370591Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-17T22:57:37.37082Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-17T22:57:37.397456Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-17T22:57:37.370801Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-17T22:57:37.396611Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":18},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### ▶ Train the diffusion model\nOne line per epoch: `train` loss, EMA `val` loss, best validation loss and its epoch, learning rate, early-stopping counter\nand duration. A `*` marks the epochs that improved (and were saved).","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"ema, history = train(model, diffusion, loaders, cfg, device, vocab, stats, dur_prior)\nprint(f\"\\nbest epoch {history['best_epoch']} | best val loss {history['best_val']:.4f} | stopped early: {history['stopped_early']}\")\nprint(\"best model saved to:\", Path(cfg.work_dir) / \"ckpt_best.pt\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-17T22:57:37.398551Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-17T22:57:37.398855Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-18T00:41:47.811315Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-17T22:57: