*, which the model and the classifier never saw. Every test clip is used; a *clean* subset (hands detected in at least `clean_hand_frac` of the frames) is reported next to it, and the nearest-real MPJPE uses the clean clips as references (the hands of the other clips are partly gap-filled).\n\n| metric | question it answers | good when |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Denoising loss** (overall and per signer) | does the denoiser generalise to new signers? | test close to validation |\n| **Recognition accuracy** | does a classifier trained on *real train* clips recognise the word of each *generated* clip? | close to the accuracy on real test clips |\n| **Fréchet distance (FD)** | are generated clips distributed like real ones (quality + diversity)? Computed on classifier embeddings, like FID | close to the real-train vs real-test \"floor\" |\n| **Nearest-real MPJPE** | mean joint error (shoulder widths) between a generated clip and the closest real test clip of the *same* word, vs of *other* words, vs real-vs-real | same-word clearly below other-word, close to real-vs-real |","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Denoising loss on a subset of clips, per signer\ndef loss_per_signer(model, diffusion, data: dict, split: str, cfg: Config, device: str) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    \"\"\"Denoising loss of every signer of `split`: shows whether some new signers are much harder than others.\"\"\"\n    rows = []\n    for pid, df in data[\"splits\"][split].groupby(\"participant_id\"):\n        ds = ASLLandmarkDataset(df, data[\"cache_path\"], data[\"vocab\"], data[\"stats\"], data[\"dur_prior\"], cfg.use_z,\n                                face_w=cfg.face_loss_weight)\n        loss = evaluate(model, diffusion, DataLoader(ds, batch_size=cfg.batch_size), device, cfg.use_duration)\n        rows.append(dict(split=split, participant_id=int(pid), clips=len(ds), loss=loss))\n    return pd.DataFrame(rows)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-18T00:41:50.020846Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-18T00:41:50.021192Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-18T00:41:50.02714Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-18T00:41:50.021152Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-18T00:41:50.026342Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":22},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### ▶ Denoising loss: validation vs test signers","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"val_loss = evaluate(ema.module, diffusion, loaders[\"val\"], device, cfg.use_duration)\ntest_loss = evaluate(ema.module, diffusion, loaders[\"test\"], device, cfg.use_duration)\nprint(f\"validation loss (val signers) : {val_loss:.4f}\")\nprint(f\"TEST loss (test signers)      : {test_loss:.4f}   ({100 * (test_loss / val_loss - 1):+.1f} % vs validation)\")\n\nper_signer_loss = pd.concat([loss_per_signer(ema.module, diffusion, data, s, cfg, device) for s in (\"val\", \"test\")])\ndisplay(per_signer_loss)\nax = per_signer_loss.plot.bar(x=\"participant_id\", y=\"loss\", figsize=(6, 2.8), legend=False,\n                              color=per_signer_loss[\"split\"].map({\"val\": \"tab:green\", \"test\": \"tab:blue\"}).tolist(),\n                              title=\"denoising loss per signer (green = val, blue = test)\")\nax.set_ylabel(\"loss\")\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-18T00:41:50.028913Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-18T00:41:50.029216Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-18T00:42:32.25338Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-18T00:41:50.029195Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-18T00:42:32.252232Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"validation loss (val signers) : 0.0569\nTEST loss (test signers)      : 0.0488   (-14.2 % vs validation)\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"  split  participant_id  clips      loss\n0   val           34503   4545  0.065827\n1   val           61333   4894  0.050934\n0  test           22343   4674  0.051407\n1  test           32319   4749  0.060217\n2  test           36257   4888  0.048467\n3  test           62590   4563  0.042188","text/html":"<div>\n<style scoped>\n    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n        vertical-align: middle;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n        vertical-align: top;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe thead th {\n        text-align: right;\n    }\n</style>\n<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n  <thead>\n    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n      <th></th>\n      <th>split</th>\n      <th>participant_id</th>\n      <th>clips</th>\n      <th>loss</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <th>0</th>\n      <td>val</td>\n      <td>34503</td>\n      <td>4545</td>\n      <td>0.065827</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>1</th>\n      <td>val</td>\n      <td>61333</td>\n      <td>4894</td>\n      <td>0.050934</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>0</th>\n      <td>test</td>\n      <td>22343</td>\n      <td>4674</td>\n      <td>0.051407</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>1</th>\n      <td>test</td>\n      <td>32319</td>\n      <td>4749</td>\n      <td>0.060217</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>2</th>\n      <td>test</td>\n      <td>36257</td>\n      <td>4888</td>\n      <td>0.048467</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>3</th>\n      <td>test</td>\n      <td>62590</td>\n      <td>4563</td>\n      <td>0.042188</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n</div>"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 600x280 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":23},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Recognition classifier (the \"judge\" for generated clips)\nclass SignClassifier(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"Small 1-D conv net over (T, C) clips (positions + frame-to-frame velocity) -> sign logits.\n    `features()` returns the clip embedding used for the Fréchet distance.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, in_channels: int, num_classes: int, hidden: int = 256, embed_dim: int = 128, dropout: float = 0.3):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.convs = nn.Sequential(\n            nn.Conv1d(2 * in_channels, hidden, 5, padding=2), nn.BatchNorm1d(hidden), nn.GELU(),\n            nn.Conv1d(hidden, hidden, 5, padding=2), nn.BatchNorm1d(hidden), nn.GELU(),\n            nn.Conv1d(hidden, hidden, 5, padding=2), nn.BatchNorm1d(hidden), nn.GELU())\n        self.embed = nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(2 * hidden, embed_dim), nn.GELU())\n        self.drop, self.head = nn.Dropout(dropout), nn.Linear(embed_dim, num_classes)\n\n    def features(self, x: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n        x = torch.cat([x, torch.diff(x, dim=1, prepend=x[:, :1])], dim=-1)    # positions + velocity: (B, T, 2C)\n        h = self.convs(x.transpose(1, 2))                                      # Conv1d expects (B, channels, T)\n        return self.embed(torch.cat([h.mean(2), h.amax(2)], dim=1))            # mean + max over time -> one vector per clip\n\n    def forward(self, x: torch.Tensor, mask: Optional[torch.Tensor] = None) -> torch.Tensor:\n        return self.head(self.drop(self.features(x)))\n\n\n@torch.no_grad()\ndef predict(clf: SignClassifier, x: torch.Tensor, device: str, batch_size: int = 512, features: bool = False) -> torch.Tensor:\n    \"\"\"Logits (or embeddings if features=True) for standardised clips x (N, T, C), returned on the CPU.\"\"\"\n    clf.eval()\n    fn = clf.features if features else clf\n    return torch.cat([fn(x[i:i + batch_size].to(device)).cpu() for i in range(0, len(x), batch_size)])\n\n\ndef topk_accuracy(logits: torch.Tensor, y: torch.Tensor) -> Tuple[float, float]:\n    top5 = logits.topk(min(5, logits.shape[1]), dim=1).indices\n    return (top5[:, 0] == y).float().mean().item(), (top5 == y[:, None]).any(1).float().mean().item()\n\n\ndef dataset_arrays(ds: ASLLandmarkDataset, max_n: Optional[int] = None, seed: int = 0, clean_thr: float = 0.5):\n    \"\"\"Read a whole dataset from the cache -> standardised clips (N, T, C), labels (word id - 1) and a (N,) bool mask of the\n    'clean' clips (hands detected in >= clean_thr of the frames).\"\"\"\n    idx = np.arange(len(ds))\n    if max_n and len(ds) > max_n:\n        idx = np.sort(np.random.default_rng(seed).choice(len(ds), max_n, replace=False))\n    raw = ds.load_raw(ds.cache_idx[idx])\n    clean = ds.meta[\"hand_frac\"].to_numpy()[idx] >= clean_thr\n    return torch.from_numpy((raw - ds.mean) / ds.std), torch.from_numpy(ds.token_ids[idx] - 1), torch.from_numpy(clean)\n\n\ndef train_classifier(loaders: dict, in_channels: int, num_classes: int, cfg: Config, device: str):\n    \"\"\"Train on REAL train clips; keep the epoch with the best accuracy on the validation signers. Labels = word id - 1.\"\"\"\n    clf = SignClassifier(in_channels, num_classes, cfg.clf_hidden, cfg.clf_embed_dim).to(device)\n    opt = torch.optim.AdamW(clf.parameters(), lr=2e-3, weight_decay=1e-2)\n    sched = torch.optim.lr_scheduler.OneCycleLR(opt, max_lr=2e-3, total_steps=cfg.clf_epochs * len(loaders[\"train\"]),\n                                                pct_start=0.15)\n    x_val, y_val, _ = dataset_arrays(loaders[\"val\"].dataset)\n    best, bad, best_state, hist = -1.0, 0, None, []\n    print(f\"{'epoch':>5} | {'val top-1':>9}\\n\" + \"-\" * 17)\n    for epoch in range(1, cfg.clf_epochs + 1):\n        clf.train()\n        for b in loaders[\"train\"]:\n            x, y = b[\"landmarks\"].to(device), b[\"token_id\"].to(device) - 1\n            loss = F.cross_entropy(clf(x), y, label_smoothing=0.1)\n            opt.zero_grad(set_to_none=True)\n            loss.backward()\n            nn.utils.clip_grad_norm_(clf.parameters(), 1.0)\n            opt.step()\n            sched.step()\n        acc = topk_accuracy(predict(clf, x_val, device), y_val)[0]\n        hist.append(acc)\n        improved = acc > best + 1e-4\n        print(f\"{epoch:>5d} | {acc:>9.3f}\" + (\"  *\" if improved else \"\"))\n        if improved:\n            best, bad, best_state = acc, 0, copy.deepcopy(clf.state_dict())\n        else:\n            bad += 1\n            if bad >= cfg.clf_patience:\n                break\n    clf.load_state_dict(best_state)\n    torch.save(clf.state_dict(), Path(cfg.work_dir) / \"classifier_best.pt\")\n    return clf.eval(), hist","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-18T00:42:32.255652Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-18T00:42:32.255976Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-18T00:42:32.274562Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-18T00:42:32.25594Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-18T00:42:32.273862Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":24},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### ▶ Train the recognition classifier on real train clips\nEarly-stopped on the validation signers. Its accuracy on the **real test clips** is the upper bound for the generated clips.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"clf, clf_hist = train_classifier(loaders, C, len(vocab) - 1, cfg, device)\nx_val, y_val, _ = dataset_arrays(datasets[\"val\"])\nx_test, y_test, clean_test = dataset_arrays(datasets[\"test\"], clean_thr=cfg.clean_hand_frac)\nclf_val, clf_test = topk_accuracy(predict(clf, x_val, device), y_val), topk_accuracy(predict(clf, x_test, device), y_test)\nclf_test_clean = topk_accuracy(predict(clf, x_test[clean_test], device), y_test[clean_test])\nprint(f\"classifier on REAL clips  | val top-1 {clf_val[0]:.3f}  top-5 {clf_val[1]:.3f} | \"\n      f\"TEST top-1 {clf_test[0]:.3f}  top-5 {clf_test[1]:.3f} | TEST clean subset top-1 {clf_test_clean[0]:.3f}\")\n\nplt.figure(figsize=(5, 2.8))\nplt.plot(range(1, len(clf_hist) + 1), clf_hist, marker=\"o\")\nplt.xlabel(\"epoch\")\nplt.ylabel(\"val top-1\")\nplt.title(\"recognition classifier (real clips)\")\nplt.grid(alpha=0.3)\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-18T00:42:32.275394Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-18T00:42:32.275712Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-18T00:48:56.172404Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-18T00:42:32.275678Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-18T00:48:56.171751Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"epoch | val top-1\n-----------------\n    1 |     0.073  *\n    2 |     0.149  *\n    3 |     0.167  *\n    4 |     0.242  *\n    5 |     0.284  *\n    6 |     0.376  *\n    7 |     0.392  *\n    8 |     0.346\n    9 |     0.423  *\n   10 |     0.406\n   11 |     0.477  *\n   12 |     0.509  *\n   13 |     0.487\n   14 |     0.503\n   15 |     0.489\n   16 |     0.535  *\n   17 |     0.525\n   18 |     0.533\n   19 |     0.508\n   20 |     0.498\nclassifier on REAL clips  | val top-1 0.535  top-5 0.775 | TEST top-1 0.522  top-5 0.781 | TEST clean subset top-1 0.566\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 500x280 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":25},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Generation metrics\ndef frechet_distance(f1: np.ndarray, f2: np.ndarray) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Fréchet distance between Gaussians fitted to two feature sets (N1, D) and (N2, D):\n        FD = |mu1 - mu2|² + Tr(S1 + S2 - 2 (S1 S2)^½)\n    It compares whole distributions (quality AND diversity), exactly like FID for images.\"\"\"\n    f1, f2 = f1.astype(np.float64), f2.astype(np.float64)\n    mu1, mu2 = f1.mean(0), f2.mean(0)\n    s1, s2 = np.cov(f1, rowvar=False), np.cov(f2, rowvar=False)\n    # Tr((S1 S2)^½) = sum of the square roots of the eigenvalues of S1 S2 (avoids scipy.linalg.sqrtm)\n    tr_sqrt = np.sqrt(np.clip(np.linalg.eigvals(s1 @ s2).real, 0.0, None)).sum()\n    return float(((mu1 - mu2) ** 2).sum() + np.trace(s1) + np.trace(s2) - 2.0 * tr_sqrt)\n\n\n@torch.no_grad()\ndef nearest_mpjpe(queries: torch.Tensor, refs: torch.Tensor) -> Tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n    \"\"\"For every query clip, find the closest reference clip.\n    queries (Q, T, N, D), refs (M, T, N, D) -> (mean joint error to the nearest ref (Q,), per-joint error (Q, N)).\"\"\"\n    errs, per_joint = [], []\n    for q in queries:\n        pj = (refs - q).norm(dim=-1).mean(dim=1)       # (M, N): error of every joint vs every ref, averaged over time\n        j = pj.mean(dim=1).argmin()                     # nearest reference clip\n        errs.append(pj[j].mean().item())\n        per_joint.append(pj[j].cpu().numpy())\n    return np.array(errs), np.stack(per_joint)\n\n\ndef mpjpe_metrics(real: torch.Tensor, real_y: torch.Tensor, gen: torch.Tensor, gen_y: torch.Tensor, words: List[int],\n                  n_query: int, n_other: int = 3, seed: int = 0) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Nearest-real joint errors, word by word.\n\n    For a word w, its first `n_query` real clips are held out as \"real queries\"; the remaining real clips of w form the\n    reference pool. Then:\n        own   = generated clips of w -> nearest clip in the pool               (should be small)\n        other = generated clips of w -> nearest real clip of another word      (averaged over n_other random words)\n        rr    = real queries of w    -> nearest clip in the pool               (real-vs-real baseline, same pool)\"\"\"\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    words = [w for w in words if (real_y == w).any()]  # a word needs at least one real reference clip\n    own, other, rr, per_joint = [], [], [], []\n    for w in words:\n        real_w, gen_w = real[real_y == w], gen[gen_y == w]\n        n_q = min(n_query, len(real_w) - 1)             # always keep at least one clip in the pool\n        pool = real_w[n_q:]\n        e, pj = nearest_mpjpe(gen_w, pool)\n        own.append(e)\n        per_joint.append(pj)\n        if n_q > 0:\n            rr.append(nearest_mpjpe(real_w[:n_q], pool)[0])\n        others = rng.choice([o for o in words if o != w], size=min(n_other, len(words) - 1), replace=False)\n        if len(others):\n            other.append(np.mean([nearest_mpjpe(gen_w, real[real_y == int(o)])[0] for o in others], axis=0))\n    per_joint = np.concatenate(per_joint)\n    groups = PART_GROUPS                                # left_hand, right_hand, arms, lips, brows, eyes, nose + contour\n    return {\"mpjpe_gen_to_nearest_real_same_word\": float(np.concatenate(own).mean()),\n            \"mpjpe_gen_to_nearest_real_other_word\": float(np.concatenate(other).mean()) if other else None,\n            \"mpjpe_real_to_nearest_real_same_word\": float(np.concatenate(rr).mean()) if rr else None,\n            \"mpjpe_per_group_same_word\": {g: float(per_joint[:, sl].mean()) for g, sl in groups.items()}}\n\n\n@torch.no_grad()\ndef evaluate_generation(ema_model, diffusion, clf, data: dict, cfg: Config, device: str, seed: int = 0):\n    \"\"\"Generate `cfg.gen_per_word` clips per test word, then compute recognition, FD and MPJPE on the test split.\"\"\"\n    vocab, stats = data[\"vocab\"], data[\"stats\"]\n    ds_test = data[\"datasets\"][\"test\"]\n    x_test, y_test, clean = dataset_arrays(ds_test, clean_thr=cfg.clean_hand_frac)\n    d_test = torch.from_numpy(ds_test.dur)                  # standardised log-duration of every real test clip (same order)\n    words = sorted(set(y_test.tolist()))\n    if cfg.eval_max_words:\n        words = sorted(np.random.default_rng(seed).choice(words, min(cfg.eval_max_words, len(words)), replace=False).tolist())\n        keep = torch.isin(y_test, torch.tensor(words))\n        x_test, y_test, clean, d_test = x_test[keep], y_test[keep], clean[keep], d_test[keep]\n\n    # 1) generation: gen_per_word clips for every test word\n    gen_y = torch.tensor(words).repeat_interleave(cfg.gen_per_word)\n    t0 = time.time()\n    # durations: drawn from each word's prior, exactly what a user who only gives a word would get\n    dur = None\n    if cfg.use_duration:\n        dur = torch.tensor(data[\"dur_prior\"].sample((gen_y + 1).numpy(), np.random.default_rng(seed)), dtype=torch.float32)\n    x_gen = sample_ids(ema_model, diffusion, gen_y + 1, ds_test.T, ds_test.C, cfg.gen_steps, cfg.guidance, device, seed=seed, dur=dur)\n    print(f\"generated {len(x_gen)} clips for {len(words)} words in {time.time() - t0:.0f}s\")\n\n    # 2) recognition: real test clips (upper bound) vs generated clips\n    real_top1, real_top5 = topk_accuracy(predict(clf, x_test, device), y_test)\n    real_top1_c, real_top5_c = topk_accuracy(predict(clf, x_test[clean], device), y_test[clean])    # clean subset only\n    gen_logits = predict(clf, x_gen, device)\n    gen_top1, gen_top5 = topk_accuracy(gen_logits, gen_y)\n    per_word = (pd.DataFrame({\"word\": [vocab.decode(int(w) + 1) for w in gen_y], \"correct\": (gen_logits.argmax(1) == gen_y).numpy()})\n                .groupby(\"word\")[\"correct\"].mean().rename(\"gen_top1\").reset_index())\n\n    # 3) Fréchet distance on classifier embeddings; the floor compares two REAL sets (train vs test signers)\n    f_real = predict(clf, x_test, device, features=True).numpy()\n    f_gen = predict(clf, x_gen, device, features=True).numpy()\n    x_tr, _, clean_tr = dataset_arrays(data[\"datasets\"][\"train\"], max_n=len(x_test), clean_thr=cfg.clean_hand_frac)\n    f_train = predict(clf, x_tr, device, features=True).numpy()\n    c_te, c_tr = clean.numpy(), clean_tr.numpy()\n\n    # 4) nearest-real MPJPE in landmark coordinates (shoulder widths), references = CLEAN real clips only\n    x_ref, y_ref = x_test[clean], y_test[clean]\n    real_seq = torch.from_numpy(destandardise(x_ref.numpy(), stats)).float().to(device)\n    gen_seq = torch.from_numpy(destandardise(x_gen.numpy(), stats)).float().to(device)\n    mpjpe = mpjpe_metrics(real_seq, y_ref.to(device), gen_seq, gen_y.to(device), words, cfg.gen_per_word, seed=seed)\n\n    results = {\"n_words\": len(words), \"n_generated\": len(x_gen), \"n_real_test\": len(x_test), \"n_real_test_clean\": int(clean.sum()),\n               \"guidance\": cfg.guidance, \"ddim_steps\": cfg.gen_steps, \"use_z\": cfg.use_z, \"use_duration\": cfg.use_duration,\n               \"face_preset\": cfg.face_preset,\n               \"recognition_top1_generated\": gen_top1, \"recognition_top5_generated\": gen_top5,\n               \"recognition_top1_real_test\": real_top1, \"recognition_top5_real_test\": real_top5,\n               \"recognition_top1_real_test_clean\": real_top1_c, \"recognition_top5_real_test_clean\": real_top5_c,\n               \"frechet_distance_gen_vs_real_test\": frechet_distance(f_real, f_gen),\n               \"frechet_distance_floor_real_train_vs_real_test\": frechet_distance(f_train, f_real),\n               \"frechet_distance_gen_vs_real_test_clean\": frechet_distance(f_real[c_te], f_gen),\n               \"frechet_distance_floor_clean\": frechet_distance(f_train[c_tr], f_real[c_te]),\n               **mpjpe}\n    per_word.to_csv(Path(cfg.work_dir) / \"per_word_generated_accuracy.csv\", index=False)\n    arrays = dict(real_seq=real_seq.cpu().numpy(), real_labels=y_ref.numpy(), real_dur_z=d_test[clean].numpy(), gen_seq=gen_seq.cpu().numpy(),\n                  gen_labels=gen_y.numpy(), words=words, per_word=per_word,\n                  gen_seconds=None if dur is None else data[\"dur_prior\"].seconds(dur.numpy()))\n    return results, arrays","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-18T00:48:56.173644Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-18T00:48:56.173962Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-18T00:48:56.20217Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-18T00:48:56.173928Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-18T00:48:56.201378Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":26},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### ▶ Evaluate the generated motion on the test split","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"results, arrs = evaluate_generation(ema.module, diffusion, clf, data, cfg, device)\nresults.update(val_denoising_loss=val_loss, test_denoising_loss=test_loss, best_epoch=history[\"best_epoch\"],\n               stopped_early=history[\"stopped_early\"], classifier_top1_real_val=clf_val[0], classifier_top1_real_test=clf_test[0])\n_ = plot_eval_summary(results, os.path.join(cfg.work_dir, \"eval_summary.png\"))\nplt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy