pe":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1520x760 with 32 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1520x760 with 32 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":30},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 7. Temporal smoothing of the generated motion\n\nA diffusion model samples every frame from noise, so the generated landmarks **jitter** a little from one frame to the next, and\na rendered avatar would tremble. The cure needs **no retraining**: filter the sequence over time.\n\nWe use a **One Euro filter**, the standard choice for hand / body tracking. It is a low-pass filter whose cut-off follows the speed:\nwhen a coordinate is almost still the cut-off is low (`smooth_min_cutoff`) and the jitter disappears, when it moves fast the cut-off\nrises (`+ smooth_beta × speed`) so fast signing is not blurred. The *zero-phase* version used here runs the filter forwards and\nbackwards, which cancels the delay of a single pass (fine for clips that are finished before they are shown).\n\nThe filter needs the real time step, so it uses `fps = T / duration` of the clip (this is why the duration of section 8 matters).\n**The trade-off is real:** any smoothing slightly shrinks the movement (`path_length_ratio` < 1) and can blur very fast, small\nmovements such as finger flicks; the table below lets you choose the strength.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Temporal smoothing: One Euro filter (+ zero-phase version) and jitter metrics\ndef _alpha(cutoff, fps: float):\n    \"\"\"Smoothing factor of a first-order low-pass filter with the given cut-off frequency (Hz) at `fps` samples per second.\"\"\"\n    tau = 1.0 / (2.0 * math.pi * cutoff)\n    return 1.0 / (1.0 + tau * fps)\n\n\ndef one_euro(x: np.ndarray, fps: float, min_cutoff: float = 1.5, beta: float = 3.0, d_cutoff: float = 1.0) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"One Euro filter (Casiez et al., CHI 2012) along the first axis of x (T, ...), every coordinate on its own.\n\n    A low-pass filter whose cut-off adapts to the speed of the signal:\n        * almost still  -> low cut-off  (`min_cutoff`)            -> the small jitter is removed\n        * moving fast   -> high cut-off (min_cutoff + beta*|speed|) -> the filter lags less, the movement is kept\n    It is causal (usable in real time) but it delays the signal slightly; `smooth_sequence` removes that delay.\"\"\"\n    flat = x.reshape(len(x), -1).astype(np.float64)\n    out = np.empty_like(flat)\n    out[0] = flat[0]\n    speed = np.zeros(flat.shape[1])                       # filtered speed (units per second)\n    a_d = _alpha(d_cutoff, fps)\n    for t in range(1, len(flat)):\n        raw_speed = (flat[t] - out[t - 1]) * fps\n        speed = a_d * raw_speed + (1.0 - a_d) * speed\n        a = _alpha(min_cutoff + beta * np.abs(speed), fps)   # one factor per coordinate: fast coordinates are filtered less\n        out[t] = a * flat[t] + (1.0 - a) * out[t - 1]\n    return out.reshape(x.shape)\n\n\ndef smooth_sequence(seq: np.ndarray, fps: float, min_cutoff: float = 1.5, beta: float = 3.0, d_cutoff: float = 1.0,\n                    zero_phase: bool = True) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Smooth ONE clip seq (T, NUM_NODES, D) over time. fps = frames per SECOND of the clip, i.e. T / duration.\n\n    zero_phase=True: filter forwards, then backwards (the second pass cancels the delay of the first). Fine for generated\n    clips, which are complete before they are shown. zero_phase=False: causal, for live streaming.\"\"\"\n    y = one_euro(seq, fps, min_cutoff, beta, d_cutoff)\n    if zero_phase:\n        y = one_euro(y[::-1], fps, min_cutoff, beta, d_cutoff)[::-1]\n    return y.astype(seq.dtype)\n\n\ndef effective_fps(num_frames: int, seconds: float, default_seconds: float = 1.5) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Frames per second of a clip that has `num_frames` frames and lasts `seconds` (NaN/None -> assume `default_seconds`).\"\"\"\n    ok = seconds is not None and np.isfinite(seconds) and seconds > 0\n    return num_frames / (seconds if ok else default_seconds)\n\n\ndef smooth_clips(clips: np.ndarray, seconds, cfg: Config) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"clips (N, T, NUM_NODES, D), seconds (N,) or None -> smoothed copy, using cfg.smooth_* (identity if cfg.smooth is False).\"\"\"\n    if not cfg.smooth:\n        return clips\n    secs = np.full(len(clips), np.nan) if seconds is None else np.asarray(seconds, float)\n    return np.stack([smooth_sequence(c, effective_fps(len(c), s), cfg.smooth_min_cutoff, cfg.smooth_beta, cfg.smooth_d_cutoff)\n                     for c, s in zip(clips, secs)])\n\n\ndef jitter(seqs: np.ndarray) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Roughness of motion = mean length of the 2nd temporal difference (acceleration) in shoulder widths / frame²,\n    per body part. seqs (N, T, NUM_NODES, D). Lower = smoother. A real signer does not jitter, but MediaPipe tracking noise does.\"\"\"\n    acc = np.linalg.norm(seqs[:, 2:] - 2 * seqs[:, 1:-1] + seqs[:, :-2], axis=-1)      # (N, T-2, NODES)\n    return {name: float(acc[..., sl].mean()) for name, sl in PART_GROUPS.items()}\n\n\ndef path_length(seqs: np.ndarray, part: slice = slice(0, 42)) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Mean distance travelled by the nodes of `part` (default: both hands) over a clip, in shoulder widths.\"\"\"\n    return float(np.linalg.norm(np.diff(seqs[:, :, part], axis=1), axis=-1).sum(1).mean())","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-18T00:52:08.066409Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-18T00:52:08.066792Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-18T00:52:08.079484Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-18T00:52:08.066767Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-18T00:52:08.078659Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":31},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### ▶ Effect of smoothing on the generated test clips\nFor several filter strengths: `jitter_*` (mean acceleration in shoulder widths per frame², lower = smoother), `deviation_from_raw`\n(how far the filtered clip moved away from the raw one, in shoulder widths), `path_length_ratio` (1 = the hands travel as far as\nbefore) and the **recognition accuracy** of the classifier on the filtered clips (smoothing must not hurt it). The *real clips*\nrow is the reference: real MediaPipe recordings also contain tracking noise, so \"smoother than real\" is not necessarily better.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"real_seq, gen_seq, gen_lab = arrs[\"real_seq\"], arrs[\"gen_seq\"], arrs[\"gen_labels\"]\ngen_secs = arrs[\"gen_seconds\"] if arrs.get(\"gen_seconds\") is not None else [None] * len(gen_seq)\n\n\ndef top1_of(seqs: np.ndarray) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Recognition top-1 of the classifier on (N, T, NODES, D) clips in landmark coordinates.\"\"\"\n    x = torch.from_numpy(((seqs.reshape(len(seqs), seqs.shape[1], -1) - stats[0]) / stats[1]).astype(np.float32))\n    return topk_accuracy(predict(clf, x, device), torch.from_numpy(gen_lab))[0]\n\n\ndef smoothing_row(name, sm):\n    j = jitter(sm)\n    face = [v for k, v in j.items() if k not in (\"left_hand\", \"right_hand\", \"arms\")]\n    return dict(setting=name, jitter_hands=(j[\"left_hand\"] + j[\"right_hand\"]) / 2, jitter_arms=j[\"arms\"], jitter_face=float(np.mean(face)),\n                deviation_from_raw=float(np.linalg.norm(sm - gen_seq, axis=-1).mean()), path_length_ratio=path_length(sm) / path_length(gen_seq),\n                gen_top1=top1_of(sm))\n\n\nsettings = {\"raw (no smoothing)\": None, \"light\": (4.0, 8.0), f\"default (cfg: {cfg.smooth_min_cutoff}, {cfg.smooth_beta})\": (cfg.smooth_min_cutoff, cfg.smooth_beta),\n            \"strong\": (1.0, 2.0)}\nrows = []\nfor name, s in settings.items():\n    sm = gen_seq if s is None else np.stack([smooth_sequence(c, effective_fps(len(c), sec), s[0], s[1], cfg.smooth_d_cutoff)\n                                             for c, sec in zip(gen_seq, gen_secs)])\n    rows.append(smoothing_row(name, sm))\njr = jitter(real_seq)\nrows.append(dict(setting=\"real test clips (reference)\", jitter_hands=(jr[\"left_hand\"] + jr[\"right_hand\"]) / 2, jitter_arms=jr[\"arms\"],\n                 jitter_face=float(np.mean([v for k, v in jr.items() if k not in (\"left_hand\", \"right_hand\", \"arms\")]))))\ndisplay(pd.DataFrame(rows).set_index(\"setting\").round(4))\n\n# one coordinate over time: raw vs smoothed (index fingertip of the right hand, horizontal position)\nc0, s0 = gen_seq[0], gen_secs[0]\nsm0 = smooth_sequence(c0, effective_fps(len(c0), s0), cfg.smooth_min_cutoff, cfg.smooth_beta, cfg.smooth_d_cutoff)\nplt.figure(figsize=(6.5, 2.8))\nplt.plot(c0[:, RH.start + 8, 0], label=\"raw (generated)\", alpha=0.7)\nplt.plot(sm0[:, RH.start + 8, 0], label=\"smoothed\", lw=2)\nplt.xlabel(\"frame\")\nplt.ylabel(\"x (shoulder widths)\")\nplt.title(\"right index fingertip, one generated clip\")\nplt.legend()\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-18T00:52:08.080423Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-18T00:52:08.081498Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-18T00:52:37.001262Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-18T00:52:08.08143Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-18T00:52:37.000601Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"                             jitter_hands  jitter_arms  jitter_face  \\\nsetting                                                               \nraw (no smoothing)                 0.0202       0.0318       0.0049   \nlight                              0.0071       0.0128       0.0010   \ndefault (cfg: 2.0, 4.0)            0.0049       0.0089       0.0006   \nstrong                             0.0033       0.0058       0.0003   \nreal test clips (reference)        0.0137       0.0096       0.0014   \n\n                             deviation_from_raw  path_length_ratio  gen_top1  \nsetting                                                                       \nraw (no smoothing)                       0.0000             1.0000    0.7988  \nlight   