dy>\n</table>\n</div>"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 650x280 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":32},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 8. Clip duration\n\nThe model was trained with the **original clip length** as a condition (section 3-4), so:\n\n* with a word only, `generate(...)` draws a plausible duration from the word's **duration prior** (the train clips of that word);\n* with `duration_s=1.2`, the clip is generated for that duration;\n* `resample_to_duration` turns the 64 generated frames into real-time frames (`round(seconds × fps)`), which is what an animation or\n  an avatar needs. Smoothing (section 7) and the export (section 11) use the same duration.\n\nTwo checks follow. **(a)** Does the word help to predict the duration? **(b)** Does the model really *use* the duration it is given?\nFor (b) we ask, for the same word, whether longer clips contain more movement, in real data and in generated data (a correlation\ncomputed inside each word, so differences between words do not count). If the two correlations have the same sign and similar size,\nthe model has learnt what a duration means. Remember that `cfg.fps = 30` is an **assumption** (the competition gives no frame rate): it\nonly scales the seconds, not the model.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Duration helpers\ndef duration_prior_report(dur_prior: DurationPrior, meta_test: pd.DataFrame, vocab: SignVocab) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    \"\"\"Does knowing the word help to guess how long the signing lasts? Compares, on the TEST clips, the per-word prior with a\n    single global duration (error of the log-duration and of the duration in seconds).\"\"\"\n    n = np.maximum(meta_test[\"n_frames\"].to_numpy(np.float64), 1.0)\n    ids = np.array([vocab.encode(s) for s in meta_test[\"sign\"]])\n    rows = []\n    for name, mu in ((\"global duration for every word\", np.full(len(n), dur_prior.log_mu)), (\"per-word prior\", dur_prior.word_mu[ids])):\n        rows.append(dict(predictor=name, rmse_log=float(np.sqrt(((np.log(n) - mu) ** 2).mean())),\n                         mae_seconds=float(np.abs(n - np.exp(mu)).mean() / dur_prior.fps)))\n    return pd.DataFrame(rows)\n\n\ndef resample_to_duration(seq: np.ndarray, seconds: float, fps_out: float = 30.0) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"seq (T, NUM_NODES, D) generated for `seconds` -> (round(seconds * fps_out), NUM_NODES, D) played at fps_out.\n    This is what gives the clip its real speed again (the model works on 64 frames whatever the duration).\"\"\"\n    n_out = max(2, int(round(seconds * fps_out)))\n    return resample_time(seq.reshape(len(seq), -1), n_out).reshape(n_out, *seq.shape[1:])\n\n\ndef within_word_corr(values: np.ndarray, log_dur: np.ndarray, word_ids: np.ndarray) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Correlation between a clip feature and the log-duration AFTER removing each word's mean (so only 'for the same sign, a longer\n    clip has more / less of X' is measured). NaN if it cannot be computed.\"\"\"\n    v, d = np.asarray(values, float).copy(), np.asarray(log_dur, float).copy()\n    for w in np.unique(word_ids):\n        m = word_ids == w\n        v[m] -= v[m].mean()\n        d[m] -= d[m].mean()\n    return float(np.corrcoef(v, d)[0, 1]) if v.std() > 0 and d.std() > 0 else float(\"nan\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-18T00:52:37.0023Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-18T00:52:37.002666Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-18T00:52:37.011691Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-18T00:52:37.002644Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-18T00:52:37.01085Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":33},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### ▶ Duration prior and duration control","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"if not cfg.use_duration:\n    print(\"cfg.use_duration is False: the model was trained without the duration condition, nothing to check.\")\nelse:\n    print(\"(a) predicting the duration of a TEST clip:\")\n    display(duration_prior_report(dur_prior, splits[\"test\"], vocab).round(3))\n\n    # (b) does a longer clip contain more movement? same words, real vs generated, inside each word\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(0)\n    words_b = rng.choice(arrs[\"words\"], min(30, len(arrs[\"words\"])), replace=False)\n    per_clip = lambda seqs: np.array([path_length(s[None]) for s in seqs])         # hand path length of every clip\n    m_real = np.isin(arrs[\"real_labels\"], words_b)\n    real_logd = arrs[\"real_dur_z\"][m_real] * dur_prior.log_sd + dur_prior.log_mu\n    c_real = within_word_corr(per_clip(arrs[\"real_seq\"][m_real]), real_logd, arrs[\"real_labels\"][m_real])\n    gen_clips, gen_secs_b = generate(ema.module, diffusion, vocab, [vocab.decode(int(w) + 1) for w in words_b], stats, T, C, dur_prior,\n                                     n_per_word=8, steps=cfg.gen_steps, guidance=cfg.guidance, device=device, seed=1)\n    g_seq = np.concatenate([gen_clips[vocab.decode(int(w) + 1)] for w in words_b])\n    g_lab = np.repeat(words_b, 8)\n    g_logd = np.log(np.concatenate([gen_secs_b[vocab.decode(int(w) + 1)] for w in words_b]) * dur_prior.fps)\n    c_gen = within_word_corr(per_clip(g_seq), g_logd, g_lab)\n    print(f\"(b) within-word correlation between log-duration and hand path length:  real clips {c_real:+.2f}   generated clips {c_gen:+.2f}\")\n\n    # the same word generated for three durations, played back at its real speed\n    word = vocab.decode(int(words_b[0]) + 1)\n    fig, axes = plt.subplots(3, 6, figsize=(12, 6.2), sharex=True, sharey=True)\n    for r, sec in enumerate((0.5, 1.2, 2.5)):\n        c, s = generate(ema.module, diffusion, vocab, [word], stats, T, C, dur_prior, n_per_word=1, steps=cfg.gen_steps,\n                        guidance=cfg.guidance, device=device, seed=3, duration_s=sec)\n        clip30 = resample_to_duration(smooth_clips(c[word], s[word], cfg)[0], sec, cfg.fps)       # real-time frames\n        for k, t in enumerate(np.linspace(0, len(clip30) - 1, 6).astype(int)):\n            _draw_frame(axes[r, k], clip30[t])\n            axes[r, k].set_aspect(\"equal\")\n            axes[r, k].axis(\"off\")\n            axes[r, k].set_title(f\"{t / cfg.fps:.2f} s\", fontsize=8)\n        axes[r, 0].text(-0.1, 0.5, f\"{sec} s\\n({len(clip30)} frames)\", transform=axes[r, 0].transAxes, ha=\"right\", va=\"center\", fontsize=9)\n    axes[0, 0].invert_yaxis()\n    fig.suptitle(f\"'{word}' generated for 0.5 s, 1.2 s and 2.5 s (time axis in seconds)\")\n    plt.tight_layout()\n    plt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-18T00:52:37.01341Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-18T00:52:37.01375Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-18T00:52:54.678043Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-18T00:52:37.013729Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-18T00:52:54.677183Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"(a) predicting the duration of a TEST clip:\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"                        predictor  rmse_log  mae_seconds\n0  global duration for every word     0.842        0.732\n1                  per-word prior     0.834        0.730","text/html":"<div>\n<style scoped>\n    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n        vertical-align: middle;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n        vertical-align: top;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe thead th {\n        text-align: right;\n    }\n</style>\n<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n  <thead>\n    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n      <th></th>\n      <th>predictor</th>\n      <th>rmse_log</th>\n      <th>mae_seconds</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <th>0</th>\n      <td>global duration for every word</td>\n      <td>0.842</td>\n      <td>0.732</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>1</th>\n      <td>per-word prior</td>\n      <td>0.834</td>\n      <td>0.730</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n</div>"},"metadata":{}},{"name":"stdout","text":"(b) within-word correlation between log-duration and hand path length:  real clips +0.62   generated clips +0.91\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1200x620 with 18 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":34},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 9. Face detail: lips, eyebrows, eyes\n\nWith `FACE_PRESET = \"expressive\"` the model generates **79 face points** (outer and inner lips, both eyebrows, both eye contours, nose, face\ncontour) instead of 9. The parquet files already contain the full 468-point face mesh, so nothing new had to be recorded: only the\nselection in `FACE_PRESETS` and the preprocessing changed. Face coordinates carry less weight in the loss (`face_loss_weight`) so that they\ndo not drown out the hands; the face is *ignored* in frames where MediaPipe lost it.\n\nWhy it matters: in ASL, **non-manual markers** (raised eyebrows for yes/no questions, furrowed brows for wh-questions, mouth shapes, eye gaze)\nare part of the grammar. The error of the face parts is reported separately (`lips`, `brows`, `eyes`, `nose + contour`) in the test summary above.\n\nFor an avatar, a point cloud is not directly usable: `face_blendshapes` converts the landmarks into six **blend-shape weights** between 0 and 1\n(`jawOpen`, `mouthWide`, `browUp_R/L`, `eyeBlink_R/L`), the controls most avatar rigs (VRM, ARKit, Unity, Blender shape keys) understand.\nDistances are divided by the eye-to-eye width, and the neutral / extreme values come from real train clips (`fit_face_reference`).","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Face blend-shape curves (for an avatar's face) from the extended face landmarks\nBLEND_NAMES = [\"jawOpen\", \"mouthWide\", \"browUp_R\", \"browUp_L\", \"eyeBlink_R\", \"eyeBlink_L\"]\n\n\ndef face_features(seq: np.ndarray) -> Dict[str, np.ndarray]:\n    \"\"\"seq (T, NUM_NODES, D) -> distances between face landmarks, divided by the distance between the outer eye corners (so they\n    do not depend on the size of the face). Needs FACE_PRESET = \"expressive\". Every value is a (T,) curve.\"\"\"\n    assert FACE_PRESET == \"expressive\", \"face features need FACE_PRESET = 'expressive'\"\n    P = lambda raw: seq[:, FACE_NODE[raw], :2]\n    d = lambda a, b: np.linalg.norm(P(a) - P(b), axis=-1)\n    iod = np.maximum(d(33, 263), 1e-6)\n    return {\"jaw_open\": d(13, 14) / iod,                   # gap between the inner lips\n            \"mouth_width\": d(61, 291) / iod,               # mouth corners\n            \"brow_r\": d(105, 159) / iod, \"brow_l\": d(334, 386) / iod,      # eyebrow to upper eyelid\n            \"eye_r\": d(159, 145) / iod, \"eye_l\": d(386, 374) / iod}        # eyelid opening\n\n\ndef fit_face_reference(real_seqs: np.ndarray) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Neutral value (median) and extremes (5th / 95th percentile) of every feature over REAL clips (N, T, NUM_NODES, D).\n    They turn a feature into a 0..1 blend-shape weight in `face_blendshapes`.\"\"\"\n    feats = [face_features(s) for s in real_seqs]\n    ref = {}\n    for k in feats[0]:\n        v = np.concatenate([f[k] for f in feats])\n        ref[k] = dict(neutral=float(np.median(v)), lo=float(np.percentile(v, 5)), hi=float(np.percentile(v, 95)))\n    return ref\n\n\ndef face_blendshapes(seq: np.ndarray, ref: dict) -> Dict[str, np.ndarray]:\n    \"\"\"seq (T, NUM_NODES, D) -> {blend-shape name: (T,) weights in [0, 1]}.\n    Open-type shapes (jaw, mouth, brows) grow above the neutral value; blinks grow when the eyelid opening shrinks below it.\"\"\"\n    f = face_features(seq)\n    up = lambda k: np.clip((f[k] - ref[k][\"neutral\"]) / max(ref[k][\"hi\"] - ref[k][\"neutral\"], 1e-6), 0, 1)\n    down = lambda k: np.clip((ref[k][\"neutral\"] - f[k]) / max(ref[k][\"neutral\"] - ref[k][\"lo\"], 1e-6), 0, 1)\n    return {\"jawOpen\": up(\"jaw_open\"), \"mouthWide\": up(\"mouth_width\"), \"browUp_R\": up(\"brow_r\"), \"browUp_L\": up(\"brow_l\"),\n            \"eyeBlink_R\": down(\"eye_r\"), \"eyeBlink_L\": down(\"eye_l\")}\n\n\ndef plot_face(seqs: List[np.ndarray], titles: List[str], frames: List[int]):\n    \"\"\"Close-up of the face of several clips (list of (T, NUM_NODES, D)) at the given frames: one row per clip.\"\"\"\n    fig, axes = plt.subplots(len(seqs), len(frames), figsize=(2.0 * len(frames), 2.0 * len(seqs)), squeeze=False)\n    allp = np.concatenate([s[:, FACE, :2].reshape(-1, 2) for s in seqs])\n    lo, hi = np.percentile(allp, 0.5, axis=0), np.percentile(allp, 99.5, axis=0)\n    for r, (s, title) in enumerate(zip(seqs, titles)):\n        for c, t in enumerate(frames):\n            ax = axes[r, c]\n            for name, sl in FACE_SLICE.items():\n                pts = s[t, sl, :2]\n                pts = np.vstack([pts, pts[:1]]) if name in FACE_LOOPS else pts\n                (ax.plot(pts[:, 0], pts[:, 1], \"-\", color=FACE_STYLE[name], lw=1) if name in FACE_LOOPS + FACE_LINES\n                 else ax.plot(pts[:, 0], pts[:, 1], \".\", color=FACE_STYLE[name], ms=3))\n            ax.set_xlim(lo[0], hi[0])\n            ax.set_ylim(hi[1], lo[1])\n            ax.set_aspect(\"equal\")\n            ax.axis(\"off\")\n            if r == 0:\n                ax.set_title(f\"t={t}\", fontsize=8)\n            if c == 0:\n                ax.text(-0.05, 0.5, title, transform=ax.transAxes, rotation=90, ha=\"right\", va=\"center\", fontsize=8)\n    fig.tight_layout()\n    return fig","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-18T00:52:54.679128Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-18T00:52:54.679765Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-18T00:52:54.694421Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-18T00:52:54.679741Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-18T00:52:54.693698Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":35},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### ▶ Face close-up and blend-shape curves (real vs generated)","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"if FACE_PRESET != \"expressive\":\n    print(\"FACE_PRESET is 'basic': the face has only 9 points, nothing to show here.\")\nelse:\n    # neutral / extreme values of every face measurement, from real TRAIN clips\n    x_tr, _, _ = dataset_arrays(datasets[\"train\"], max_n=1500)\n    face_ref = fit_face_reference(destandardise(x_tr.numpy(), stats))\n    Path(cfg.work_dir, \"face_reference.json\").write_text(json.dumps(face_ref, indent=1))\n    print(\"saved\", Path(cfg.work_dir, \"face_reference.json\"))\n\n    w = int(arrs[\"words\"][0])\n    word = vocab.decode(w + 1)\n    real_c, gen_c = arrs[\"real_seq\"][arrs[\"real_labels\"] == w][0], arrs[\"gen_seq\"][arrs[\"gen_labels\"] == w][0]\n    frames = list(np.linspace(0, T - 1, 6).astype(int))\n    _ = plot_face([real_c, gen_c], [\"real\", \"generated\"], frames)\n    plt.suptitle(f\"face of '{word}': real (test signer) vs generated\", y=1.02)\n    plt.show()\n\n    fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(12, 2.8), sharey=True)\n    for ax, key in zip(axes, (\"jawOpen\", \"browUp_R\", \"eyeBlink_R\")):\n        ax.plot(face_blendshapes(real_c, face_ref)[key], label=\"real\")\n        ax.plot(face_blendshapes(gen_c, face_ref)[key], label=\"generated\")\n        ax.set_title(key)\n        ax.set_xlabel(\"frame\")\n    axes[0].legend()\n    plt.tight_layout()\n    plt.show()\n    display(pd.Series(results[\"mpjpe_per_group_same_word\"], name=\"nearest-real MPJPE per part (generated, same word)\").round(4).to_frame())","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-18T00:52:54.695388Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-18T00:52:54.695732Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-18T00:52:55.852116Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-18T00:52:54.695711Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-18T00:52:55.851501Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"saved /kaggle/working/face_reference.json\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1200x400 with 12 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1200x280 with 3 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"                nearest-real MPJPE per part (generated, same word)\nleft_hand                                                  0.3219 \nright_hand                                                 0.6178 \narms                                                       0.2533 \nlips                                                       0.0821 \nbrows                                                      0.0938 \neyes                                                       0.0856 \nnose + contour                                             0.0915 ","text/html":"<div>\n<style scoped>\n    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n        vertical-align: middle;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n        vertical-align: top;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe thead th {\n        text-align: right;\n    }\n</style>\n<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n  <thead>\n    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n      <th></th>\n      <th>nearest-real MPJPE per part (generated, same word)</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <th>left_hand</th>\n      <td>0.3219</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>right_hand</th>\n      <td>0.6178</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>arms</th>\n      <td>0.2533</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>lips</th>\n      <td>0.0821</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>brows</th>\n      <td>0.0938</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>eyes</th>\n      <td>0.0856</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>nose + contour</th>\n      <td>0.0915</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n</div>"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":36},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 10. Going 3D: how good is MediaPipe `z`, and where does depth come from?\n\nAn avatar lives in 3-D, but the model so far generates `(x, y)`. Two ways to get depth:\n\n1. **`cfg.use_z = True`**: the model generates `z` too. The cache already contains it, so the switch costs nothing at preprocessing. MediaPipe\n   estimates `z` from a single 2-D image, so it is noisy; whether the model can still learn something useful from it is an experiment, not a\n   given. Run it in a second working directory and compare the two runs with `compare_runs` below (and, above all, with the human\n   evaluation of section 12).\n2. **A depth lifter**: a separate small network that predicts `z` from the generated `(x, y)` clips (trained on real train clips, with MediaPipe's\n   `z` as the target). It cannot be better than its target, but it averages out the per-frame noise and keeps the generator's task simple.\n\n**Honest limits.** In both cases the \"ground truth\" for depth is MediaPipe's own estimate, so there is no real 3-D reference: we can measure\n*noise* and *agreement with MediaPipe*, not true depth accuracy. Without any `z`, an avatar can still move its arms in the image plane, but a\ncurled finger only looks *shorter* instead of *bent*.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# 3D: how noisy is MediaPipe z, a depth lifter (2-D -> z) and a helper to compare runs\ndef _rough(x: np.ndarray) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Roughness of a coordinate: RMS of its 2nd temporal difference / how much it moves (std over time). x (N, T, nodes).\n    ~0 = smooth trajectory, large = mostly measurement noise.\"\"\"\n    acc = x[:, 2:] - 2 * x[:, 1:-1] + x[:, :-2]\n    return float(np.sqrt((acc ** 2).mean()) / (x.std(axis=1).mean() + 1e-9))\n\n\ndef load_xyz(meta: pd.DataFrame, cache_path, n: int, seed: int = 0):\n    \"\"\"Random `n` clips of `meta` from the cache -> xy (n, T, NODES, 2), z (n, T, NODES), present (n, T, 3) bool.\"\"\"\n    rows = np.sort(meta[\"cache_idx\"].to_numpy()[np.random.default_rng(seed).choice(len(meta), min(n, len(meta)), replace=False)])\n    x = np.asarray(np.load(cache_path, mmap_mode=\"r\")[rows], np.float32)\n    x = x.reshape(len(rows), x.shape[1], NUM_NODES, 3)\n    return x[..., :2], x[..., 2], np.asarray(np.load(parts_path(cache_path), mmap_mode=\"r\")[rows], bool)\n\n\ndef z_noise_report(cache_path, meta: pd.DataFrame, n: int = 1500, seed: int = 0) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    \"\"\"Per body part: roughness of x, y and z on clips whose hands are almost always detected. If z is much rougher than x and y,\n    it is mostly noise (MediaPipe estimates depth from a single 2-D image) and feeding it to the model needs care.\"\"\"\n    good = meta[meta[\"hand_frac\"] >= 0.9]\n    if len(good) < 20:                                    # tiny / unusual dataset: use whatever there is\n        good = meta\n    xy, z, _ = load_xyz(good, cache_path, n, seed)\n    rows = []\n    for name, sl in ((\"left hand\", LH), (\"right hand\", RH), (\"arms\", POSE), (\"face\", FACE)):\n        rows.append(dict(part=name, rough_x=_rough(xy[:, :, sl, 0]), rough_y=_rough(xy[:, :, sl, 1]), rough_z=_rough(z[:, :, sl]),\n                         spread_z_vs_xy=float(z[:, :, sl].std() / xy[:, :, sl].std())))\n    df = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n    df[\"z_rougher_by\"] = df[\"rough_z\"] / ((df[\"rough_x\"] + df[\"rough_y\"]) / 2)\n    return df\n\n\nclass DepthLifter(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"Predicts the depth z of every landmark from the 2-D landmarks of the whole clip (temporal 1-D convolutions, so a frame\n    is read in the context of its neighbours). xy (B, T, NODES, 2) -> z (B, T, NODES), in shoulder widths.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, hidden: int = 256):\n        super().__init__()\n        layers, c_in = [], NUM_NODES * 2\n        for dil in (1, 2, 4, 1):\n            layers += [nn.Conv1d(c_in, hidden, 5, padding=2 * dil, dilation=dil), nn.BatchNorm1d(hidden), nn.GELU()]\n            c_in = hidden\n        self.net = nn.Sequential(*layers, nn.Conv1d(hidden, NUM_NODES, 1))\n        self.register_buffer(\"z_scale\", torch.ones(()))\n\n    def forward(self, xy: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n        h = self.net(xy.flatten(2).transpose(1, 2))             # (B, NODES, T)\n        return h.transpose(1, 2) * self.z_scale\n\n\ndef _depth_weights(present: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n    \"\"\"present (B, T, 3) -> weights (B, T, NODES): 0 for hands / face that were not detected (their z is gap-filling).\"\"\"\n    w = torch.ones(present.shape[0], present.shape[1], NUM_NODES)\n    w[..., LH], w[..., RH], w[..., FACE] = present[..., 0:1].float(), present[..., 1:2].float(), present[..., 2:3].float()\n    return w\n\n\ndef depth_metrics(lifter: DepthLifter, xy, z, present, baseline_z: np.ndarray, device: str) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    \"\"\"RMSE of z and correlation with MediaPipe's z, per part, for the lifter and for a '2-D blind' baseline (mean z per node).\"\"\"\n    lifter.eval()\n    with torch.no_grad():\n        pred = torch.cat([lifter(torch.from_numpy(xy[i:i + 256]).to(device)).cpu() for i in range(0, len(xy), 256)]).numpy()\n    w = _depth_weights(torch.from_numpy(present)).numpy() > 0\n    rows = []\n    for name, sl in ((\"hands\", slice(0, 42)), (\"arms\", POSE), (\"face\", FACE)):\n        m = w[:, :, sl]\n        t, p, b = z[:, :, sl][m], pred[:, :, sl][m], np.broadcast_to(baseline_z[sl], z[:, :, sl].shape)[m]\n        rows.append(dict(part=name, rmse_baseline_mean_z=float(np.sqrt(((t - b) ** 2).mean())), rmse_lifter=float(np.sqrt(((t - p) ** 2).mean())),\n                         corr_lifter=float(np.corrcoef(t, p)[0, 1]) if t.std() > 0 and p.std() > 0 else float(\"nan\")))\n    return pd.DataFrame(rows)\n\n\ndef train_depth_lifter(cache_path, splits: Dict[str, pd.DataFrame], cfg: Config, device: str, n_train: int = 6000, n_eval: int = 2000,\n                       epochs: int = 12, lr: float = 2e-3):\n    \"\"\"Train the lifter on REAL train clips (target = MediaPipe's z), report val / test metrics. -> (lifter, metrics DataFrame).\"\"\"\n    xy, z, pr = load_xyz(splits[\"train\"], cache_path, n_train, cfg.seed)\n    w_all = _depth_weights(torch.from_numpy(pr)).numpy()\n    lifter = DepthLifter().to(device)\n    lifter.z_scale.fill_(float(np.sqrt((z ** 2 * w_all).sum() / w_all.sum())))\n    baseline_z = (z * w_all).sum((0, 1)) / np.maximum(w_all.sum((0, 1)), 1)\n    xy_t, z_t, w_t = torch.from_numpy(xy), torch.from_numpy(z / float(lifter.z_scale)), torch.from_numpy(w_all)\n    opt = torch.optim.AdamW(lifter.parameters(), lr=lr, weight_decay=1e-2)\n    steps = epochs * math.ceil(len(xy) / 64)\n    sched = torch.optim.lr_scheduler.OneCycleLR(opt, max_lr=lr, total_steps=steps, pct_start=0.2)\n    for epoch in range(epochs):\n        lifter.train()\n        perm = torch.randperm(len(xy))\n        for i in range(0, len(xy), 64):\n            b = perm[i:i + 64]\n            pred = lifter(xy_t[b].to(device)) / lifter.z_scale\n            loss = (((pred - z_t[b].to(device)) ** 2) * w_t[b].to(device)).sum() / w_t[b].sum()\n            opt.zero_grad(set_to_none=True)\n            loss.backward()\n            opt.step()\n            sched.step()\n    out = []\n    for name in (\"val\", \"test\"):\n        xy_e, z_e, p_e = load_xyz(splits[name], cache_path, n_eval, cfg.seed)\n        out.append(depth_metrics(lifter, xy_e, z_e, p_e, baseline_z, device).assign(split=name))\n    torch.save({\"state\": lifter.state_dict()}, Path(cfg.work_dir) / \"depth_lifter.pt\")\n    return lifter.eval(), pd.concat(out)[[\"split\", \"part\", \"rmse_baseline_mean_z\", \"rmse_lifter\", \"corr_lifter\"]].reset_index(drop=True)\n\n\n@torch.no_grad()\ndef lift_depth(lifter: DepthLifter, seq: np.ndarray, device: str = \"cpu\") -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Add a predicted z to 2-D clips: (N, T, NODES, 2) or (T, NODES, 2) -> same shape with a third coordinate.\"\"\"\n    single = seq.ndim == 3\n    xy = torch.from_numpy(np.asarray(seq[None] if single else seq, np.float32)[..., :2]).to(device)\n    z = lifter.to(device).eval()(xy).cpu().numpy()\n    out = np.concatenate([xy.cpu().numpy(), z[..., None]], axis=-1)\n    return out[0] if single else out\n\n\ndef compare_runs(runs: Dict[str, str]) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    \"\"\"{run name: work_dir} -> the main test metrics of every run side by side (reads <work_dir>/eval_results.json).\n    Use it to compare e.g. use_z=False vs use_z=True. Runs with different channels are only ROUGHLY comparable (the classifier,\n    the Fréchet space and the MPJPE all change with the channels): look at 'gen/real top-1' and, above all, at the human evaluation.\"\"\"\n    rows = []\n    for name, d in runs.items():\n        r = json.loads(Path(d, \"eval_results.json\").read_text())\n        rows.append({\"run\": name, \"use_z\": r.get(\"use_z\"), \"face\": r.get(\"face_preset\"), \"test loss\": r[\"test_denoising_loss\"],\n                     \"top-1 generated\": r[\"recognition_top1_generated\"], \"top-1 real\": r[\"recognition_top1_real_test\"],\n                     \"gen/real top-1\": r[\"recognition_top1_generated\"] / max(r[\"recognition_top1_real_test\"], 1e-9),\n                     \"FD\": r[\"frechet_distance_gen_vs_real_test\"], \"FD floor\": r[\"frechet_distance_floor_real_train_vs_real_test\"],\n                     \"MPJPE same word\": r[\"mpjpe_gen_to_nearest_real_same_word\"]})\n    return pd.DataFrame(rows)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-18T00:52:55.853134Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-18T00:52:55.853394Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-18T00:52:55.882998Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-18T00:52:55.853372Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-18T00:52:55.882246Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":37},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### ▶ How noisy is `z`? Train the depth lifter\n`rough_*` = roughness of each coordinate (large = mostly noise); `z_rougher_by` is the ratio of z-roughness to the x/y roughness. The lifter\ntable compares, per part, the z error of a baseline that knows nothing about the pose (the mean z of each landmark) with the lifter, and the\ncorrelation with MediaPipe's z. Training takes about a minute on a GPU.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"display(z_noise_report(cache_path, meta).round(3))\n\nlifter, lifter_report = train_depth_lifter(cache_path, splits, cfg, device)\ndisplay(lifter_report.round(4))\nprint(\"saved\", Path(cfg.work_dir, \"depth_lifter.pt\"))\n\n# one real test clip: MediaPipe's z vs the lifter's z for the right index fingertip, relative to the wrist\nxy_e, z_e, p_e = load_xyz(splits[\"test\"], cache_path, 50, seed=1)\nk = int(np.argmax(p_e[:, :, 1].mean(1)))                                       # a clip where the right hand is tracked\nz_hat = lift_depth(lifter, xy_e[k], device)[..., 2]\nplt.figure(figsize=(6.5, 2.8))\nplt.plot(z_e[k][:, RH.start + 8] - z_e[k][:, RH.start], label=\"MediaPipe z (noisy target)\")\nplt.plot(z_hat[:, RH.start + 8] - z_hat[:, RH.start], label=\"depth lifter z\")\nplt.xlabel(\"frame\")\nplt.ylabel(\"z fingertip - z wrist\")\nplt.legend()\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-18T00:52:55.884059Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-18T00:52:55.884398Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-18T00:53:17.575173Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-18T00:52:55.884371Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-18T00:53:17.574516Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"         part  rough_x  rough_y  rough_z  spread_z_vs_xy  z_rougher_by\n0   left hand    0.395    0.717    0.604           1.538         1.086\n1  right hand    0.326    0.479    0.754           1.367         1.873\n2        arms    0.485    0.762    0.547           2.145         0.878\n3        face    0.274    0.330    0.403           0.309         1.334","text/html":"<div>\n<style scoped>\n    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n        vertical-align: middle;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n        vertical-align: top;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe thead th {\n        text-align: right;\n    }\n</style>\n<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n  <thead>\n    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n      <th></th>\n      <th>part</th>\n      <th>rough_x</th>\n      <th>rough_y</th>\n      <th>rough_z</th>\n      <th>spread_z_vs_xy</th>\n      <th>z_rougher_by</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <th>0</th>\n      <td>left hand</td>\n      <td>0.395</td>\n      <td>0.717</td>\n      <td>0.604</td>\n      <td>1.538</td>\n      <td>1.086</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>1</th>\n      <td>right hand</td>\n      <td>0.326</td>\n      <td>0.479</td>\n      <td>0.754</td>\n      <td>1.367</td>\n      <td>1.873</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>2</th>\n      <td>arms</td>\n      <td>0.485</td>\n      <td>0.762</td>\n      <td>0.547</td>\n      <td>2.145</td>\n      <td>0.878</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>3</th>\n      <td>face</td>\n      <td>0.274</td>\n      <td>0.330</td>\n      <td>0.403</td>\n      <td>0.309</td>\n      <td>1.334</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n</div>"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"  split   part  rmse_baseline_mean_z  rmse_lifter  corr_lifter\n0   val  hands                0.1086       0.1050       0.4772\n1   val   arms                1.1926       0.6242       0.8561\n2   val   face                0.0336       0.0279       0.9144\n3  test  hands                0.0995       0.0941       0.5226\n4  test   arms                1.0961       0.6864       0.8278\n5  test   face                0.0303       0.0252       0.9334","text/html":"<div>\n<style scoped>\n    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n        vertical-align: middle;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n        vertical-align: top;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe thead th {\n        text-align: right;\n    }\n</style>\n<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n  <thead>\n    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n      <th></th>\n      <th>split</th>\n      <th>part</th>\n      <th>rmse_baseline_mean_z</th>\n      <th>rmse_lifter</th>\n      <th>corr_lifter</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <th>0</th>\n      <td>val</td>\n      <td>hands</td>\n      <td>0.1086</td>\n      <td>0.1050</td>\n      <td>0.4772</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>1</th>\n      <td>val</td>\n      <td>arms</td>\n      <td>1.1926</td>\n      <td>0.6242</td>\n      <td>0.8561</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>2</th>\n      <td>val</td>\n      <td>face</td>\n      <td>0.0336</td>\n      <td>0.0279</td>\n      <td>0.9144</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>3</th>\n      <td>test</td>\n      <td>hands</td>\n      <td>0.0995</td>\n      <td>0.0941</td>\n      <td>0.5226</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>4</th>\n      <td>test</td>\n      <td>arms</td>\n      <td>1.0961</td>\n      <td>0.6864</td>\n      <td>0.8278</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>5</th>\n      <td>test</td>\n      <td>face</td>\n      <td>0.0303</td>\n      <td>0.0252</td>\n      <td>0.9334</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n</div>"},"metadata":{}},{"name":"stdout","text":"saved /kaggle/working/depth_lifter.pt\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 650x280 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":38},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Testing `use_z = True`\nSet `cfg.use_z = True` (and a new `work_dir`, e.g. `/kaggle/working/run_z`, with `cache_dir` pointing to the existing cache so nothing is recomputed),\nthen run the notebook again from the data-loader cell. Afterwards compare the runs:\n\n```python\ncompare_runs({\"xy only\": \"/kaggle/working\", \"xyz\": \"/kaggle/working/run_z\"})\n```","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 11. From landmarks to an avatar (retargeting)\n\nLandmarks are *positions*; an avatar is driven by *bone rotations*. The conversion (retargeting) is done in `retarget_sequence`:\n\n| part | method |\n|---|---|\n| **arms** | analytic **two-bone IK**: the wrist goes where the signer's wrist is (relative to the shoulder), the elbow is placed with the law of cosines and the observed elbow decides on which side it bends. The hand therefore touches the forehead / chin / chest exactly where the sign needs it, even if the avatar's arms are not as long as the signer's. |\n| **hand** | full 3-D orientation from the palm landmarks (wrist, index, middle and little-finger bases). The roll about the forearm axis is shared between forearm and wrist (`twist_share`), as in a real arm. |\n| **fingers** | **IK with joint limits** in the hand's own frame: for each finger a bounded least-squares problem finds the 4 joint angles (knuckle flexion + spread, 2 hinge joints) whose joints are closest to the observed ones. Impossible poses (a finger bent backwards, a sideways bend at the last joints) are projected onto the nearest reachable pose. |\n| **face** | blend-shape weights (section 9) |\n\nEverything is done in a generic **humanoid upper body in a T-pose with Unity-style bone names** (`LeftUpperArm`, `LeftIndexProximal`, ...), so the output\ncan be mapped to most rigs. **I do not know your avatar's format**: rig proportions, rest pose and bone orientations differ between Unity Humanoid,\nVRM, Mixamo and Blender rigs, so the last step (mapping to *your* skeleton) is yours: either edit `AvatarSpec` to your character's measurements and\nuse the BVH in Blender / Unity's retargeting, or read the JSON in your engine. `bone_name(name, \"vrm\" | \"mixamo\")` renames the bones.\n\n**Conventions.** Landmark space: x right, y down, z = MediaPipe depth. Avatar space: right-handed, +X = the avatar's left, +Y up, +Z = the direction the avatar\nfaces, unit = shoulder width. Unity is left-handed (negate x when importing). A mirrored video (the signer's left shoulder on the left of the image) is detected\nautomatically.\n\n**Limits.** Head, torso, shoulders and eye gaze are not animated (identity). Without depth (`D = 2` and no lifter) the motion is flat. Retargeting\nis deterministic geometry: it cannot repair a bad generated sign.\n\n**Self-check.** The retargeting code was verified by *forward kinematics round trips*: random avatar poses → landmarks → retargeting → landmarks again (arm\nerror ≈ 1e-15, hand orientation exact, finger error ≈ 1e-4 shoulder widths) and BVH files re-read independently. The cell below repeats a quick version on your generated clips.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Avatar retargeting, part 1: geometry helpers, avatar description, skeleton\nfrom scipy.optimize import least_squares\nfrom scipy.spatial.transform import Rotation as Rot\nfrom dataclasses import field\n\n# ---- coordinate systems --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Landmark space : x to the right of the IMAGE, y DOWN, z = MediaPipe depth (smaller = closer to the camera). Unit = shoulder width.\n# Avatar space   : right-handed, X = the avatar's LEFT, Y = up, Z = the direction the avatar faces (towards the viewer). Unit = shoulder\n#                  width, origin = shoulder mid-point (chest). T-pose: the left arm points to +X, the right arm to -X, palms down.\n# If the \"left\" shoulder is on the LEFT of the image the video is mirrored: X = -x_image undoes the mirroring.\ndef _unit(v: np.ndarray, eps: float = 1e-9) -> np.ndarray:\n    return v / np.maximum(np.linalg.norm(v, axis=-1, keepdims=True), eps)\n\n\ndef skew(v: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"(..., 3) -> (..., 3, 3) matrices K with K @ u = v x u.\"\"\"\n    z = np.zeros(v.shape[:-1])\n    return np.stack([np.stack([z, -v[..., 2], v[..., 1]], -1), np.stack([v[..., 2], z, -v[..., 0]], -1),\n                     np.stack([-v[..., 1], v[..., 0], z], -1)], -2)\n\n\ndef swing(a: np.ndarray, b: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Shortest-arc rotation matrices taking the direction a to the direction b (any batch shape, vectors (..., 3)).\"\"\"\n    a, b = np.broadcast_arrays(_unit(a), _unit(b))\n    c = (a * b).sum(-1)[..., None, None]\n    K = skew(np.cross(a, b))\n    R = np.eye(3) + K + (K @ K) / np.maximum(1.0 + c, 1e-9)         # Rodrigues; singular only when b = -a (handled below)\n    flip = c[..., 0, 0] < -1.0 + 1e-7\n    if flip.any():                                                  # opposite directions: half-turn about any perpendicular axis\n        aa = a[flip]\n        e = np.where(np.abs(aa[:, :1]) < 0.9, np.array([[1.0, 0, 0]]), np.array([[0, 1.0, 0]]))\n        u = _unit(np.cross(aa, e))\n        R[flip] = 2 * u[:, :, None] * u[:, None, :] - np.eye(3)\n    return R\n\n\ndef axis_rot(axis: np.ndarray, angle: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Rotation matrices about `axis` (3,) or (..., 3) by `angle` (...,) radians.\"\"\"\n    angle = np.asarray(angle, float)\n    K = skew(np.broadcast_to(_unit(np.asarray(axis, float)), angle.shape + (3,)))\n    return np.eye(3) + np.sin(angle)[..., None, None] * K + (1 - np.cos(angle))[..., None, None] * (K @ K)\n\n\ndef rot_x(a): return axis_rot(np.array([1.0, 0, 0]), a)\ndef rot_z(a): return axis_rot(np.array([0, 0, 1.0]), a)\n\n\ndef detect_mirrored(seq: np.ndarray) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"True if the anatomical LEFT shoulder is on the left of the image (= a mirrored / selfie video).\"\"\"\n    return bool(np.mean(seq[:, P_LS, 0]) < np.mean(seq[:, P_RS, 0]))\n\n\ndef to_avatar_space(seq: np.ndarray, mirrored: bool) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"(T, NODES, 3) landmark space -> avatar space (see the comment above).\"\"\"\n    return np.stack([(-1.0 if mirrored else 1.0) * seq[..., 0], -seq[..., 1], -seq[..., 2]], axis=-1)\n\n\ndef from_avatar_space(seq: np.ndarray, mirrored: bool) -> np.ndarray:\n    return np.stack([(-1.0 if mirrored else 1.0) * seq[..., 0], -seq[..., 1], -seq[..., 2]], axis=-1)   # the map is its own inverse\n\n\n# ---- the avatar ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFINGERS = [\"Thumb\", \"Index\", \"Middle\", \"Ring\", \"Little\"]\nPHALANGES = [\"Proximal\", \"Intermediate\", \"Distal\"]\nHAND_REST_BASIS = {                           # columns = (side s, forward f, palm normal n) of the hand in the T-pose, avatar space\n    \"Left\": np.array([[0, 1, 0], [0, 0, -1], [1, 0, 0]], float),      # s = +Z (thumb forward), f = +X, n = -Y (palm down)\n    \"Right\": np.array([[0, -1, 0], [0, 0, -1], [1, 0, 0]], float),    # s = +Z,                 f = -X, n = -Y\n}\n# Joint limits of the finger IK (radians). Angles per finger: [MCP flexion, MCP abduction, PIP flexion, DIP flexion]\n# (thumb: CMC flexion, CMC abduction, MCP flexion, IP flexion). Positive flexion curls the finger towards the palm.\n_D = math.radians\nFINGER_LO = np.array([[_D(-15), _D(-40), _D(-10), _D(-10)]] + [[_D(-30), _D(-25), _D(0), _D(0)]] * 4)\nFINGER_HI = np.array([[_D(60), _D(60), _D(70), _D(80)]] + [[_D(100), _D(25), _D(110), _D(90)]] * 4)\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass AvatarSpec:\n    \"\"\"Proportions of the avatar skeleton, in shoulder widths. The defaults describe an average adult; `fit_avatar_spec` measures them\n    on real MediaPipe hands/arms so that the avatar matches the data. Replace the numbers with your own character's to retarget to it.\n    The hand frame is (x = towards the thumb side, y = forward = wrist -> middle finger base, z = palm normal).\"\"\"\n    upper_arm: float = 0.62\n    forearm: float = 0.55\n    finger_base: np.ndarray = field(default_factory=lambda: np.array(          # first joint of each finger, relative to the wrist\n        [[0.075, 0.08, 0.0], [0.075, 0.25, 0.0], [0.0, 0.26, 0.0], [-0.06, 0.24, 0.0], [-0.11, 0.21, 0.0]]))\n    finger_len: np.ndarray = field(default_factory=lambda: np.array(           # bone lengths: proximal, intermediate, distal\n        [[0.09, 0.08, 0.065], [0.10, 0.06, 0.05], [0.11, 0.07, 0.055], [0.10, 0.065, 0.05], [0.08, 0.045, 0.04]]))\n    finger_rest: np.ndarray = field(default_factory=lambda: np.array(          # direction of every finger when the hand is open and flat\n        [[0.64, 0.77, 0.0]] + [[0.0, 1.0, 0.0]] * 4))\n    twist_share: float = 0.5               # share of the hand's roll about the forearm axis given to the forearm (rest: the wrist)\n\n\ndef fit_avatar_spec(seqs3d: np.ndarray, presents: np.ndarray, mirrored: bool) -> AvatarSpec:\n    \"\"\"Measure arm and finger proportions as medians over real clips. seqs3d (N, T, NODES, 3) in LANDMARK space (x, y, z of the cache),\n    presents (N, T, 3) detection flags. Hand frames use the same definition as the retargeting, so spec and retargeting agree.\"\"\"\n    spec = AvatarSpec()\n    av = np.stack([to_avatar_space(s, mirrored) for s in seqs3d])\n    up = np.linalg.norm(av[:, :, P_LS] - av[:, :, P_LE], axis=-1), np.linalg.norm(av[:, :, P_RS] - av[:, :, P_RE], axis=-1)\n    fo = np.linalg.norm(av[:, :, P_LE] - av[:, :, P_LW], axis=-1), np.linalg.norm(av[:, :, P_RE] - av[:, :, P_RW], axis=-1)\n    spec.upper_arm, spec.forearm = float(np.median(np.concatenate([u.ravel() for u in up]))), float(np.median(np.concatenate([f.ravel() for f in fo])))\n    base, length = [], []\n    for side, sl, col in ((\"Left\", LH, 0), (\"Right\", RH, 1)):\n        ok = presents[:, :, col]                                          # frames where this hand was really detected\n        pts = av[:, :, sl][ok]                                            # (M, 21, 3)\n        if len(pts) < 10:\n            continue\n        q = hand_canonical(pts[:, None], side)[:, 0]                      # (M, 21, 3) in the hand frame\n        base.append(np.stack([np.nanmedian(q[:, 1 + 4 * k], axis=0) for k in range(5)]))\n        length.append(np.stack([[np.nanmedian(np.linalg.norm(q[:, 1 + 4 * k + j + 1] - q[:, 1 + 4 * k + j], axis=-1)) for j in range(3)] for k in range(5)]))\n    if base:\n        spec.finger_base, spec.finger_len = np.mean(base, 0), np.mean(length, 0)\n        spec.finger_base[2, 0] = 0.0                                      # the middle finger defines the forward axis: x = 0 by definition\n    return spec\n\n\ndef hand_frame(hand_pts: np.ndarray, side: str) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Orthonormal basis of the hand from its landmarks. hand_pts (T, 21, 3) in avatar space -> B (T, 3, 3) with columns (s, f, n):\n    f = wrist -> middle-finger base, s = towards the thumb side (index base - little-finger base, made perpendicular to f),\n    n = palm normal (f x s for the left hand, s x f for the right hand). Degenerate frames (hand not tracked) give NaN.\"\"\"\n    wrist = hand_pts[:, 0]\n    f = hand_pts[:, 9] - wrist\n    s = hand_pts[:, 5] - hand_pts[:, 17]\n    bad = (np.linalg.norm(f, axis=-1) < 1e-4) | (np.linalg.norm(s, axis=-1) < 1e-4)\n    f = _unit(f)\n    s = _unit(s - (s * f).sum(-1, keepdims=True) * f)\n    n = np.cross(f, s) if side == \"Left\" else np.cross(s, f)\n    B = np.stack([s, f, n], axis=-1)\n    B[bad] = np.nan\n    return B\n\n\ndef hand_canonical(hand_pts: np.ndarray, side: str) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"hand landmarks (T, 21, 3) [or (T, 1, 21, 3)] in avatar space -> coordinates in the hand frame (x thumb side, y forward, z palm).\"\"\"\n    squeeze = hand_pts.ndim == 4\n    p = hand_pts[:, 0] if squeeze else hand_pts\n    B = hand_frame(p, side)\n    q = np.einsum(\"tji,tkj->tki\", B, p - p[:, :1])                       # q = B^T (p - wrist): coordinates in the hand frame\n    return q[:, None] if squeeze else q\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Skeleton:\n    names: List[str]\n    parent: List[int]\n    offset: np.ndarray                 # (J, 3) rest offset from the parent joint, avatar axes (all rest rotations are the identity)\n    end_site: Dict[str, np.ndarray]    # name of a fingertip joint -> offset of its end (the fingertip)\n    index: Dict[str, int]\n\n\ndef build_skeleton(spec: AvatarSpec) -> Skeleton:\n    \"\"\"Humanoid upper body in a T-pose with Unity-style bone names: Hips, Spine, Chest, Neck, Head, then for each side\n    Shoulder, UpperArm, LowerArm, Hand and 3 phalanges per finger. Head, spine and shoulders are not animated (identity).\"\"\"\n    names, parent, offs, ends = [], [], [], {}\n\n    def add(name, par, off):\n        names.append(name)\n        parent.append(-1 if par is None else names.index(par))\n        offs.append(np.asarray(off, float))\n\n    add(\"Hips\", None, (0, -0.80, 0))\n    add(\"Spine\", \"Hips\", (0, 0.40, 0))\n    add(\"Chest\", \"Spine\", (0, 0.40, 0))                       # the chest is at the origin = shoulder mid-point\n    add(\"Neck\", \"Chest\", (0, 0.12, 0))\n    add(\"Head\", \"Neck\", (0, 0.18, 0))\n    for side, sgn in ((\"Left\", 1.0), (\"Right\", -1.0)):\n        add(f\"{side}Shoulder\", \"Chest\", (sgn * 0.2, 0, 0))\n        add(f\"{side}UpperArm\", f\"{side}Shoulder\", (sgn * 0.3, 0, 0))      # shoulder joint at +-0.5 = half a shoulder width\n        add(f\"{side}LowerArm\", f\"{side}UpperArm\", (sgn * spec.upper_arm, 0, 0))\n        add(f\"{side}Hand\", f\"{side}LowerArm\", (sgn * spec.forearm, 0, 0))\n        B = HAND_REST_BASIS[side]\n        for k, fn in enumerate(FINGERS):\n            rest, L = spec.finger_rest[k], spec.finger_len[k]\n            add(f\"{side}{fn}Proximal\", f\"{side}Hand\", B @ spec.finger_base[k])\n            add(f\"{side}{fn}Intermediate\", f\"{side}{fn}Proximal\", B @ (L[0] * rest))\n            add(f\"{side}{fn}Distal\", f\"{side}{fn}Intermediate\", B @ (L[1] * rest))\n            ends[f\"{side}{fn}Distal\"] = B @ (L[2] * rest)\n    return Skeleton(names, parent, np.stack(offs), ends, {n: i for i, n in enumerate(names)})\n\n\ndef forward_kinematics(local_rot: np.ndarray, skel: Skeleton):\n    \"\"\"local_rot (T, J, 3, 3) -> (global rotations (T, J, 3, 3), joint positions (T, J, 3), fingertip positions {name: (T, 3)}).\"\"\"\n    T, J = local_rot.shape[:2]\n    G, P = np.zeros((T, J, 3, 3)), np.zeros((T, J, 3))\n    for j in range(J):                                         # parents always come before their children\n        p = skel.parent[j]\n        if p < 0:\n            G[:, j], P[:, j] = local_rot[:, j], skel.offset[j]\n        else:\n            G[:, j] = G[:, p] @ local_rot[:, j]\n            P[:, j] = P[:, p] + G[:, p] @ skel.offset[j]\n    tips = {n: P[:, skel.index[n]] + G[:, skel.index[n]] @ off for n, off in skel.end_site.items()}\n    return G, P, tips","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-18T00:53:17.576225Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-18T00:53:17.576577Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-18T00:53:18.204814Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-18T00:53:17.576554Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-18T00:53:18.203988Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":39},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Avatar retargeting, part 2: arm IK, hand frame, finger IK -> local bone rotations\ndef _rx(a: float) -> np.ndarray:                  # fast scalar rotations used inside the finger solver\n    c, s = math.cos(a), math.sin(a)\n    return np.array([[1, 0, 0], [0, c, -s], [0, s, c]])\n\n\ndef _rz(a: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    c, s = math.cos(a), math.sin(a)\n    return np.array([[c, -s, 0], [s, c, 0], [0, 0, 1]])\n\n\ndef finger_fk(theta: np.ndarray, base: np.ndarray, lens: np.ndarray, rest: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Forward kinematics of one finger in the hand frame. theta = (MCP flexion, MCP abduction, PIP flexion, DIP flexion).\n    Returns the positions of the 2nd joint, the 3rd joint and the fingertip, shape (3, 3).\"\"\"\n    R1 = _rz(theta[1]) @ _rx(theta[0])             # first joint: flexion (curl towards the palm), then abduction (spread)\n    R2 = R1 @ _rx(theta[2])                        # second and third joints: hinges (flexion only)\n    R3 = R2 @ _rx(theta[3])\n    p1 = base + lens[0] * (R1 @ rest)\n    p2 = p1 + lens[1] * (R2 @ rest)\n    return np.stack([p1, p2, p2 + lens[2] * (R3 @ rest)])\n\n\ndef solve_finger(target: np.ndarray, base, lens, rest, lo, hi, x0) -> Tuple[np.ndarray, float]:\n    \"\"\"INVERSE KINEMATICS of one finger: the 4 joint angles, inside their limits, whose joints / fingertip are closest to `target` (3, 3).\n    Bounded least squares, started from the previous frame (x0) so the solution stays continuous; if that start does not give a good\n    fit it is retried from a straight and from a half-bent finger. A target that violates the joint limits (e.g. a finger bent\n    backwards, or a bend sideways at the last two joints) is projected onto the nearest reachable pose: this is the constraint step.\"\"\"\n    f = lambda th: (finger_fk(th, base, lens, rest) - target).ravel()\n    best = None\n    for init in (x0, np.zeros(4), 0.5 * (lo + hi)):\n        r = least_squares(f, np.clip(init, lo + 1e-6, hi - 1e-6), bounds=(lo, hi), xtol=1e-9, ftol=1e-9, gtol=1e-9)\n        if best is None or r.cost < best.cost:\n            best = r\n        if best.cost < 1e-9:\n            break\n    return best.x, float(best.cost)\n\n\ndef two_bone_ik(shoulder: np.ndarray, wrist_target: np.ndarray, elbow_hint: np.ndarray, l1: float, l2: float):\n    \"\"\"Analytic two-bone IK (law of cosines). Bones of length l1 (upper arm) and l2 (forearm) starting at `shoulder` (3,) must reach\n    `wrist_target` (T, 3); the elbow lies on a circle around the shoulder-wrist axis, and `elbow_hint` (T, 3) (the observed elbow)\n    chooses the point of the circle (the 'pole'). A target that is too far is pulled back to the full extension of the arm.\n    Returns (elbow (T, 3), reachable wrist (T, 3)).\"\"\"\n    u = wrist_target - shoulder\n    d = np.clip(np.linalg.norm(u, axis=-1), abs(l1 - l2) + 1e-4, l1 + l2 - 1e-4)\n    u = _unit(u)\n    a = (l1 ** 2 - l2 ** 2 + d ** 2) / (2 * d)                       # distance from the shoulder to the foot of the elbow\n    h = np.sqrt(np.maximum(l1 ** 2 - a ** 2, 0.0))                   # elbow height above the shoulder-wrist axis\n    v = elbow_hint - shoulder\n    v = v - (v * u).sum(-1, keepdims=True) * u                       # observed elbow direction, perpendicular to the axis\n    weak = np.linalg.norm(v, axis=-1) < 1e-4                         # arm almost straight: the hint says nothing -> elbow down / back\n    if weak.any():\n        dflt = np.array([0.0, -1.0, -0.2])\n        v[weak] = (dflt - (dflt * u[weak]).sum(-1, keepdims=True) * u[weak])\n    v = _unit(v)\n    return shoulder + a[:, None] * u + h[:, None] * v, shoulder + d[:, None] * u\n\n\ndef retarget_sequence(seq: np.ndarray, spec: AvatarSpec, skel: Optional[Skeleton] = None, mirrored: Optional[bool] = None,\n                      arm_scale: float = 1.0) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Landmarks -> bone rotations of the avatar skeleton.\n\n    seq (T, NODES, 3): x, y, z in landmark space (shoulder widths). For clips without z, add one first (`as_xyz`: depth lifter or flat).\n\n    Per arm:   the wrist target (relative to the shoulder, scaled by `arm_scale`) is reached with analytic two-bone IK, so the hand\n               lands where the sign needs it (e.g. on the forehead) even if the avatar's arms are not as long as the signer's.\n               Upper arm / forearm rotations are the shortest arcs from the T-pose direction to the new bone direction.\n    Hand:      full 3-D orientation from the palm landmarks (wrist, index / middle / little finger base). The roll about the forearm\n               axis is shared between forearm (`spec.twist_share`) and wrist, as in a real arm.\n    Fingers:   bone directions measured in the hand frame become targets for `solve_finger` (IK with joint limits).\n    Returns dict(local (T, J, 3, 3) rotation of every joint relative to its parent, skeleton, mirrored, finger_cost (T, 2, 5)).\"\"\"\n    assert seq.shape[-1] == 3, \"retarget_sequence needs x, y, z\"\n    skel = skel or build_skeleton(spec)\n    mirrored = detect_mirrored(seq) if mirrored is None else mirrored\n    av = to_avatar_space(seq, mirrored)\n    T, J = len(av), len(skel.names)\n    local = np.tile(np.eye(3), (T, J, 1, 1))\n    cost = np.zeros((T, 2, 5))\n    ix = skel.index\n    for si, (side, sgn, S, E, W, hand) in enumerate(((\"Left\", 1.0, P_LS, P_LE, P_LW, LH), (\"Right\", -1.0, P_RS, P_RE, P_RW, RH))):\n        rest = np.array([sgn, 0.0, 0.0])                                         # direction of the arm bones in the T-pose\n        shoulder = skel.offset[ix[f\"{side}Shoulder\"]] + skel.offset[ix[f\"{side}UpperArm\"]]   # chest = origin\n        # ---- arm: two-bone IK for the elbow, shortest-arc rotations for the bones ----\n        elbow, wrist = two_bone_ik(shoulder, shoulder + arm_scale * (av[:, W] - av[:, S]), shoulder + arm_scale * (av[:, E] - av[:, S]),\n                                   spec.upper_arm, spec.forearm)\n        R1 = swing(rest, elbow - shoulder)                                       # upper arm (global = local: the parent is the identity)\n        R2s = swing(rest, wrist - elbow)                                         # forearm direction, without roll\n        # ---- hand orientation from the palm landmarks ----\n        B_rest = HAND_REST_BASIS[side]\n        B = hand_frame(av[:, hand], side)\n        lost = np.isnan(B).any(axis=(1, 2))                                      # hand not tracked: keep it in line with the forearm\n        R_hand = np.where(lost[:, None, None], R2s, np.nan_to_num(B) @ B_rest.T)\n        # ---- roll: how much the hand is turned about the forearm axis relative to the forearm's own swing ----\n        q = Rot.from_matrix(R2s.transpose(0, 2, 1) @ R_hand).as_quat()           # (x, y, z, w)\n        roll = 2.0 * np.arctan2(q[:, :3] @ rest, q[:, 3])\n        roll = (roll + np.pi) % (2 * np.pi) - np.pi                              # wrap to (-pi, pi]\n        R2 = R2s @ axis_rot(rest, spec.twist_share * roll)                       # forearm takes its share of the roll\n        local[:, ix[f\"{side}UpperArm\"]] = R1\n        local[:, ix[f\"{side}LowerArm\"]] = R1.transpose(0, 2, 1) @ R2\n        local[:, ix[f\"{side}Hand\"]] = R2.transpose(0, 2, 1) @ R_hand\n        # ---- fingers: IK in the hand frame ----\n        q_hand = hand_canonical(av[:, hand][:, None], side)[:, 0]                # (T, 21, 3)\n        for k, fn in enumerate(FINGERS):\n            b, prev = 1 + 4 * k, np.zeros(4)\n            ang = np.zeros((T, 4))\n            for t in range(T):\n                if lost[t]:\n                    ang[t] = prev\n                    continue\n                d = _unit(q_hand[t, b + 1:b + 4] - q_hand[t, b:b + 3])           # observed directions of the 3 phalanges\n                p1 = spec.finger_base[k] + spec.finger_len[k, 0] * d[0]          # targets: walk along them with the AVATAR's bone lengths\n                p2 = p1 + spec.finger_len[k, 1] * d[1]\n                target = np.stack([p1, p2, p2 + spec.finger_len[k, 2] * d[2]])\n                ang[t], cost[t, si, k] = solve_finger(target, spec.finger_base[k], spec.finger_len[k], spec.finger_rest[k],\n                                                      FINGER_LO[k], FINGER_HI[k], prev)\n                prev = ang[t]\n            # canonical rotations -> rotations in the avatar's rest-aligned axes:  R_world = B_rest R_canonical B_rest^T\n            ax = lambda R: B_rest @ R @ B_rest.T\n            local[:, ix[f\"{side}{fn}Proximal\"]] = ax(axis_rot(np.array([0, 0, 1.0]), ang[:, 1]) @ axis_rot(np.array([1.0, 0, 0]), ang[:, 0]))\n            local[:, ix[f\"{side}{fn}Intermediate\"]] = ax(axis_rot(np.array([1.0, 0, 0]), ang[:, 2]))\n            local[:, ix[f\"{side}{fn}Distal\"]] = ax(axis_rot(np.array([1.0, 0, 0]), ang[:, 3]))\n    return dict(local=local, skeleton=skel, mirrored=mirrored, finger_cost=cost)\n\n\ndef avatar_landmarks(local: np.ndarray, skel: Skeleton) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Forward kinematics -> positions of the avatar's joints arranged like our landmark nodes, in AVATAR space (T, NODES, 3):\n    shoulders / elbows / wrists and the 21 points of each hand. Face nodes are NaN. Used to check and to draw the retargeted motion.\"\"\"\n    _, P, tips = forward_kinematics(local, skel)\n    out = np.full((len(local), NUM_NODES, 3), np.nan)\n    for side, sl, (ps, pe, pw) in ((\"Left\", LH, (P_LS, P_LE, P_LW)), (\"Right\", RH, (P_RS, P_RE, P_RW))):\n        i = skel.index\n        out[:, ps], out[:, pe], out[:, pw] = P[:, i[f\"{side}UpperArm\"]], P[:, i[f\"{side}LowerArm\"]], P[:, i[f\"{side}Hand\"]]\n        out[:, sl.start] = P[:, i[f\"{side}Hand\"]]\n        for k, fn in enumerate(FINGERS):\n            for j, ph in enumerate(PHALANGES):\n                out[:, sl.start + 1 + 4 * k + j] = P[:, i[f\"{side}{fn}{ph}\"]]\n            out[:, sl.start + 4 + 4 * k] = tips[f\"{side}{fn}Distal\"]\n    return out\n\n\ndef as_xyz(seq: np.ndarray, lifter: Optional[\"DepthLifter\"] = None, device: str = \"cpu\") -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"(T, NODES, D) -> (T, NODES, 3). D == 3: unchanged. D == 2: the depth comes from the depth lifter, or is 0 if there is none\n    (a flat avatar: arms and hand orientation are then only right in the image plane, and curled fingers look shorter instead of bent).\"\"\"\n    if seq.shape[-1] == 3:\n        return seq\n    if lifter is not None:\n        return lift_depth(lifter, seq, device)\n    return np.concatenate([seq, np.zeros(seq.shape[:-1] + (1,))], axis=-1)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-18T00:53:18.205971Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-18T00:53:18.206525Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-18T00:53:18.234142Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-18T00:53:18.20649Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-18T00:53:18.233485Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":40},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Avatar export: bone names, BVH, JSON (quaternions + face blend-shapes), drawing\ndef bone_name(name: str, style: str = \"unity\") -> str:\n    \"\"\"Our (Unity HumanBodyBones) bone name -> the naming of another rig: \"unity\" (unchanged), \"vrm\" (leftUpperArm, ...), \"mixamo\".\"\"\"\n    if style == \"unity\":\n        return name\n    if style == \"vrm\":\n        return name[0].lower() + name[1:]\n    if style == \"mixamo\":\n        base = {\"Hips\": \"Hips\", \"Spine\": \"Spine\", \"Chest\": \"Spine1\", \"Neck\": \"Neck\", \"Head\": \"Head\"}\n        for side in (\"Left\", \"Right\"):\n            if name.startswith(side):\n                rest = name[len(side):]\n                if rest in (\"Shoulder\", \"Hand\"):\n                    return f\"mixamorig:{side}{rest}\"\n                if rest in (\"UpperArm\", \"LowerArm\"):\n                    return f\"mixamorig:{side}{'Arm' if rest == 'UpperArm' else 'ForeArm'}\"\n                for fn in FINGERS:\n                    if rest.startswith(fn):\n                        return f\"mixamorig:{side}Hand{fn}{PHALANGES.index(rest[len(fn):]) + 1}\"\n        return \"mixamorig:\" + base[name]\n    raise ValueError(f\"unknown style {style!r}\")\n\n\ndef write_bvh(path, local: np.ndarray, skel: Skeleton, fps: float, style: str = \"unity\") -> Path:\n    \"\"\"Write the animation as a BVH file (the usual motion-capture exchange format; Blender, Unity, MotionBuilder, ... import it).\n    Rotation channels are \"Zrotation Xrotation Yrotation\" (degrees); only the root has position channels (it never moves).\"\"\"\n    T, J = local.shape[:2]\n    eul = Rot.from_matrix(local.reshape(-1, 3, 3)).as_euler(\"ZXY\", degrees=True).reshape(T, J, 3)   # intrinsic ZXY: R = Rz Rx Ry\n    kids = [[j for j in range(J) if skel.parent[j] == i] for i in range(J)]\n    lines, order = [\"HIERARCHY\"], []\n\n    def emit(j: int, depth: int):\n        pad = \"  \" * depth\n        order.append(j)\n        o = skel.offset[j]\n        lines.append(f\"{pad}{'ROOT' if skel.parent[j] < 0 else 'JOINT'} {bone_name(skel.names[j], style)}\")\n        lines.append(f\"{pad}{{\")\n        lines.append(f\"{pad}  OFFSET {o[0]:.6f} {o[1]:.6f} {o[2]:.6f}\")\n        lines.append(f\"{pad}  CHANNELS \" + (\"6 Xposition Yposition Zposition \" if skel.parent[j] < 0 else \"3 \") + \"Zrotation Xrotation Yrotation\")\n        for c in kids[j]:\n            emit(c, depth + 1)\n        if not kids[j]:                                                         # leaf: head or fingertip\n            e = skel.end_site.get(skel.names[j], np.array([0.0, 0.2, 0.0]))\n            lines.extend([f\"{pad}  End Site\", f\"{pad}  {{\", f\"{pad}    OFFSET {e[0]:.6f} {e[1]:.6f} {e[2]:.6f}\", f\"{pad}  }}\"])\n        lines.append(f\"{pad}}}\")\n\n    emit(0, 0)\n    lines += [\"MOTION\", f\"Frames: {T}\", f\"Frame Time: {1.0 / fps:.6f}\"]\n    root = skel.offset[0]\n    for t in range(T):\n        vals = [*root] + [v for j in order for v in eul[t, j]]\n        lines.append(\" \".join(f\"{v:.5f}\" for v in vals))\n    path = Path(path)\n    path.write_text(\"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\")\n    return path\n\n\ndef export_avatar_json(path, local: np.ndarray, skel: Skeleton, fps: float, blend: Optional[Dict[str, np.ndarray]] = None,\n                       meta: Optional[dict] = None, style: str = \"unity\") -> Path:\n    \"\"\"JSON for game engines / web viewers: the skeleton (names, parents, rest offsets), the local rotation of every bone in every frame\n    as a quaternion (x, y, z, w), the face blend-shape weights, and the coordinate conventions.\"\"\"\n    quat = Rot.from_matrix(local.reshape(-1, 3, 3)).as_quat().reshape(*local.shape[:2], 4)\n    obj = {\"format\": \"asl-avatar-motion/1\", \"fps\": fps,\n           \"coordinate_system\": \"right-handed; +X = avatar's left, +Y up, +Z = direction the avatar faces; unit = shoulder width; \"\n                                \"convert the handedness / scale when importing into a left-handed engine (e.g. Unity: x -> -x)\",\n           \"rotations\": \"local rotation of every bone relative to its parent, quaternion (x, y, z, w); rest pose = T-pose = all identity\",\n           \"bones\": [{\"name\": bone_name(n, style), \"parent\": None if skel.parent[i] < 0 else bone_name(skel.names[skel.parent[i]], style),\n                      \"rest_offset\": [round(float(v), 5) for v in skel.offset[i]]} for i, n in enumerate(skel.names)],\n           \"frames\": np.round(quat, 5).tolist(),\n           \"blendshapes\": {k: np.round(np.asarray(v), 4).tolist() for k, v in (blend or {}).items()},\n           \"meta\": meta or {}}\n    path = Path(path)\n    path.write_text(json.dumps(obj))\n    return path\n\n\ndef read_bvh_positions(path) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Tiny BVH reader used to CHECK an exported file: returns the joint positions (T, J, 3) computed from the file alone\n    (joints in file order). Not a general parser: it expects the files written by `write_bvh`.\"\"\"\n    text = Path(path).read_text().splitlines()\n    names, parent, offs, chan, stack, i = [], [], [], [], [], 0\n    while text[i].strip() != \"MOTION\":\n        tok = text[i].split()\n        if tok and tok[0] in (\"ROOT\", \"JOINT\"):\n            names.append(tok[1])\n            parent.append(stack[-1] if stack else -1)\n            stack.append(len(names) - 1)\n        elif tok and tok[0] == \"OFFSET\" and len(offs) < len(names):\n            offs.append(np.array(tok[1:4], float))\n        elif tok and tok[0] == \"End\":                                   # skip the End Site block (4 lines)\n            i += 3\n        elif tok == [\"}\"]:\n            stack.pop()\n        i += 1\n    frames = int(text[i + 1].split()[1])\n    data = np.array([[float(v) for v in ln.split()] for ln in text[i + 3:i + 3 + frames]])\n    J = len(names)\n    root, ang = data[:, :3], data[:, 3:].reshape(frames, J, 3)\n    G = Rot.from_euler(\"ZXY\", ang.reshape(-1, 3), degrees=True).as_matrix().reshape(frames, J, 3, 3)\n    P = np.zeros((frames, J, 3))\n    for j in range(J):\n        if parent[j] < 0:\n            P[:, j] = root\n        else:\n            G[:, j] = G[:, parent[j]] @ G[:, j]\n            P[:, j] = P[:, parent[j]] + G[:, parent[j]] @ offs[j]\n    return P\n\n\ndef draw_avatar(ax, local_frame: np.ndarray, skel: Skeleton, view: str = \"front\"):\n    \"\"\"Draw one frame (J, 3, 3) of the avatar's skeleton by forward kinematics. view = 'front' (x, y) or 'side' (z, y).\"\"\"\n    _, P, tips = forward_kinematics(local_frame[None], skel)\n    P = P[0]\n    cols = {\"Left\": \"tab:blue\", \"Right\": \"tab:red\"}\n    ax_i = (0, 1) if view == \"front\" else (2, 1)\n    for j, p in enumerate(skel.parent):\n        if p >= 0:\n            side = next((s for s in cols if skel.names[j].startswith(s)), None)\n            ax.plot(P[[p, j], ax_i[0]], P[[p, j], ax_i[1]], \"-\", color=cols.get(side, \"k\"), lw=1.2)\n    for n, t in tips.items():\n        j = skel.index[n]\n        ax.plot([P[j, ax_i[0]], t[0, ax_i[0]]], [P[j, ax_i[1]], t[0, ax_i[1]]], \"-\", color=cols[n[:4] if n.startswith(\"Left\") else n[:5]], lw=1.2)\n    ax.set_aspect(\"equal\")\n    ax.axis(\"off\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-18T00:53:18.236025Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-18T00:53:18.236339Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-18T00:53:18.263161Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-18T00:53:18.236308Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-18T00:53:18.262576Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":41},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### ▶ Fit the avatar proportions to the data and retarget one generated clip\n1. Arm and finger proportions are measured on real train clips (`fit_avatar_spec`; replace them with your character's numbers if you have them).\n2. One generated, smoothed clip is converted to real-time frames (section 8), given a depth (depth lifter), retargeted, and drawn: grey = the\n   input landmarks, colours = the avatar's skeleton after forward kinematics.\n3. Checks: the avatar's wrists must be where the signer's wrists are (arm IK), the fingertips close to the observed ones, and the exported BVH must\n   describe exactly the same motion as the rotations in memory.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# 1) avatar proportions from real train clips (x, y AND z are in the cache)\nxy_r, z_r, p_r = load_xyz(splits[\"train\"], cache_path, 1500, seed=0)\nreal3d = np.concatenate([xy_r, z_r[..., None]], axis=-1)\nis_mirrored = detect_mirrored(real3d.reshape(-1, NUM_NODES, 3))\nspec = fit_avatar_spec(real3d, p_r, is_mirrored)\nskel = build_skeleton(spec)\nprint(f\"data are mirrored: {is_mirrored} | upper arm {spec.upper_arm:.3f}, forearm {spec.forearm:.3f} shoulder widths | \"\n      f\"middle finger bones {np.round(spec.finger_len[2], 3)} | {len(skel.names)} bones\")\n\n# 2) one generated clip -> smoothed -> real-time frames -> 3-D -> bone rotations\nword = vocab.decode(int(arrs[\"words\"][0]) + 1)\nclip, sec = arrs[\"gen_seq\"][arrs[\"gen_labels\"] == arrs[\"words\"][0]][0], (arrs[\"gen_seconds\"][arrs[\"gen_labels\"] == arrs[\"words\"][0]][0] if arrs.get(\"gen_seconds\") is not None else 1.5)\nclip = smooth_sequence(clip, effective_fps(len(clip), sec), cfg.smooth_min_cutoff, cfg.smooth_beta, cfg.smooth_d_cutoff) if cfg.smooth else clip\nclip30 = resample_to_duration(clip, sec, 30.0)\nxyz = as_xyz(clip30, lifter, device)                       # depth from the lifter (or the model's own z if cfg.use_z)\nt0 = time.time()\nanim = retarget_sequence(xyz, spec, skel)\nprint(f\"retargeted {len(xyz)} frames of '{word}' in {time.time() - t0:.1f} s\")\n\n# 3) checks\nfk_lm = from_avatar_space(avatar_landmarks(anim[\"local\"], skel), anim[\"mirrored\"])\nwrist_err = np.linalg.norm(fk_lm[:, [P_LW, P_RW]] - xyz[:, [P_LW, P_RW]], axis=-1)\ntip_err = np.stack([np.linalg.norm(fk_lm[:, sl.start + 4 + 4 * k] - xyz[:, sl.start + 4 + 4 * k], axis=-1) for sl in (LH, RH) for k in range(5)])\nprint(f\"wrist error (avatar vs signer): mean {wrist_err.mean():.3f}, max {wrist_err.max():.3f} shoulder widths\")\nprint(f\"fingertip error: mean {np.nanmean(tip_err):.3f} shoulder widths (limited by the finger joint limits and by the depth quality)\")\n\n# 4) picture: landmarks (grey) vs avatar (colour), front and side view\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 5, figsize=(13, 5.4))\nfor k, t in enumerate(np.linspace(0, len(xyz) - 1, 5).astype(int)):\n    for row, view in enumerate((\"front\", \"side\")):\n        ax = axes[row, k]\n        av_in = to_avatar_space(xyz[t], anim[\"mirrored\"])\n        ci = (0, 1) if view == \"front\" else (2, 1)\n        ax.plot(av_in[:42, ci[0]], av_in[:42, ci[1]], \".\", color=\"0.6\", ms=2)\n        ax.plot(av_in[42:48, ci[0]], av_in[42:48, ci[1]], \"o\", color=\"0.6\", ms=3)\n        draw_avatar(ax, anim[\"local\"][t], skel, view)\n        ax.set_title(f\"{view}, {t / 30:.2f} s\", fontsize=8)\nplt.suptitle(f\"'{word}': input landmarks (grey) vs avatar skeleton (blue = left side, red = right side)\")\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()\n\n# 5) export: BVH + JSON (+ face blend-shapes), and check the BVH against the rotations in memory\nbs = face_blendshapes(clip30, face_ref) if FACE_PRESET == \"expressive\" else None\nbvh = write_bvh(Path(cfg.work_dir) / f\"avatar_{word}.bvh\", anim[\"local\"], skel, 30.0)\njs = export_avatar_json(Path(cfg.work_dir) / f\"avatar_{word}.json\", anim[\"local\"], skel, 30.0, bs, {\"word\": word, \"seconds\": float(sec)})\nerr = np.abs(read_bvh_positions(bvh) - forward_kinematics(anim[\"local\"], skel)[1]).max()\nprint(f\"saved {bvh.name} and {js.name} | BVH re-read vs rotations in memory: max joint position difference {err:.1e}\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-18T00:53:18.264327Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-18T00:53:18.264644Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-18T00:53:26.302848Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-18T00:53:18.264622Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-18T00:53:26.302169Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"data are mirrored: False | upper arm 0.908, forearm 1.350 shoulder widths | middle finger bones [0.166 0.088 0.064] | 43 bones\nretargeted 18 frames of 'after' in 6.0 s\nwrist error (avatar vs signer): mean 0.885, max 1.922 shoulder widths\nfingertip error: mean 2.192 shoulder widths (limited by the finger joint limits and by the depth quality)\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1300x540 with 10 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"name":"stdout","text":"saved avatar_after.bvh and avatar_after.json | BVH re-read vs rotations in memory: max joint position difference 1.1e-06\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":42},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### ▶ `sign_word`: word → generated, smoothed, retargeted motion (+ files)\nOne call does the whole chain: generation (with the duration prior or a duration you give), One Euro smoothing, real-time resampling, depth,\nretargeting, export, and an animation next to the avatar skeleton. Change the word (`vocab.itos[1:]` lists them all) and, if you like, the duration.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"from matplotlib.animation import FuncAnimation\nfrom IPython.display import HTML\n\n\ndef sign_word(word: str, seconds: Optional[float] = None, guidance: Optional[float] = None, steps: Optional[int] = None, seed: int = 0,\n              animate: bool = True, export: bool = True) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"word -> motion for an avatar. seconds=None: duration drawn from the word's prior. Saves `avatar_<word>.bvh` and\n    `avatar_<word>.json` in work_dir. Returns dict(landmarks (T', NODES, 3), rotations (T', J, 3, 3), seconds, files).\"\"\"\n    word = SignVocab.normalize(word)\n    if word not in vocab.stoi:\n        raise ValueError(f\"unknown word '{word}'. Examples: {vocab.itos[1:12]} ... (all: vocab.itos[1:])\")\n    clips, secs = generate(ema.module, diffusion, vocab, [word], stats, T, C, dur_prior if cfg.use_duration else None, n_per_word=1,\n                           steps=steps or cfg.gen_steps, guidance=guidance or cfg.guidance, device=device, seed=seed, duration_s=seconds)\n    seq, sec = clips[word][0], float(secs[word][0])\n    sec = sec if np.isfinite(sec) else 1.5\n    if cfg.smooth:\n        seq = smooth_sequence(seq, effective_fps(len(seq), sec), cfg.smooth_min_cutoff, cfg.smooth_beta, cfg.smooth_d_cutoff)\n    seq30 = resample_to_duration(seq, sec, 30.0)                      # real-time frames at 30 fps\n    xyz = as_xyz(seq30, lifter, device)\n    out = retarget_sequence(xyz, spec, skel)\n    files = {}\n    if export:\n        bs = face_blendshapes(seq30, face_ref) if FACE_PRESET == \"expressive\" else None\n        files = {\"bvh\": write_bvh(Path(cfg.work_dir) / f\"avatar_{word}.bvh\", out[\"local\"], skel, 30.0),\n                 \"json\": export_avatar_json(Path(cfg.work_dir) / f\"avatar_{word}.json\", out[\"local\"], skel, 30.0, bs,\n                                            {\"word\": word, \"seconds\": sec, \"seed\": seed})}\n        print(f\"'{word}': {sec:.2f} s, {len(seq30)} frames at 30 fps -> {files['bvh'].name}, {files['json'].name}\")\n    if animate:\n        lo, hi = np.percentile(seq30[..., :2].reshape(-1, 2), 0.5, axis=0), np.percentile(seq30[..., :2].reshape(-1, 2), 99.5, axis=0)\n        fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(7, 3.6))\n\n        def draw(t):\n            for ax in axes:\n                ax.clear()\n            _draw_frame(axes[0], seq30[t])\n            axes[0].set_xlim(lo[0], hi[0])\n            axes[0].set_ylim(hi[1], lo[1])\n            axes[0].set_aspect(\"equal\")\n            axes[0].axis(\"off\")\n            axes[0].set_title(f\"generated landmarks  '{word}'\", fontsize=8)\n            draw_avatar(axes[1], out[\"local\"][t], skel, \"front\")\n            axes[1].set_xlim(-1.6, 1.6)\n            axes[1].set_ylim(-1.2, 1.6)\n            axes[1].set_title(\"avatar skeleton (front)\", fontsize=8)\n\n        anim = FuncAnimation(fig, draw, frames=len(seq30), interval=1000 / 30)\n        plt.close(fig)\n        display(HTML(anim.to_jshtml()))\n    return dict(landmarks=xyz, rotations=out[\"local\"], seconds=sec, files=files)\n\n\n_ = sign_word(\"thirsty\" if \"thirsty\" in vocab.stoi else vocab.itos[1])          # change the word here","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-18T00:53:26.303775Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-18T00:53:26.304105Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-18T00:53:37.846688Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-18T00:53:26.304084Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-18T00:53:37.845867Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"'thirsty': 0.82 s, 25 frames at 30 fps -> avatar_thirsty.bvh, avatar_thirsty.json\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<IPython.core.display.HTML object>","text/html":"\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\"\nhref=\"https://maxcdn.bootstrapcdn.com/font-awesome/4.4.0/css/font-awesome.min.css\">\n<script language=\"javascript\">\n  function isInternetExplorer() {\n    ua = navigator.userAgent;\n    /* MSIE used to detect old browsers and Trident used to newer ones*/\n    return ua.indexOf(\"MSIE \") > -1 || ua.indexOf(\"Trident/\") > -1;\n  }\n\n  /* Define the Animation class */\n  function Animation(frames, img_id, slider_id, interval, loop_select_id){\n    this.img_id = img_id;\n    this.slider_id = slider_id;\n    this.loop_select_id = loop_select_id;\n    this.interval = interval;\n    this.current_frame = 0;\n    this.direction = 0;\n    this.timer = null;\n    this.frames = new Array(frames.length);\n\n    for (var i=0; i<frames.length; i++)\n    {\n     this.frames[i] = new Image();\n     this.frames[i].src = frames[i];\n    }\n    var slider = document.getElementById(this.slider_id);\n    slider.max = this.frames.length - 1;\n    if (isInternetExplorer()) {\n        // switch from oninput to onchange because IE <= 11 does not conform\n        // with W3C specification. It ignores oninput and onchange behaves\n        // like oninput. In contrast, Microsoft Edge behaves correctly.\n        slider.setAttribute('onchange', slider.getAttribute('oninput'));\n        slider.setAttribute('oninput', null);\n    }\n    this.set_frame(this.current_frame);\n  }\n\n  Animation.prototype.get_loop_state = function(){\n    var button_group = document[this.loop_select_id].state;\n    for (var i = 0; i < button_group.length; i++) {\n        var button = button_group[i];\n        if (button.checked) {\n            return button.value;\n        }\n    }\n    return undefined;\n  }\n\n  Animation.prototype.set_frame = function(frame){\n    this.current_frame = frame;\n    document.getElementById(this.img_id).src =\n            this.frames[this.current_frame].src;\n    document.getElementById(this.slider_id).value = this.current_frame;\n  }\n\n  Animation.prototype.next_frame = function()\n  {\n    this.set_frame(Math.min(this.frames.length - 1, this.current_frame + 1));\n  }\n\n  Animation.prototype.previous_frame = function()\n  {\n    this.set_frame(Math.max(0, this.current_frame - 1));\n  }\n\n  Animation.prototype.first_frame = function()\n  {\n    this.set_frame(0);\n  }\n\n  Animation.prototype.last_frame = function()\n  {\n    this.set_frame(this.frames.length - 1);\n  }\n\n  Animation.prototype.slower = function()\n  {\n    this.interval /= 0.7;\n    if(this.direction > 0){this.play_animation();}\n    else if(this.direction < 0){this.reverse_animation();}\n  }\n\n  Animation.prototype.faster = function()\n  {\n    this.interval *= 0.7;\n    if(this.direction > 0){this.play_animation();}\n    else if(this.direction < 0){this.reverse_animation();}\n  }\n\n  Animation.prototype.anim_step_forward = function()\n  {\n    this.current_frame += 1;\n    if(this.current_frame < this.frames.length){\n      this.set_frame(this.current_frame);\n    }else{\n      var loop_state = this.get_loop_state();\n      if(loop_state == \"loop\"){\n        this.first_frame();\n      }else if(loop_state == \"reflect\"){\n        this.last_frame();\n        this.reverse_animation();\n      }else{\n        this.pause_animation();\n        this.last_frame();\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  Animation.prototype.anim_step_reverse = function()\n  {\n    this.current_frame -= 1;\n    if(this.current_frame >= 0){\n      this.set_frame(this.current_frame);\n    }else{\n      var loop_state = this.get_loop_state();\n      if(loop_state == \"loop\"){\n        this.last_frame();\n      }else if(loop_state == \"reflect\"){\n        this.first_frame();\n        this.play_animation();\n      }else{\n        this.pause_animation();\n        this.first_frame();\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  Animation.prototype.pause_animation = function()\n  {\n