paired Wilcoxon test, the split by group and the accuracy per word. The recognition accuracy of\n**real** clips is the ceiling: a stick figure is hard to read even for experts, so judge the generated clips *relative to the real ones*.\n\n**Please note.** (1) The stick figure shows hands, arms and face, not a rendered avatar: re-run the evaluation with the avatar itself before\ndeploying it. (2) Pay and credit your raters, explain what the data will be used for, and do not collect more than you need. (3) The competition terms forbid using\nthe landmark data to identify individuals: keep the evaluation anonymous. (4) 20 words × 2 clips takes about 10 minutes per person; aim for at least\n10 participants per group you want to report on.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Human evaluation kit: blind rating page (HTML) + analysis of the answers\nEVAL_HTML = r\"\"\"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\">\n<title>ASL avatar rating</title>\n<style>\n body{font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;max-width:760px;margin:0 auto;padding:16px;line-height:1.45;color:#1b1b1b;background:#fff}\n @media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{background:#17171a;color:#eee}canvas{background:#222!important}input,select,textarea{background:#2a2a2e;color:#eee;border:1px solid #555}}\n canvas{width:100%;max-width:520px;height:auto;background:#f6f6f6;border-radius:8px;display:block;margin:8px auto}\n fieldset{border:1px solid #8884;border-radius:8px;margin:12px 0}\n label.r{margin-right:12px;white-space:nowrap}\n button{font-size:1rem;padding:8px 16px;border-radius:8px;border:1px solid #888;cursor:pointer}\n button:disabled{opacity:.4;cursor:default}\n input[type=text],select,textarea{font-size:1rem;padding:6px;width:100%;box-sizing:border-box}\n #bar{height:6px;background:#8883;border-radius:3px}#bar div{height:6px;background:#2a7;border-radius:3px;width:0}\n .small{font-size:.85rem;opacity:.8}\n</style></head><body>\n<div id=\"intro\">\n <h2>Rating generated sign language</h2>\n <p>You will see short stick-figure animations (hands, arms and face) of single ASL signs. Some come from real signers recorded by a camera,\n some were produced by a computer. <b>You are not told which is which.</b> For each animation please tell us which sign you think it is,\n how easy it is to understand and how natural the movement looks. It takes about __MINUTES__ minutes and you can stop at any time.</p>\n <p>The page runs in your browser: nothing is sent anywhere. At the end you download a small CSV file with your answers and send it back to the person who gave you this page.\n Please do not type your name: use any code you like.</p>\n <fieldset><legend>About you (optional, used only to compare groups)</legend>\n  <p><label>Participant code <input type=\"text\" id=\"pid\" placeholder=\"e.g. P07\"></label></p>\n  <p><label>How do you use ASL?\n   <select id=\"group\"><option value=\"\">(prefer not to say)</option><option>Deaf signer</option><option>Hearing native signer (e.g. child of Deaf parents)</option>\n   <option>Interpreter / teacher</option><option>ASL learner</option><option>Does not sign</option></select></label></p>\n  <p><label>Years of signing <input type=\"text\" id=\"years\" placeholder=\"e.g. 12\"></label></p>\n </fieldset>\n <p><label><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"consent\"> I understand the above and agree to take part.</label></p>\n <button id=\"start\" disabled>Start</button>\n</div>\n<div id=\"task\" hidden>\n <div id=\"bar\"><div></div></div><p class=\"small\" id=\"count\"></p>\n <canvas id=\"cv\" width=\"520\" height=\"520\"></canvas>\n <p style=\"text-align:center\"><button id=\"replay\">Replay</button></p>\n <fieldset><legend>1. Which sign is it?</legend>\n  <input type=\"text\" id=\"word\" list=\"words\" placeholder=\"start typing a word...\" autocomplete=\"off\">\n  <datalist id=\"words\"></datalist>\n  <p><label><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"cant\"> I cannot tell</label></p></fieldset>\n <fieldset><legend>2. How easy is it to understand?</legend>\n  <label class=\"r\">1 <input type=\"radio\" name=\"u\" value=\"1\"></label><label class=\"r\">2 <input type=\"radio\" name=\"u\" value=\"2\"></label>\n  <label class=\"r\">3 <input type=\"radio\" name=\"u\" value=\"3\"></label><label class=\"r\">4 <input type=\"radio\" name=\"u\" value=\"4\"></label>\n  <label class=\"r\">5 <input type=\"radio\" name=\"u\" value=\"5\"></label><span class=\"small\">(1 = impossible, 5 = perfectly clear)</span></fieldset>\n <fieldset><legend>3. How natural does the movement look?</legend>\n  <label class=\"r\">1 <input type=\"radio\" name=\"n\" value=\"1\"></label><label class=\"r\">2 <input type=\"radio\" name=\"n\" value=\"2\"></label>\n  <label class=\"r\">3 <input type=\"radio\" name=\"n\" value=\"3\"></label><label class=\"r\">4 <input type=\"radio\" name=\"n\" value=\"4\"></label>\n  <label class=\"r\">5 <input type=\"radio\" name=\"n\" value=\"5\"></label><span class=\"small\">(1 = robotic, 5 = like a real signer)</span></fieldset>\n <p><textarea id=\"comment\" rows=\"2\" placeholder=\"Optional comment (what looks wrong?)\"></textarea></p>\n <button id=\"next\" disabled>Next</button>\n</div>\n<div id=\"done\" hidden>\n <h2>Thank you!</h2>\n <p>Please download your answers and send the file back.</p>\n <p><button id=\"dl\">Download answers (CSV)</button></p>\n <p class=\"small\">If the download does not start, copy the text below into a file named <code>answers.csv</code>.</p>\n <textarea id=\"csv\" rows=\"6\" readonly></textarea>\n</div>\n<script>\nconst DATA = __DATA__;\nconst $ = id => document.getElementById(id);\nlet order = [], pos = 0, rows = [], frame = 0, timer = null, t0 = 0, replays = 0;\nfunction rng(seed){let a=seed>>>0;return()=>{a|=0;a=a+0x6D2B79F5|0;let t=Math.imul(a^a>>>15,1|a);t=t+Math.imul(t^t>>>7,61|t)^t;return((t^t>>>14)>>>0)/4294967296}}\nfunction hash(s){let h=2166136261;for(const c of s){h^=c.charCodeAt(0);h=Math.imul(h,16777619)}return h>>>0}\nDATA.words.forEach(w=>{const o=document.createElement(\"option\");o.value=w;$(\"words\").appendChild(o)});\n$(\"consent\").onchange=()=>{$(\"start\").disabled=!$(\"consent\").checked};\n$(\"start\").onclick=()=>{\n  const r=rng(hash($(\"pid\").value||\"anon\"));order=DATA.items.map((_,i)=>i);\n  for(let i=order.length-1;i>0;i--){const j=Math.floor(r()*(i+1));[order[i],order[j]]=[order[j],order[i]]}\n  $(\"intro\").hidden=true;$(\"task\").hidden=false;show();};\nfunction ready(){const u=document.querySelector('input[name=u]:checked'),n=document.querySelector('input[name=n]:checked');\n  $(\"next\").disabled=!(u&&n&&($(\"word\").value.trim()||$(\"cant\").checked))}\n[\"word\",\"cant\"].forEach(i=>$(i).oninput=ready);document.querySelectorAll(\"input[type=radio]\").forEach(e=>e.onchange=ready);\nfunction draw(item,f){\n  const cv=$(\"cv\"),ctx=cv.getContext(\"2d\"),L=DATA.layout,N=L.n,[x0,x1,y0,y1]=item.box;\n  const s=Math.min(cv.width/(x1-x0),cv.height/(y1-y0))*0.95,ox=(cv.width-(x1-x0)*s)/2,oy=(cv.height-(y1-y0)*s)/2;\n  const P=i=>[ox+(item.f[(f*N+i)*2]/1000-x0)*s,oy+(item.f[(f*N+i)*2+1]/1000-y0)*s];\n  ctx.clearRect(0,0,cv.width,cv.height);ctx.lineWidth=2;ctx.lineCap=\"round\";\n  const line=(a,b,c)=>{const p=P(a),q=P(b);ctx.strokeStyle=c;ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(p[0],p[1]);ctx.lineTo(q[0],q[1]);ctx.stroke()};\n  const dark=matchMedia(\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\").matches,ink=dark?\"#ddd\":\"#222\";\n  L.pose.forEach(e=>line(e[0],e[1],ink));\n  [[L.lh,\"#1f77b4\"],[L.rh,\"#d62728\"]].forEach(([st,c])=>L.hand.forEach(e=>line(st+e[0],st+e[1],c)));\n  L.face.forEach(g=>{for(let i=g.a;i<g.b-1;i++)line(i,i+1,g.c);if(g.loop)line(g.b-1,g.a,g.c);\n    if(!g.loop&&!g.line)for(let i=g.a;i<g.b;i++){const p=P(i);ctx.fillStyle=g.c;ctx.fillRect(p[0]-1.5,p[1]-1.5,3,3)}});\n}\nfunction play(){clearInterval(timer);const item=DATA.items[order[pos]];frame=0;\n  timer=setInterval(()=>{draw(item,frame);frame=(frame+1)%DATA.T;if(frame===0)replays++},Math.max(10,1000*item.seconds/DATA.T));}\n$(\"replay\").onclick=()=>{replays++;play()};\nfunction show(){const item=DATA.items[order[pos]];$(\"count\").textContent=`Animation ${pos+1} of ${order.length}`;\n  $(\"bar\").firstElementChild.style.width=(100*pos/order.length)+\"%\";\n  $(\"word\").value=\"\";$(\"cant\").checked=false;document.querySelectorAll(\"input[type=radio]\").forEach(e=>e.checked=false);$(\"comment\").value=\"\";\n  $(\"next\").disabled=true;t0=Date.now();replays=0;play();}\n$(\"next\").onclick=()=>{const item=DATA.items[order[pos]];\n  rows.push([$(\"pid\").value||\"anon\",$(\"group\").value,$(\"years\").value,item.id,$(\"word\").value.trim(),$(\"cant\").checked?1:0,\n    document.querySelector('input[name=u]:checked').value,document.querySelector('input[name=n]:checked').value,\n    ((Date.now()-t0)/1000).toFixed(1),replays,$(\"comment\").value.replace(/\\s+/g,\" \")]);\n  pos++;if(pos>=order.length){clearInterval(timer);$(\"task\").hidden=true;$(\"done\").hidden=false;finish()}else show();};\nfunction finish(){const head=\"participant,group,years,item_id,word_answer,cant_tell,understand,natural,seconds_spent,replays,comment\";\n  const q=v=>'\"'+String(v).replace(/\"/g,'\"\"')+'\"';const csv=[head,...rows.map(r=>r.map(q).join(\",\"))].join(\"\\n\");\n  $(\"csv\").value=csv;$(\"dl\").onclick=()=>{const a=document.createElement(\"a\");\n    a.href=URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([csv],{type:\"text/csv\"}));a.download=\"answers_\"+($(\"pid\").value||\"anon\")+\".csv\";a.click()}}\n</script></body></html>\n\"\"\"\n\n\ndef build_eval_kit(items: List[dict], vocab: SignVocab, path, fps_note: float = 30.0, seed: int = 0) -> Tuple[Path, Path]:\n    \"\"\"Write a self-contained HTML rating page and a separate answer key.\n\n    items: list of dict(source = 'real' | 'generated', word, seq (T, NODES, D), seconds).\n    The page shows each animation at its real duration (stick figure: arms, both hands, face) and asks for the word, a 1-5 clarity\n    rating and a 1-5 naturalness rating, WITHOUT saying whether it is real or generated; items are shown in a random order per\n    participant. Participants download a CSV (`answers_<code>.csv`). The key (item_id -> source, word, duration) stays with you: it is\n    NOT inside the page. Returns (html path, key csv path).\"\"\"\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    perm = rng.permutation(len(items))                                    # item ids carry no information about the source\n    T = len(items[0][\"seq\"])\n    pack, key = [], []\n    for new_id, k in enumerate(perm):\n        it = items[int(k)]\n        xy = np.asarray(it[\"seq\"][..., :2], float)\n        lo, hi = np.percentile(xy.reshape(-1, 2), 0.5, axis=0), np.percentile(xy.reshape(-1, 2), 99.5, axis=0)\n        pack.append({\"id\": f\"item{new_id:03d}\", \"seconds\": round(float(it[\"seconds\"]), 3), \"box\": [round(float(v), 3) for v in (lo[0], hi[0], lo[1], hi[1])],\n                     \"f\": np.round(xy.reshape(-1) * 1000).astype(int).tolist()})\n        key.append({\"item_id\": f\"item{new_id:03d}\", \"source\": it[\"source\"], \"word\": it[\"word\"], \"seconds\": round(float(it[\"seconds\"]), 3)})\n    face = [{\"a\": FACE_SLICE[n].start, \"b\": FACE_SLICE[n].stop, \"c\": FACE_STYLE[n].replace(\"crimson\", \"#dc143c\").replace(\"darkred\", \"#8b0000\")\n             .replace(\"tab:brown\", \"#8c564b\").replace(\"tab:cyan\", \"#17becf\").replace(\"tab:green\", \"#2ca02c\"),\n             \"loop\": n in FACE_LOOPS, \"line\": n in FACE_LINES} for n in FACE_SLICE]\n    layout = {\"n\": NUM_NODES, \"lh\": LH.start, \"rh\": RH.start, \"hand\": [list(e) for e in HAND_EDGES], \"pose\": [list(e) for e in POSE_EDGES], \"face\": face}\n    data = {\"words\": vocab.itos[1:], \"T\": T, \"layout\": layout, \"items\": pack}\n    html = EVAL_HTML.replace(\"__DATA__\", json.dumps(data, separators=(\",\", \":\"))).replace(\"__MINUTES__\", str(max(3, round(len(items) * 0.25))))\n    path = Path(path)\n    path.write_text(html, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    key_path = path.with_name(path.stem + \"_key.csv\")\n    pd.DataFrame(key).to_csv(key_path, index=False)\n    return path, key_path\n\n\ndef _participant_boot(df: pd.DataFrame, col: str, n_boot: int = 2000, seed: int = 0) -> Tuple[float, float, float]:\n    \"\"\"Mean of `col` with a 95 % bootstrap interval that resamples PARTICIPANTS (answers of one person are not independent).\"\"\"\n    per = df.groupby(\"participant\")[col].mean().to_numpy(float)\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    boots = [rng.choice(per, len(per)).mean() for _ in range(n_boot)]\n    return float(per.mean()), float(np.percentile(boots, 2.5)), float(np.percentile(boots, 97.5))\n\n\ndef analyse_responses(csv_paths: List, key_csv) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Read the answer files of all participants + the key -> dict with\n        'by_source'  : word accuracy, clarity and naturalness for real vs generated clips (mean and 95 % CI over participants)\n        'parity'     : generated / real ratio of each of them (1.0 = as good as the real clips)\n        'by_group'   : the same per self-declared group (Deaf signer, learner, ...)\n        'per_word'   : word accuracy per word and source\n        'tests'      : paired Wilcoxon test real vs generated on the participant means (needs >= 6 participants)\n    An answer is correct if it equals the true word (case-insensitive) and 'cannot tell' was not ticked.\"\"\"\n    from scipy.stats import wilcoxon\n    df = pd.concat([pd.read_csv(p).assign(file=Path(p).name) for p in csv_paths], ignore_index=True)\n    df[\"participant\"] = df[\"participant\"].astype(str) + \"/\" + df[\"file\"]\n    m = df.merge(pd.read_csv(key_csv), on=\"item_id\", how=\"left\")\n    m[\"correct\"] = ((m[\"word_answer\"].fillna(\"\").astype(str).str.strip().str.lower() == m[\"word\"].str.lower()) & (m[\"cant_tell\"] == 0)).astype(float)\n    metrics = {\"word_accuracy\": \"correct\", \"clarity (1-5)\": \"understand\", \"naturalness (1-5)\": \"natural\"}\n    rows = []\n    for src, d in m.groupby(\"source\"):\n        row = {\"source\": src, \"answers\": len(d), \"participants\": d[\"participant\"].nunique()}\n        for name, col in metrics.items():\n            mean, lo, hi = _participant_boot(d, col)\n            row[name], row[name + \" 95% CI\"] = round(mean, 3), f\"[{lo:.2f}, {hi:.2f}]\"\n        rows.append(row)\n    by_source = pd.DataFrame(rows).set_index(\"source\")\n    out = {\"by_source\": by_source}\n    if {\"real\", \"generated\"} <= set(by_source.index):\n        out[\"parity\"] = pd.Series({n: by_source.loc[\"generated\", n] / max(by_source.loc[\"real\", n], 1e-9) for n in metrics}, name=\"generated / real\")\n        wide = m.groupby([\"participant\", \"source\"])[list(metrics.values())].mean().unstack(\"source\").dropna()\n        tests = {}\n        for name, col in metrics.items():\n            a, b = wide[col][\"real\"].to_numpy(), wide[col][\"generated\"].to_numpy()\n            tests[name] = float(wilcoxon(a, b).pvalue) if len(a) >= 6 and np.any(a != b) else float(\"nan\")\n        out[\"tests\"] = pd.Series(tests, name=\"paired Wilcoxon p-value (real vs generated)\")\n    out[\"by_group\"] = (m.assign(group=m[\"group\"].fillna(\"(not said)\")).groupby([\"group\", \"source\"])\n                       .agg(participants=(\"participant\", \"nunique\"), word_accuracy=(\"correct\", \"mean\"), clarity=(\"understand\", \"mean\"),\n                            naturalness=(\"natural\", \"mean\")).round(3))\n    out[\"per_word\"] = m.groupby([\"word\", \"source\"])[\"correct\"].mean().unstack(\"source\").round(2)\n    return out","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-18T00:53:37.848168Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-18T00:53:37.848508Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-18T00:53:37.871311Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-18T00:53:37.848477Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-18T00:53:37.870672Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":44},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### ▶ Build the rating kit from the test clips\nTakes `n_words` test words and, for each, one **real** clip (a clean test clip of an unseen signer) and one **generated** clip (smoothed, with a duration drawn from the prior).\nWrites `eval_kit.html` (send this) and `eval_kit_key.csv` (keep this).","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"n_words = min(20, len(arrs[\"words\"]))\npick = np.random.default_rng(7).choice(arrs[\"words\"], n_words, replace=False)\nitems = []\nfor w in pick:\n    word = vocab.decode(int(w) + 1)\n    r_idx = np.nonzero(arrs[\"real_labels\"] == w)[0]\n    g_idx = np.nonzero(arrs[\"gen_labels\"] == w)[0]\n    if len(r_idx) == 0 or len(g_idx) == 0:\n        continue\n    r_sec = float(dur_prior.seconds(arrs[\"real_dur_z\"][r_idx[0]])) if cfg.use_duration else 1.5\n    g_sec = float(arrs[\"gen_seconds\"][g_idx[0]]) if arrs.get(\"gen_seconds\") is not None else 1.5\n    g_seq = arrs[\"gen_seq\"][g_idx[0]]\n    if cfg.smooth:\n        g_seq = smooth_sequence(g_seq, effective_fps(len(g_seq), g_sec), cfg.smooth_min_cutoff, cfg.smooth_beta, cfg.smooth_d_cutoff)\n    items.append(dict(source=\"real\", word=word, seq=arrs[\"real_seq\"][r_idx[0]], seconds=r_sec))\n    items.append(dict(source=\"generated\", word=word, seq=g_seq, seconds=g_sec))\n\nkit_html, kit_key = build_eval_kit(items, vocab, Path(cfg.work_dir) / \"eval_kit.html\")\nprint(f\"{len(items)} animations ({len(items) // 2} words x real / generated) -> {kit_html} ({kit_html.stat().st_size / 1e6:.1f} MB)\")\nprint(\"answer key (keep it, do NOT send it):\", kit_key)\nprint(\"\\nAfter collecting the answer files:\\n\"\n      \"    res = analyse_responses(['answers_P1.csv', 'answers_P2.csv', ...], key_csv='eval_kit_key.csv')\\n\"\n      \"    display(res['by_source']); display(res['parity']); display(res['tests']); display(res['by_group'])\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-18T00:53:37.872296Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-18T00:53:37.872643Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-18T00:53:38.049931Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-18T00:53:37.872622Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-18T00:53:38.049085Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"40 animations (20 words x real / generated) -> /kaggle/working/eval_kit.html (3.0 MB)\nanswer key (keep it, do NOT send it): /kaggle/working/eval_kit_key.csv\n\nAfter collecting the answer files:\n    res = analyse_responses(['answers_P1.csv', 'answers_P2.csv', ...], key_csv='eval_kit_key.csv')\n    display(res['by_source']); display(res['parity']); display(res['tests']); display(res['by_group'])\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":45},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 13. Export the best model\n`ckpt_best.pt` is a single self-contained bundle (EMA weights + config + vocabulary + normalisation statistics).\n`export_for_download` zips it with the classifier, the metrics and the figures. Everything in `/kaggle/working` also appears in\nthe notebook's **Output** tab after *Save Version*.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Export\ndef export_for_download(work_dir: str, zip_name: str = \"asl_diffusion_best.zip\") -> Path:\n    work = Path(work_dir)\n    names = [\"ckpt_best.pt\", \"classifier_best.pt\", \"vocab.json\", \"stats.npz\", \"eval_results.json\", \"eval_summary.png\",\n             \"loss_curves.png\", \"per_word_generated_accuracy.csv\", \"duration_prior.json\", \"depth_lifter.pt\", \"face_reference.json\"]\n    files = ([work / n for n in names if (work / n).exists()] + sorted(work.glob(\"real_vs_generated_*.png\"))\n             + sorted(work.glob(\"avatar_*.bvh\")) + sorted(work.glob(\"avatar_*.json\")) + sorted(work.glob(\"eval_kit*.html\")))\n    zpath = work / zip_name\n    with zipfile.ZipFile(zpath, \"w\", zipfile.ZIP_DEFLATED) as z:\n        for f in files:\n            z.write(f, f.name)\n    print(f\"[export] {zpath} ({zpath.stat().st_size / 1e6:.1f} MB): {[f.name for f in files]}\")\n    print(\"Reload with:  model, diffusion, 